[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2608.07239, 'Unified framework for asymptotically uniform iterative construction of generalised random '] Consider the iterative edge-colored graph process on $V$ and $\d^{(g)}$, $\d'^{(g)}$ and $X^{(g)}$ for $g=1,\ldots,\chi$. Let $x_{\max}^{(g)}$ be the maximum degree in $(V,X^{(g)})$, and let
		\begin{align}
			d_{\max}^{(g)}&:=\max\{d_1^{(g)},\ldots,d_n^{(g)},d_1'^{(g)},\ldots,d_{n'}'^{(g)}\},
			\\\Delta^{(g)}&:=d_{\max}^{(g)}\left(x_{\max}^{(g)}+\sum_{h=1}^{g}d_{\max}^{(h)}\right)+m^{(g)}\sum_{h=g+1}^{\chi}\frac{(d_{\max}^{(h)})^2}{m^{(h)}}.
		\end{align}
		Consider the asymptotics as $m_{\min}:=\min\{m^{(1)},\ldots,m^{(\chi)}\}\to\infty$, and assume that $\Delta^{(g)}=O((m^{(g)})^{\sfrac12}/(\log m^{(g)})^2)$ for $g=1,\ldots,\chi$. Then each iteration $g=1,\ldots,\chi$ has probability $O(\Delta^{(g)}/m^{(g)})$ of rejection. In particular, for $m_{\min}$ large enough, there exist edge-disjoint simple bipartite graphs for $g=1,\ldots,\chi$ with degree sequences $\d^{(g)}$ and $\d'^{(g)}$ on their parts and with no edges from $X^{(g)}$. Furthermore, any such graphs are sampled with probability $e^{O(\mathscr{E})}\mathscr{P}$, where $\mathscr{E}:=\sum_{g=1}^{\chi}\mathscr{E}(m^{(g)},\Delta^{(g)})$ and
		\begin{align}
			\mathscr{P}&:=\exp\Bigg(\sum_{g=1}^{\chi}\Bigg(\tfrac12\lambda_{\d^{(g)}}\lambda_{\d'^{(g)}}+\sum_{h=g+1}^{\chi}\lambda_{\d^{(g)},\d^{(h)}}\lambda_{\d'^{(g)},\d'^{(h)}}+\mu_{\d^{(g)},\d'^{(g)}}^{X^{(g)}}\Bigg)\Bigg)
			\\&\quad\cdot\prod_{g=1}^{\chi}\left(\frac1{m^{(g)}!}\prod_{i=1}^{n}d_i^{(g)}!\prod_{j=1}^{n'}d_j'^{(g)}!\right),
		\end{align}
		which is asymptotically uniform if $\mathscr{E}=o(1)$. The total number of such graphs is thus $e^{O(\mathscr{E})}\mathscr{P}^{-1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem_irreg_nonoptimal of arXiv:2608.09105, 'Longest convex chains with i.i.d.\ points'] Assume (equation p_upper of the paper).
Given $\rho\in(0,\tfrac12)$, define the random variable
\eq{
\mathscr{L}_n^\mathsf{irr} \coloneqq \max\big\{\#\mathcal{C}:\, \text{$\mathcal{C}\subseteq\mathcal{S}_n$ and $\mathcal{C}$ is a $\rho$-irregular convex chain}\big\}.
}
For every $\epsilon>0$, there exists $\rho = \rho(\epsilon,\mathfrak{C})\in(0,\tfrac12)$ small enough that
\eeq{ 
\limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac{\mathscr{L}_n^\mathsf{irr}}{n^{1/3}} \leqslant \epsilon \quad \text{almost surely.}
}

