body:
[Definition def:iglbox-frame-conditions of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] Let $\mathfrak{F} = (W, \leq, \sqsubset)$ be an f-frame, and put ${\sqsubset_\beta} \coloneq (\sqsubset \cdot \leq)$.
  When $\mathfrak{F}$ is $\Box$-p, this is the modal relation of its $\Box$-condensation $\beta \mathfrak{F}$.
  \begin{itemize}
    \item We write
          $\operatorname{Up}_{\leq}(W) \coloneq \set*{ A \subseteq W; \forall x,y\, (x \in A \mathrel{\text{\&}} x \leq y \mathrel{\Rightarrow} y \in A) }$
          for the set of all $\leq$-upsets of $W$.
    \item We say $\mathfrak{F}$ is \emph{$\sqsubset_\beta$-Noetherian}
          if for any $A \in \operatorname{Up}_{\leq}(W)$ such that $A \ne W$,
          there is $w_A \in W \setminus A$ such that $\forall v \in W\, (w_A \sqsubset_\beta v \mathrel{\Rightarrow} v \in A)$.
    \item We say $\mathfrak{F}$ is \emph{$\sqsubset_\beta$-strong} if ${\sqsubset_\beta} \subseteq {\leq}$,
          and is \emph{$\sqsubset$-strong} if ${\sqsubset} \subseteq {\leq}$.
  \end{itemize}

[Definition eq:maindeifnition of arXiv:2411.02030, 'Finite ergodic components for upper probabilities'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V,T)$ be an UPPS. The upper probability $V$ is said to be of finite ergodic components if there exists a partition $\alpha=\{A_1,\ldots,A_n\}\subset \mathcal{I}$, such that for each $i\in\{1,2,\ldots,n\}$, $V_i$  is an ergodic upper probability with respect to $T$ on $(\Omega,\mathcal{F})$, where 
	\begin{equation}
		V_i(A):=\sup\{P(A):P\in\operatorname{core}(V)\text{ and } P(A_i)=1\}\text{ for any }A\in\mathcal{F}.
	\end{equation}

