body:
[Lemma L:1st-der-generic-lemma of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] For $i \in \{1,2\}$ and $p \in \mathbb{N}$, let the process $D_r^{W_i}X_t^{\varepsilon}$ be the solution of equations in system (equation E:Multiscale-Diffusion-Main-Eq of the paper). Then, there exist time-independent positive constants $K$ and $K_{c_x}$ such that
\begin{multline*}
\mathbb{E} \left[(D_r^{W_i}X_t^{\varepsilon})^{2p} \right] \le K{\varepsilon^{p}}e^{-(2p)\alpha (t-r)} \mathds{1}_{(i=1)} + K \underbrace{\int_r^t \cdots \int_r^t}_{2p\operatorname{-times}} \prod_{j=1}^{2p}e^{-\alpha (t-s_j)} \prod_{j=1}^{2p} \left\{ \mathbb{E} (D_r^{W_i}Y_{s_j}^{\eta})^{2p} \right\}^{\frac{1}{2p}}\thinspace ds_1 \cdots ds_{2p} \\
+ K \varepsilon^p e^{-(2p)\alpha (t-r)} \left[ \underbrace{ \int_r^t \cdots \int_r^t}_{2p\operatorname{-times}} \prod_{j=1}^{2p}e^{K_{c_x} (s_j-r)} \prod_{j=1}^{2p} \left\{ \mathbb{E} (D_r^{W_i}Y_{s_j}^{\eta})^{4p} \right\}^{\frac{1}{2p}}\thinspace ds_1 \cdots ds_{2p} \right]^{\frac{1}{2}}.
\end{multline*}

