body:
[Lemma lem:rod_retention of arXiv:2605.16086, 'Loop pruning and downward deviations for maximum local time of discrete-time simple random'] Fix a sub-interval \(I_0=[I_0^-,I_0^+]\subset I\) and \(u\in[m]\) such that \([\rho_u-L,\rho_u+L]\subset I_0\).
Suppose that, for some \(v_0\in\{-K,\ldots,K-1\}\), \(\zeta^+_{u v_0}\ge t_{u,v_0+1}\).
Then
\begin{equation}
\zeta^+_{uw}>t_{uK}\qquad\text{for all }w\in\{v_0,\ldots,K-1\},
\end{equation}
and consequently
\begin{equation}
\zeta_{u,K}\subset \zeta_{u,K-1}\subset\cdots\subset \zeta_{u v_0}.
\end{equation}

