[Dfn 90 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] For any finite subset $F$ of $\G$, we write $\S^\rm{u}_k(F)$ for the set of all positive semidefinite elements $Q$ of $\rmM_F(\rmM_k)$ that (i) have all diagonal blocks $Q(g,g)$ equal to $I_k$, and (ii) satisfy the symmetry
\begin{equation}
	Q(g_1,h_1) = Q(g_2,h_2) \quad \hbox{whenever}\ g_1,g_2,h_1,h_2 \in F\ \hbox{and}\ g_1^{-1}h_1 = g_2^{-1}h_2.
\end{equation}
	We refer to the elements of $\S^\rm{u}_k(F)$ as \textbf{partial positive definite functions over $F$}.

	We write $\S_k^\circ(F)$ for the subset of nonsingular members of $\S^\rm{u}_k(F)$.

