[Theorem thm:main-fixed of arXiv:2608.19050, 'Online Permutation Embedding: \\ Optimal Stopping and Scaling Laws'] Let $\pi \in \Pi_k$ and let $\mathcal{A}^*\in\mathrm{OA}(\pi)$ denote (alg:canonical-general2 of the paper). Then
    \begin{equation}
        \E{T_{\mathcal{A}^*}}=\beta(\pi),
    \end{equation}
    and, furthermore, for some universal constant $C > 0$,
    \begin{equation}
        \PP[\mathcal{S}]{|T_{\mathcal{A}^*} - \beta(\pi)| > y \,\beta(\pi)^{3/4}} \le C\,y^{-2}\,, \qquad y \ge 1 \,. 
    \end{equation}
    Conversely, for any $\mathcal{A} \in \mathrm{OA}(\pi)$ and any $\delta \in (0,1)$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \PP[\mathcal{S}]{T_\mathcal{A} \le (1-\delta)\beta(\pi) } \le 1-\delta\,.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

