[Lemma lem:MetricComparison of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Fix $\delta > 0$. Then, for all $\eta, \zeta \in \mathrm{Macro}(\delta)$, and $n \in \mathbb{N}$ sufficiently large, we have
    \begin{equation}

        \frac{1}{4} \left\lVert\eta - \zeta\right\rVert_1 \leqslant d_G(\eta,\zeta) \leqslant \frac{d-1}{2d} \left\lVert\eta - \zeta\right\rVert_1. 
    \end{equation}
    This statement remains true when we consider the graph distance of $G$ restricted to $\mathrm{Macro}(\delta)$ with $\delta > 0$ sufficiently small, or to $\mathrm{Centre}(C)$ for some fixed constant $C > 0$.

