[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2603.25615, 'Fourier dimension of Mandelbrot cascades on planar curves'] Let $I\subset[0,1]$. Then
    \begin{equation*}
    \left|\int_{\gamma(I)}\exp\left(-2\pi i x\cdot\xi \right)\,dx\right|\lesssim |\xi|^{-1/2}\,.
\end{equation*}
    For $j \geq 1 $, assume that $b^{-j}|\xi| \leq |\gamma'(t) \cdot \xi|$ for all $t \in I$. Then
    \begin{equation*}
    \left|\int_{\gamma(I)}\exp\left(-2\pi i x\cdot\xi \right)\,dx\right|\lesssim b^j/|\xi|\,,    
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:pure-boundary of arXiv:2607.03639, '\vspace{-0.6in}An AI-Assisted Solution to the Signed BAR Conjecture: Uniqueness in the Har'] Let $\eta_i\in\mathcal M(F_i)$ be finite signed measures. If
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{i=1}^d\int_{F_i}D_i f\,d\eta_i=0,
 \qquad f\in C_b^2(E),
\end{equation}
then $\eta_i=0,$ for all $i=1\ldots,d.$

