[Lemma lem:grad-var-rmulmc of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] Let $h \lesssim 1/\beta^{1/2}$, $\gamma \lesssim \sqrt{\beta}$, and let $(\hat X_{\mathsf{u} h}^+, X_{\mathsf{u}h})$ be as defined in~(eq:rm-ulmc of the paper) and~(eq:ULD of the paper) respectively, where both processes are started at $(x, p)$ and synchronously coupled with the same Brownian motion ${\{B_t\}}_{t \geqslant 0}$. Then, for any $\mathsf{u} \in [0, 1]$,
    \begin{align*}
        \norm{\nabla V(\hat X_{\mathsf{u} h}^+) - \nabla V(X_{\mathsf{u} h})}_{L^2} \lesssim \beta^{2} h^3\, \norm{p}
        + \beta^{2} \gamma^{1/2}d^{1/2} h^{7/2}
        + \beta^{2} h^4\,\norm{\nabla V(x)}\,.
    \end{align*}
    In particular, this also holds when $\mathsf{u}$ is drawn from the distribution specified in (equation eq:interpolant-dist of the paper).

