$|t+b_i|\ge T/2$.  The normalization above gives
\begin{equation*}
\ell(5/4+i(t+b_i))
=\operatorname{Log}\left(1-\frac{2}{9/4+i(t+b_i)}\right)
=O(T^{-1}).
\end{equation*}
Equation~\eqref{eq:regularisation-identity} and absolute convergence on
$\Re s=5/4$ therefore show that
\begin{equation}
|\tilde F_{\mathbf b}(5/4+it)-F_{\mathbf b}(5/4+it)|
\ll T^{-1}.
\end{equation}
On the whole line $\Re s=5/4$, absolute convergence and ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:1ecfb408a82fd23ed99a00ff1ac4946ac1589973fbebcc4d993fd403e1d307f4","revision_digest":"sha256:96a35670f047d13af05819e791990edf47255f6ffa7ca129ef99f5dd6045c4b7","source_id":"arxiv:2609.01101","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

