{"artifact_digest":"sha256:5269a42370f7af5c48e4775b594d095a3dbcf4d2c6f1ab354d92007c9337a0bb","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/52/5269a42370f7af5c48e4775b594d095a3dbcf4d2c6f1ab354d92007c9337a0bb.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:1bb641ab4c20032637dd092546b8e85c156dcf31a563967eb3f32e5a94cdb891","bundle_entry_key":"2511-19391-lemma-5-lemma3","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_095","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_095.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2511-19391-lemma-5-lemma3","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Note that $S(u)$ is $\mathcal{A}^{(|u|-1)}$-measurable and $\varphi_{u}$ is independent of $\mathcal{A}^{(|u|-1)}$. Next, recall that the conditional expectation of a non-negative random variable is well-defined, even if the variable itself is not integrable (see e.g., [Shiryaev1996]). Then, 
\begin{align}  
\mathbb{E}[ (\varphi_{u}(t-S(u)))^{2} \mid \mathcal{A}^{(|u|-1)}] \stackrel{a.s.}{=} \mathbb{E}[\varphi^{2}](t-S(u)).
