body:
[Lemma computation for exact asymptotics of arXiv:2605.29095, 'Asymptotics of the number of components of random polynomial lemniscates'] Let $X$ be a uniform random variable in the unit disk. Then 
    \begin{equation*}
I := \mathbb{E}\left[ [\log|1-X|]^2\right] = \frac{1}{\pi} \int_0^1 \int_0^{2\pi} \left( \log \left| 1 - r e^{i\theta} \right| \right)^2 \, r \, d\theta \, dr = \frac{\zeta(2) - 1}{2}= \frac{\pi^2 - 6}{12}.
\end{equation*}

