body:
[Prop prop1 of arXiv:2411.14766, 'Axis-Driven Random Walks on $\Z^2$ \\ (transient cases)'] Assume $0<\alpha<1/2$, when $i\rightarrow +\infty$ in probability
    \begin{align*}
    \frac{\overline{Z}_{\rho_i}}{i^{\frac{1}{(1-\alpha)}}} \rightarrow  {\mathbf{c_{_1}}},
    \end{align*}
  where $ {\mathbf{c_{_1}}}=(2(1-\alpha))^{1/(1-\alpha)}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition Villain model on a percolation configuration of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given an edge percolation configuration $\omega \in \{0 , 1\}^{E(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}^d})}$, a finite set $\Lambda \subseteq \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}^d}$ and an inverse temperature $\beta \geq 0$, we consider the Villain model on the percolation configuration $\omega$ to be the probability distribution on the set of configurations $[0 , 2\pi)^{\Lambda}$
\begin{equation*}
    \mu_{\Lambda , \beta , \omega}^{\mathrm{Vil}}(d \theta) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda, \beta, \omega}^{\mathrm{Vil}}} \prod_{\substack{x , y \in \Lambda \\ x \sim y}} v_{\omega_{xy}\beta} \left( \theta_x - \theta_y \right) \prod_{x \in \Lambda} d \theta_x.
\end{equation*}
We denote by $\mu_{\beta,\omega}^{\mathrm{Vil}}$ the thermodynamic limit obtained by taking the limit $\Lambda \uparrow \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}^d}$ (whose existence
and uniqueness is once again guaranteed by compactness arguments and the Ginibre inequality), and denote by $\left\langle \cdot \right\rangle_{\beta, \omega}$ the corresponding expectation.

[Prop 37 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] We have the following explicit expressions for our four degenerate terms:
	\begin{equation*}
		M_{ij}(s)=M^0_{ij}(s) h_{ij,\q}(s),\quad\text{for } i,j\in\{0,1\},
	\end{equation*}
	for $s$ lying at a general position. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Defn def-vel of arXiv:2607.25567, 'Random Trees in Hyperbolic FPP'] Let $\xi \in {\partial G}$. The velocity  in the direction of $\xi$ is defined as
${v} (\xi) := \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{{\mathbb E}({\mathbf T}(1, x_n))}{n},$
where $x_n\to \xi$ with $d(1,x_n)=n$ is any sequence \emph{provided such a limit exists.}

[Lemma lem:FaceIntegralAsymptotic of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $\vec\ell$ be of convergent type for the face $\cal F$ and assume that $\cal F$ is not contained in a coordinate hyperplane. Then there exists $\epsilon >0$ such that we have

\begin{align*}
\int_{\cal F(\log B)} \prod_{i=1}^s (t_i+1)^{\ell_i} d\mu = (\log B)^{d+\ell} \int_{\cal F} \prod_{i=1}^s t_i^{\ell_i} d\mu \left(1+O_\epsilon\!\left((\log B)^{-\epsilon}\right)\right).
\end{align*}

