[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.07839, 'Bounds on Spectral Gaps for Non-Reversible Markov Chains with Applications to Temporal Dif'] Let $P$ be a Markov kernel and  let $\nu$ be a probability measure. If there are positive numbers $\gamma$ and $\delta$ and an integer $m\ge 1$ such that
  \begin{equation}

  \gamma \nu(A) \ge P^m(x,A)\ge \delta \nu(A) \quad \forall x\in\cX,\forall A\in\cB,
  \end{equation}
  then
  \begin{align*}
    \gap(P^m)&\ge \frac{\delta^2}{\gamma}\\
    \gap(P)&\ge 1-\left(1-2^{-m}\frac{\delta^2}{\gamma}\right)^{1/m}. 
  \end{align*}

