[Theorem th:Schauder_est_intr of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] For any $\alpha,\gamma\geq 0 $ and $T>0$, there exists $C=C(\alpha,\gamma,T,B)>0$ such that 
\begin{align}
 \|\mathscr{P}'_{\cdot}\, \varphi\|_{\mathcal{C}_B^{\alpha+\gamma}((r,T)\times\mathbb{R}^d)}  &\leq C\, r^{-\frac{\alpha}{2}} \|\varphi\|_{B,\gamma},\\ 
\|\mathscr{P}_{T-\cdot}\, \varphi\|_{{\mathcal{C}_B^{\alpha+\gamma}((0,T-r)\times\mathbb{R}^d)} }& \leq C\, (T-r)^{-\frac{\alpha}{2}} \|\varphi\|_{B,\gamma}, 
\end{align}
for any  $r\in (0,T)$ and for any $\varphi\in C^{b}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition of arXiv:2510.07682, 'From tug-of-war to Brownian Boost: \\ explicit ODE solutions for player-funded stochastic-'] To $(S_-,S_+) \in \mathcal{S}_0^2$, associate $(b,a):\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}} \to [0,\infty)$ as usual. 
\begin{enumerate}
\item Let $S_-' \in \mathcal{S}_0$ be associated to $b':Z \to [0,\infty)$. If $b'_i \geq b_i$ for all $i \in Z$, then $(S_-',S_+)$ is called a left strengthening of $(S_-,S_+)$.
\item Now let  $S_+' \in \mathcal{S}_0$ be associated to $a':Z \to [0,\infty)$. If $a'_i \geq a_i$ for all $i \in Z$, then $(S_-,S_+')$ is called a right strengthening of $(S_-,S_+)$.  
\end{enumerate} 
When the assumed bounds are reversed, we speak of a left or right weakening.

