[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.14812, 'Joint convergence in Wiener chaos via transport hierarchy and Malliavin covariances'] Let $p\geq 2$ and let $(X_N = I_p(f_N), N\geq 1)$ with $f_N\in H^{\odot p}$ 
	for all $N\geq 1$. Assume \eqref{c1}. Then, for every $Y\in L^2(\Omega)$,
	\begin{equation*}
		(X_N, Y) \xrightarrow[N\to\infty]{(d)} (Z, Y),
	\end{equation*}
	where $Z\sim N(0,\sigma^2)$ and $Z$, $Y$ are independent. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Defn bound-edges of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Given an oriented planar map $\mathfrak m$ with missing edges, make the following definitions (see the map on the left-hand side of Figure~(fig-bipolar-boundaries of the paper)). 
\begin{itemize}
    \item The \textbf{upper-left} (resp.\ \textbf{lower-right}) \textbf{boundary} of $\mathfrak m$ is defined to be the set of edges $e\in\mathcal E(\mathfrak m)$ lying on the boundary of the external face of $\mathfrak m$  which are oriented so that the external face of $\mathfrak m$ is  immediately to the left (resp.\ right) of $e$. For all of the maps we consider, the upper-left and lower-right boundaries of $\mathfrak m$ will be (possibly empty) simple directed paths.
    \item The \textbf{upper-right} (resp.\ \textbf{lower-left}) \textbf{boundary} of $\mathfrak m$ is defined to be the set of consecutive \emph{missing} edges $e\notin\mathcal E(\mathfrak m)$ between the terminal (resp.\ initial) vertex of the upper-left boundary and the terminal (resp.\ initial) vertex of the lower-right boundary.  
\end{itemize}
When the orientation of  $\mathfrak m$ is bipolar and there are no missing edges, we simply call the upper-left boundary \textbf{left} boundary and the lower-right boundary \textbf{right} boundary.

[Lemma lem:p-moment estimate of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Suppose Assumption (asp:potential of the paper) holds. For any $p\geq 2$ and $\xi\in L^p(\Omega,\mathcal F_0,\mathbf P)$, there exists $C(p)=C(p,\alpha,\beta,\delta,\overline{\sigma}, L)>0$ such that the unique solution $\{X_t^{\xi}\}_{t\geq 0}$ of (equation eq:mvsystem of the paper) satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{E}[|X_t^{\xi}|^p]\leq e^{-pt}\mathbf{E}[|\xi|^p]+C(p), \ \text{ for all } \ t\geq 0.
    \end{equation}

