body:
[Lemma le:neg_mom_1 of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $c,q,\rho\in(0,\infty)$, $p\in[1,\infty)$, $\beta \in (0, 1) $, $ n, n_0 \in {\mathbb N} $ satisfy
\begin{align}\begin{split} 
q+p\ln\beta\ge \rho
 \end{split}\end{align}
and $n> n_0$. 
Let $V_n^*$ be a non-negative random variable which satisfies for all $ \lambda \in [0,\infty) $ that
\bas{
  - \ln \mathbb{E}\bigl[ e^{-\lambda V_n^*} \bigr]
  \ge \sum_{k=n_0+1}^n \left( c \frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n} \beta^{n-k} \lambda \right) \wedge q + c \frac{1-\beta^{n_0}}{1-\beta^n} \beta^{n-n_0} \lambda.
}
Then \bas{
{\mathbb E}[(V_n^*)^{-p}]&\le \frac1{c^p} D_{\rho,p},
}
where
\bas{

  D_{\rho,p}:=\sum_{r=0}^\infty (r+1)^p e^{-\rho r}<\infty.
}

