[Proposition 30 (Conditional entropy inequality with an additive defect) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] Assume $\mathsf H(\mathsf Q\mid\mathbb P_{N,\beta})<\infty$ and
$A_{N,\beta}+N^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^NU_\beta(x_i)\in L^1(\mathsf Q)$.  Then, for every $\lambda>1$,
\begin{align}
 \cS_N(\mathsf Q)
 &\ge\left(1-\frac1\lambda\right)\mathsf H(\mathsf Q\mid\mathbb P_{N,\beta})
 -\log \mathsf K_{N,\beta}(\mu_\beta)\notag\\
 &\quad-\frac1\lambda\log\E_{\mathbb P_{N,\beta}}\left[
 \exp\left\{-\lambda\beta\left(A_{N,\beta}
 +\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^NU_\beta(x_i)\right)\right\}\right].
\end{align}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \mathfrak D_{\beta,\lambda}:=\sup_{M\ge2}\left\{\log \mathsf K_{M,\beta}(\mu_\beta)+\lambda^{-1}\log\E_{\mathbb P_{M,\beta}}\left[e^{-\lambda\beta\left(A_{M,\beta}+M^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^M U_\beta(x_i)\right)}\right]\right\}<\infty.
\end{equation}
The restricted hypotheses cover $\D\mathsf Q=f^2\,\D\mathbb P_{N,\beta}$ for every bounded collision-free compactly supported smooth $f$ with $\int_{\C^N} f^2\,\D\mathbb P_{N,\beta}=1$; the general finite-entropy form follows by truncation whenever the stated integrability is preserved.

