[Definition 10 of arXiv:2511.02725, 'Mixing of general biased adjacent transposition chains'] A vector $\vec{\ell}\in \R^{2n}$ is \vocab{$n$-admissible} if 
    \begin{align*}
         j-\ell_j^-  \le k-\ell_k^- \qquad \text{ and } \qquad j + \ell_j^+  \le k + \ell_{k}^+ \qquad \forall j<k\,.
    \end{align*}
    We let $\mathcal L_n$ denote the set of $n$-admissible vectors.

[Lemma 23 (Inner mass formula) of arXiv:2609.03339, 'Exterior Serrin Rigidity for the Homogeneous \texorpdfstring{$k$}{k}-Hessian Equation\\'] One has
		\begin{align}
			M(J[w])
			&=\alpha\beta c^kI_{k-1}
			-\frac{n-k+1}{k-1}c^{k+1}I_{k-2},\\
            M(Q[w])&=c^kI_{k-1}>0,\\
			M(K[w])&=0.
		\end{align}
		In particular, \cref{prop:boundary-curvature} implies
		\begin{equation}
			M(J[w])\ge0.
		\end{equation}

