\]

Taking $t = \sqrt{2\log N + c\log\log N}$ and union bound over all vertices gives the result.

For part (2), let $\mathbf{q} = \mathbf{1}_S/\|\mathbf{1}_S - |S|N^{-1}\mathbf{e}\|$. The Berry-Esseen bound gives concentration of $\sqrt{N}\langle \mathbf{q}, \mathbf{u}_2\rangle$ around 0, which translates to the stated mass concentration after","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:0e3ae76532b9f0d581a2da8e3b9ba7853466009d19d2896c9208291170cc1a92","revision_digest":"sha256:98c38406c6bc5bbc566ac743006922ddc7614c8b65feeba5a8a9cfa652553daf","source_id":"arxiv:2507.12502","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

