[Conjecture conj:perc of arXiv:2412.05503, 'Critical scaling profile for trees and connected subgraphs \\ on the complete graph'] For $s\in \mathbb{R}$, let
\begin{equation}

f_{\rm perc}(s) = \int_0^\infty x^2 \mathrm d\sigma_s, \qquad
\mathrm d \sigma_s =
	\frac 1 { \sqrt{2\pi} } x^{-5/2} \Psi(x^{3/2})
    e^{-\frac 1 6 x^3 + \frac s 2 x^2 - \frac{ s^2} 2 x}
    \mathrm dx
    .
\end{equation}
Then, for some $a,b>0$, as $V\to\infty$ we have
\begin{equation} 
\begin{aligned}
    \tau_{V,01}(1+sV^{-1/3}) & \sim b V^{-2/3} f_{\rm perc}(as),
    \\
    \chi_{V} ^{\rm {perc}}(1+sV^{-1/3}) & \sim b V^{1/3} f_{\rm perc}(as).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

