[Prop Prop_K_PerturbationEstimate of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] For every ${\mathbf{p}} \in \mathbf{Dir}$, $(Z,[{\mathfrak l}]) \in \mathbf{Ram}$,
  $\Phi \in K^\infty(X{\backslash} Z, S\otimes{\mathfrak l};{\mathbf{p}})$, and $\bar v \in \mathrm{Vect}(X)$
  \begin{equation*}
    \mathscr{L}_{\bar v}^KD_{\mathbf{p}}^{\mathfrak l} \Phi
    \in
    H_b^\infty\paren{X{\backslash} Z, S\otimes{\mathfrak l};{\mathbf{p}}};
  \end{equation*}
  in fact, for every $k,\ell \in {\mathbf{N}}_0$ with $\ell > d/2$, and $\varepsilon > 0$,
  there is a constant $c_k(\varepsilon) < \infty$ such that
  \begin{equation*}
    \Abs{\mathscr{L}_{\bar v}^KD_{\mathbf{p}}^{\mathfrak l} \Phi}_{H_b^k}
    \leqslant
    \varepsilon \Abs{\bar v}_{H^{k+1}}\Abs{\Phi}_{K^{\ell}}
    + c_k(\varepsilon) \Abs{\bar v}_{H^1}\Abs{\Phi}_{K^{k+\ell}}.
  \end{equation*}

