[Proposition prop:moments of arXiv:2608.23742, 'Second-order fusion asymptotics for $\Sine_\beta$ correlation functions'] Let $m\ge2$, $\beta>0$, $m\beta>1$, and put $\delta=m\beta/2$. Then
\begin{align}
\mathbb E S_1^2&=\frac{1}{4(m\beta-1)(2m+1)},\\
\mathbb E S_2&=\frac{m\beta}{4(m\beta-1)(2m+1)}.
\end{align}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\xi''(0)=-(2\delta-1)\mathbb E\xi'(0)^2.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:var2 of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $X_0 = \mathbf{x} \in \Omega_n$. Then for all $i \in [d]$, $j \in [m]$, and $t \geqslant 0$, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathrm{Var}\!\left(X_t(i, j)\right) \leqslant C_0\frac{n}{\Phi_{\ast}},
    \end{equation*}
    for some constant $C_0$ depending only on $d$ and $m$.

