[Definition 7 of arXiv:2608.23462, '2608.23462'] Let $p \geq 2$ and $\beta > 0$. We say that the frozen variable $(\hat Y_t^x)_{t \ge 0}$ is (uniformly) $p$-dissipative (with constant $\beta$), if for all $x\in \R^{d_1}$ and $y_1,y_2 \in \R^{d_2}$
\begin{align*}
    \langle y_1 - y_2, g(x,y_1)-g(x,y_2) \rangle + \frac{p-1}{2} |\sigma(x,y_1)-\sigma(x,y_2)|_F^2 \leq -\beta|y_1-y_2|^2.
\end{align*}

[Prop positivity of tau of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] For every $\beta \geq \beta_c$,
\begin{equation}
\boldsymbol{\tau}(\beta) \geq 2^d\int_{\beta_c}^\beta \big(\langle \tau_0 \rangle_u^+\big)^2 \mathrm{d}u.  
\end{equation}
In particular, for $\beta>\beta_c$, one has $\boldsymbol{\tau}(\beta)>0$.

