body:
[Corollary 21 (Threshold form) of arXiv:2605.11451, '2605.11451'] Define
\begin{equation}
 R_{p,n}:=\frac{m_{4,p,n}}{v_{p,n}^2}
 =
 \frac{\Gamma(5/p)\Gamma(1/p)}{\Gamma(3/p)^2}
 \frac{\Gamma(1+(n+2)/p)^2}
 {\Gamma(1+n/p)\Gamma(1+(n+4)/p)}.
\end{equation}
Then $\Phi_{p,n}$ is nonmonotone if $R_{p,n}<3$ and strictly decreasing if $R_{p,n}\ge3$.
For every fixed $1\le p<2$, the sequence $n\mapsto R_{p,n}$ is strictly increasing and has limit
\begin{equation}
 R_{p,\infty}=\frac{\Gamma(5/p)\Gamma(1/p)}{\Gamma(3/p)^2}>3.
\end{equation}
Consequently there is a finite threshold
\[
 N(p):=\min\{n\ge2:R_{p,n}\ge3\}
\]
such that $\Phi_{p,n}$ is nonmonotone for $n<N(p)$ and strictly decreasing for $n\ge N(p)$.

