[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2605.12175, 'Hypocoercive Langevin dynamics on the Lie group $\textbf{SE}(2)$'] Let $f\in D,$ and set $g:= \Pi f$. Then

\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\A^2 \P f 
= & \cos^2 (\theta) \partial_{\xi^1 \xi^1} g+2 \sin(\theta) \cos(\theta) \partial_{\xi^1 \xi^2} g \\[4pt]
& +\sin^2( \theta) \partial_{\xi^2 \xi^2} g -  \left(\nabla_{\xi} \Phi(\xi) \cdot v_{\perp}(\theta)\right) X_3 g(\xi).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

