[Lemma lem J14 of arXiv:2607.28167, 'Temporal properties of the stochastic fractional heat equation with rough dependence in sp'] For every $p> p_0$, there exists a finite positive constant $c_{3,20}$, which does not depend on   $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, such that
          \begin{align}
           \sup_{t\in [0,T]}\sup_{x\in \mathbb R} \left\| \mathcal J_{1, \theta}''  - \widetilde{\mathcal J}_{1,\theta}'\right\|_{L^p(\Omega)}^2
           \le c_{3,20}\varepsilon^{\theta\left( \frac{\alpha+2H-2}{\alpha}+2\vartheta_0\right)}.
