body:
[Defi process_tree of arXiv:2609.02346, 'Regularised double shuffle relations for planar \AZVs{}'] Let $T\in\mathcal{PT}_{\N^*}$ be a planar rooted tree. Its \emph{process tree $\operatorname{pr}(T)$}

  is a planar rooted tree whose vertices are decorated by elements from $\mathcal{PT}_{\N^*}$ defined recursively on $\lin(T)$.
  \begin{itemize}
   \item If $\lin(T)=0$, then $T$ is a ladder tree (eventually empty) and we set $\operatorname{pr}(T):=\begin{picture}(10,5)(-2,-1)
\put(0,0){\circle*{2}}
\put(2,-2){$\tiny T$}
\end{picture}$.

   \item Assume that for $N\in\N$, $\operatorname{pr}(S)$ has been defined for all $S\in\mathcal{PT}_{\N^*}$ with $\lin(S)\leq N$. Let $T\in\mathcal{PT}_{\N^*}$ be a planar rooted tree with $\lin(T)=N+1$. Then $T$ is not a ladder tree and

   let $(a,b)$ be its minimal incomparable pair. We set
   $$\operatorname{pr}(T) := B_+^{T}\left(\operatorname{pr}(T_{a+b})\, \operatorname{pr}(T_{b}^{a})\, \operatorname{pr}(T_{a}^{b})\right).$$
  \end{itemize}
  For any tree $T\in\mathcal{PT}_{\N^*}$, we write $\delta_{\operatorname{pr}(T)}:V(\operatorname{pr}(T))\longrightarrow\mathcal{PT}_{\N^*}$ the decoration map of $\operatorname{pr}(T)$.

[Lemma lem:elliptical_sum of arXiv:2609.00193, 'Provably Efficient Federated Reinforcement Learning with Linear Function Approximation and'] Let $\{x_t\}_{t=1}^T \subset \mathbb{R}^d$ with $\|x_t\|_2 \le 1$, and define
\[
V_t = \lambda I + \sum_{s=1}^{t} x_s x_s^\top,
\]
for some $\lambda > 0$. Then,
\[
\sum_{t=1}^T \min\bigl\{1, \|x_t\|_{V_{t-1}^{-1}}^2\bigr\}
\;\le\;
2 \log \frac{\det(V_T)}{\det(\lambda I)}
\;\le\;
2d \log\Bigl(1 + \frac{T}{d\lambda}\Bigr).
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 85 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For all $y \in D(A)$ and all $s,t \in [0,T]$ we have
\begin{align*}
| S_{s,t} y | \leq M e^{\omega T} | y |_{D(A)} \, |t-s|.
\end{align*}

