[Corollary 13 of arXiv:2604.01685, 'Probability with Measure\footnote{Lecture notes. University of Ljubljana.}'] Let $\AA\subset 2^\Omega$. If further $A\subset \Omega$, then \begin{equation}
	\sigma_\Omega(\AA)\vert_A=\sigma_A(\AA\vert_A);
	\end{equation}
	in particular, if $\AA$ is a $\sigma$-field on $\Omega$, then $\AA\vert_A$ is a $\sigma$-field on $A$.


	Besides, $\sigma_\Omega(\AA)=\cup \{\sigma_\Omega(\BB):\BB\text{ countable}\subset \AA\}$.

