[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2608.04900, 'A Sharper Hoeffding Bound for Weighted Sums of Exchangeable Random Variables'] Let $X_1,\ldots,X_N\in[-1,1]$ be exchangeable and let $\bar X_N=N^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^N X_i$. Then for all $n\le N$, all $w\in\mathbb{R}^n$, and all $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$,
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\biggl\{\lambda\sum_{i=1}^n w_i(X_i-\bar X_N)\biggr\}\bigg]
\le
\exp\biggl\{\frac{\lambda^2}{2}\Gamma_N\|P_{\mathbf{1}^\perp}\widetilde w\|_2^2\biggr\},
\end{align*}
where
\begin{align*}
\Gamma_N
=
\max_{1\le s\le \lfloor N/2\rfloor}
\frac{N(N-s)}{s}
\sum_{\ell=N-s}^{N-1}\frac{1}{\ell^2}
=
\begin{cases}
\displaystyle
N\sum_{\ell=N/2}^{N-1}\ell^{-2}, & N \text{ is even},\\[1.2em]
\displaystyle
\frac{N(N+1)}{N-1}\sum_{\ell=(N+1)/2}^{N-1}\ell^{-2}, & N \text{ is odd}.
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
Moreover, $\Gamma_N=1+3/(2N)+O(N^{-2})$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

