[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2608.30570, '2608.30570'] Assume $f:(M,g)\to (D_2\backslash D_1,g_0)$ is a proper Riemannian immersion from an open surface to a flat annulus and $\mathrm{Area}_g(M)<\infty$. Then,  there exists an integer $1\le d=\frac{\mathrm{Area}(M)}{3\pi}$ such that
\begin{enumerate}
\item $(M,g)$ is conformal to $D_{r}\backslash D_1$ for $r=2^{\frac{1}{d}}$
\item under the conformal parameterization $\varphi: D_r\backslash D_1\to M$, $f\circ \varphi(z)=(e^{i\theta_0}z)^d$ or $f\circ \varphi(z)=(e^{i\theta_0}\bar{z})^d$.
\end{enumerate}

