[Cor2 cor2 of arXiv:2508.02416, 'On the surjectivity of the conditional expectation\\ given a real random variable'] \begin{itemize}
  \item[(i)] There exists a probability measure $\pi$ on $\mathbb{R}^2$ admitting a density with respect to the Lebesgue measure such that (equation egtoutf2 of the paper) holds.
  \item[(ii)] There exists a probability measure $\pi$ on $\mathbb{R}^2$ such that its first marginal $\mu$ is absolutely continuous with respect to the Lebesgue measure, its second marginal $\nu$ is discrete, and (equation egtoutf2 of the paper) holds.
\end{itemize}

[Proposition 7 (Local asymptotics) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] Fix \(q\ge1\), a surplus vector
\(\mathbf r=(r_1,\ldots,r_q)\in\mathbb Z_{\ge0}^q\), and
\(0<a<b<\infty\).  Let \(k_i=k_i(n)\) range over integers such that
\begin{equation}
  x_i:=k_i n^{-2/3}\in[a,b].
\end{equation}
Then, uniformly over all \(\mathbf k=(k_1,\ldots,k_q)\) satisfying
\eqref{eq:local-grid},
\begin{equation}
  L_n(\mathbf k,\mathbf r)=n^{-2q/3}m_\lambda^{(q)}\bigl((x_1,r_1),\ldots,(x_q,r_q)\bigr)(1+o(1)).
\end{equation}
The estimate is also uniform when \(\lambda\) ranges over a fixed compact
interval, with \(L_n\) formed using \(p_{n,\lambda}\).

[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.05185, '\large\bf ON THE HEAT FLOW CONJECTURE FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] Let \(N\geq1\).  If \(P\) is a polynomial of degree \(d\) and \(t\in\C\),
its polynomial heat flow at scale \(N\) is defined by
\begin{equation}
 \exp\!\left(\frac{t}{2N}\partial_z^2\right)P
 \overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}
 \sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor d/2\rfloor}
 \frac{1}{k!}\left(\frac{t}{2N}\right)^k\partial_z^{2k}P.
\end{equation}
The series terminates because \(\partial_z^{2k}P=0\) for \(2k>d\).

