[Proposition prop_estimation of arXiv:2411.08846, 'On the Number of Crossings and Bouncings\\ of a Diffusion at a Sticky Threshold'] Consider the setting of Theorem~(thm_main of the paper) 
and let $t>0$.
The statistic 
\begin{equation}

	\begin{aligned}
		\varrho_n(X) &= \left(4 \sqrt{\frac 2 \pi} \right) \frac{1}{\sqrt n}\frac{\cC{2}{n,t}(X)}{ \cC{1}{n,t}(X)}
	\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
is a consistent estimator of $\rho $, conditionally on the event $\mathcal H_t $, i.e., $\varrho_n(X)  \longrightarrow  \rho $, in $\Prob^{\mathcal H_t}_x $-probability, as $n \longrightarrow  \infty $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 12 (Geometric componentwise information inequality) of arXiv:2607.20823, 'Fluctuation impossibility results for stochastic burst networks'] Suppose Assumption~\ref{ass:S-standing} holds and that each $K_i$ satisfies
\eqref{eq:S-geometric-law} for some $p_i \in (0,1]$. Then, for each $i\in\{1,\dots,N\}$,
\begin{equation}
        (\dot I)_{X_i}
        \le
        \frac{1}{\tau_i\kappa_i}
        \bigl(F_{X_i}-\kappa_i\bigr).

\end{equation}

