[Theorem thm:main-approx of arXiv:2608.23554, 'Provably adaptive sampling with uniform and remasking \\ discrete diffusion models'] Let \((X_t)_{t \in [0, T]}\) be the CTMC corresponding to the uniform or remasking process. If  \(t_{k+1} - t_k \leq \kappa \min(1, T - t_{k+1})\) for \(k \in \{0, \ldots, N - 1\}\), then
    \begin{equation*}
        \sum_{k=0}^{N - 1} \cL_{\mathrm{approx}}^{(k)} \lesssim \kappa \sum_{k=0}^{N - 1}  \sum_{i \in [d]} e^{-(T - t_{k+1})} \mathsf{KL} \left( \mu_{X_0^i} \ \big\|\ \widehat\mu_{X_0^i} \ \Bigr|\  X_{T - t_k}^{-i}\,\right).
    \end{equation*}
    Here, for fixed \(i \in [d]\), \(\mathsf{KL} \left( \mu_{X_0^i} \ \big\|\ \widehat\mu_{X_0^i} \ \Bigr|\  X_{T - t_k}^{-i}\,\right)\) is the conditional KL divergence between \(\Pr(X_0^i = \, \cdot \mid X_{T - t_k}^{-i})\) and \(\widehat \Pr(X_0^i = \, \cdot \mid X_{T - t_k}^{-i})\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

