[Lemma le:partial-fourier of arXiv:2411.12192, 'Sample path properties and small ball probabilities for stochastic fractional diffusion eq'] Recall that the fundamental solution $p(t,x)$ is given in (equation e:de-ptx of the paper). For all $t > s$, we have
  \begin{equation}
    \mathcal{F}\left[\frac{\partial}{\partial t} p(t-s,x-\cdot)\right](\xi)= \frac{\partial}{\partial t} \mathcal{F} p(t-s,x-\cdot)(\xi),
  \end{equation}
   and  if we assume $\alpha>1$, we also have
  \begin{equation}
    \mathcal{F}\left[\frac{\partial}{\partial x_i} p(t-s,x-\cdot)\right](\xi)= \frac{\partial}{\partial x_i} \mathcal{F} p(t-s,x-\cdot)(\xi),\text{ for all $i=1,\dots, d$.}
  \end{equation}

