[Question C_sharp of arXiv:2605.15066, 'The critical activation density in graph bootstrap percolation'] Is the $H$-percolation threshold sharp 
if and only if 
\begin{equation}
\max_{e\subset F\subseteq A\cup e}\, \frac{e(F)-1}{v(F)-2}>\rho(H),
\end{equation}
for all $(e,A)\in{\mathcal A}(H)$? (Stated as a question by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

