[Theorem thm:uit_avg_semi of arXiv:2412.05239, 'Conditions for uniform in time convergence: applications to averaging, numerical discretis'] Suppose (ass_avg_semi of the paper) holds. Then for all $(x,y)\in \mathbb{R}^n\times \mathbb{R}^d$, $\delta>0$ and $t\ge 0$
    \begin{align*}
        |\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)}[f(X_t^{\delta})]-\mathbb{E}_x[f(\bar{X}_t)]|\le \frac{C(\|f\|_{\mathcal{C}_b^2}+ \bar{\mu}(f))\Phi(x,y)}{1-e^{-\lambda \tau}}
    \end{align*}
    with $C=C_1 (\max(1,C_0))$.

