body:
[Corollary cor:analytic_sufficient of arXiv:2510.18106, 'Law equivalence for Ornstein--Uhlenbeck dynamics\\ driven by L\'evy noise'] Let $A$ and $\widetilde A$ generate bounded analytic semigroups on $H$, and set $K:=\widetilde A-A$. Suppose that, for some $\beta\in(0,\tfrac12)$,
\begin{equation}
        R_{A,\beta}:=Q^{-1/2}KA^{-\beta}
\end{equation}
is well-defined on $H$ and extends to an operator in $\mathcal{L}(H)$. Then:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item $KA^{-\beta}\in\mathcal{L}(H)$, hence Duhamel's formula (equation eq:Duhamel of the paper) holds in the strong operator topology;
\item the inverse-covariance Hilbert--Schmidt condition (equation eq:Gaussian-HS of the paper) holds; consequently
\[
        \mathcal{L}(Y_A(W))\sim\mathcal{L}(Y_{\widetilde A}(W))
        \quad\hbox{on }D_{H,T}.
\]
\end{enumerate}

