[Lemma RE3.5 of arXiv:2412.09850, 'Averaging principles for time-inhomogeneous multi-scale SDEs via nonautonomous Poisson equ'] Suppose that  $\alpha(\cdot)$ is differentiable on $(0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{t\to +\infty}\alpha(t)\in [0,\infty],\quad
 \lim_{t\rightarrow +\infty} \frac  {e^{-\gamma\int^t_0\alpha(u)\,du}}{\alpha(t)}=0, \quad \lim_{t\rightarrow +\infty}[1/\alpha(t)]'=0.
\end{equation}
Then for any $T>0$, there are constants $\varepsilon_0, C>0$ so that
 for any $\varepsilon\in (0,\varepsilon_0]$,
$$
\sup_{t\in [0,T]}|\Lambda_{\gamma}(t/\varepsilon)|^2\leqslant   C\int^{T/\varepsilon}_0 \alpha(s)\Lambda^2(s)\,ds.
$$

[Lemma lem:control-representation of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] The new control admits the exact representation
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
  \xi_c^+
  ={}&-\frac1H\sum_{h=0}^{H-1}
  \left(f'(\theta_{c,h})-\overline{f'(\theta_h)}\right)\\
  &-\frac1H\sum_{h=0}^{H-1}
  \left(\varepsilon_{c,h+1}-\bar\varepsilon_{h+1}\right).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
In particular, the old control $\xi_c$ has no direct term on the right-hand side.

