\end{figure}

These figures mean that they are subsurfaces and their complements are invariant under the moves. We call the subsurfaces {\it supports} of the moves. 
In Figure 7, supports of two moves $a$ and $b$ are disjoint.

We also call it a {\it Hatcher complex} of $\Sigma_{g,r}$.

In [FG], it is called $\Gamma_0(\Sigma_{g,r})$.

