[Prop quadraticFourier of arXiv:2606.08325, 'Digit Mixing under Polynomial Maps'] Let \(R_2(s)\) be defined by (equation eq:R2def of the paper).  There is an absolute constant \(c_2>0\) such that, for every real \(t\) satisfying \(|2t|\ge1\),
			\begin{equation}
				|\mathbb E e(tX^2)|\le \exp\bigl(-c_2R_2(S_2(|t|))\bigr),
			\end{equation}
			where \(S_2(|t|)=S_2^{\ast}(|t|):=\lfloor\log_2(2|t|)\rfloor+2\).  For \(|2t|<1\) the trivial estimate \(|\mathbb E e(tX^2)|\le1\) holds. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2608.23301, 'On a Telegraph Process with Generalized Mittag-Leffler Waiting times and Velocity Driven b'] Conditional on the event that the initial velocity is $v_1$, the distribution of $n$th event time of counting process $\{\mathcal{N}(t)\}_{t\geq0}$
	 	associated with $\{\mathbb{X}_{\alpha}(t)\}_{t\geq0}$ is given by
	 	\begin{align*}
	 		F_{T_n |S_0}(t|v_1)&=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\binom{n-1}{k}\Big(\frac{b+c}{c}\Big)_k \Big(\frac{r}{c}\Big)_{n-k-1}\Big(\Big(\frac{b+r+c}{c}\Big)_{n-1}\Big)^{-1}\nonumber\\
	 		&\hspace{3cm} \cdot(\lambda t^\alpha)^{\frac{b}{c}+k+1}(\mu t^\alpha)^{\frac{r}{c}+n-k-1} E_{(\alpha,\alpha),\alpha\big(\frac{b+r}{c}+n\big)+1}^{(\frac{b}{c}+k+1,\frac{r}{c}+n-k-1)}(-\lambda t^\alpha,-\mu t^\alpha).
	 	\end{align*}

