[Proposition prop:impossibility result generic of arXiv:2605.19894, 'Sharp Spectral Thresholds for Multi-View Spiked Wigner Models'] Under Assumption~(assump:distributional-spike of the paper), suppose further that condition \hyperlink{IT}{$(\star)$} holds. Then for any estimator $\hat{X}(A)\in\RR^{n \times L}$ computed from the observation model~(equation eq:observation model of the paper), its  overlap with the planted signal converges to $0$ i.e.,
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{1}{n} \hat{X}(A)^\top X \xrightarrow{\mathbb P} 0_{L \times L},
    \end{equation}
    when $\mathsf{SNR}(\lambda,B)<1$.

