[Proposition prop:real-secondmoment of arXiv:2411.08018, 'Last passage percolation in hierarchical environments'] Consider LPP where the weights are i.i.d. copies of the above random variable $X$. 
Then there exists $c>0$ such that for all sufficiently large $n$, 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\left(L_n \ge c\,\frac{n(\log n)^{\frac{3}{4} - \frac{\beta}{2}}}{\log\log n}\right)
        \ge 1-e^{-(\log n)^{97}}.
    \end{align*}

