body:
[Proposition 24 (Variance at a continuum frequency) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] There is a set $E_Y^{\mathrm{cell}}\subset E_Y$ of full Lebesgue measure such that, for every
$\theta\in E_Y^{\mathrm{cell}}$ and every $\xi\in\bR^d$,
\begin{equation}

    \E_\eta|\ell_\xi(D_\theta)|^2
    =\sum_{m\in\bZ^d}
       |\beta(\theta+m-\xi)|^2s_\eta(\theta+m).
\end{equation}
Consequently, if $\xi=\theta+q$ for some $q\in\bZ^d$, then
\begin{equation}

    \E_\eta|\ell_\xi(D_\theta)|^2=s_\eta(\xi).
\end{equation}

[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2604.17526, '2604.17526'] If~$T = \infty$ then the left hand side of~\eqref{e:Ptrk2-ub} satisfies
  \begin{equation}
    \prod_{k = 1}^K \norm{P_{k}^\infty r_{k}^2}_{L^\infty}
      \leq \exp\paren[\bigg]{
	  \sum_{k = 1}^K \chi^2(\pi_{k+1}; \pi_{k})
	}
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem lem-kmsw-boltzmann of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Let $  r \in \mathbbm N$. Let $\mathcal Z = (\mathcal L , \mathcal R) : \mathbbm N_0 \to\mathbbm Z^2$ be a walk started from $(0,0)$ with i.i.d.\ increments sampled uniformly from $\{(1,-1), (-1,0) , (1,0)\}$. Let $\tau$ be the smallest $n\in\mathbbm N$ for which $\mathcal R(n) = -r$ and let
\begin{equation*}
E := \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\{ \mathcal L(n) \geq 0,\: \forall n \in [0,\tau]\cap\mathbbm Z\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\} .
\end{equation*} 
Let $M$ be the map obtained by applying the KMSW procedure to $\mathcal Z|_{[0,\tau-1]}$.  
The conditional law of $M$ given $E$ is that of a Boltzmann bipolar-oriented triangulation with right boundary length $r$ (Definition~(def-boltzmann-right of the paper)).

[Defn 11 of arXiv:2606.21778, 'Pontryagin Maximum Principle in Free Probability Theory'] For $X_0\in\mathcal{A}^{sa}$ the set   $\mathcal{U}(X_0)\subseteq \mathcal{A}^{sa}$ is defined as the set of controls $U=(U_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$, such that
	\begin{equation}
		\int_0^T \|a(0,U_s)\|^2 + \|b^i(0,U_s)c^i(0,U_s)\|^2ds < \infty.
	\end{equation}
	When the context is clear we simply write $\mathcal{U}$ and hide the dependency on the initial value $X_0\in\mathcal{A}^{sa}$.

[Lem 5 of arXiv:2510.21595, 'One-arm exponents of high-dimensional percolation revisited'] Let $d>6$ and $L\geq L_0$. For every $p\in [0,1]$, and every $n\geq 0$,
\begin{equation}
	\varphi_{p}(\mathbb H_n)\geq \frac{1}{2d}\varphi_{p}(\Lambda_n).
\end{equation}
In particular, $\varphi_{p_c}(\mathbb H_n)\geq \tfrac{1}{2d}$.

