body:
[Proposition p:pp.conv.star of arXiv:2601.12677, 'Stable and Fréchet limit theorem for subgraph functionals in the hyperbolic random geometr'] Assume $1/2<\alpha<k-1$; then, as $n\to\infty$, 
\begin{equation}  
\sum_{i=1}^{N_n} \delta_{(i/N_n, \, a_{k,n}^{-1} \mu_{k,n}(U_i))}  \Rightarrow \mathsf{PPP}\big(\mathsf{Leb}\otimes \mathsf{m}_{2\alpha/(k-1)}\big), \  \ \text{in } M_p\big( [0,1]\times  (0,\infty ] \big), 
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}  
\sum_{i=1}^{N_n} \delta_{(i/N_n, \, a_{k,n}^{-1} \mathcal D_{k,n}(X_i))}  \Rightarrow \mathsf{PPP}\big(\mathsf{Leb}\otimes \mathsf{m}_{2\alpha/(k-1)}\big), \  \ \text{in } M_p\big( [0,1]\times  (0,\infty ] \big), 
\end{equation}
where $\mathsf{Leb}$ is Lebesgue measure on $[0,1]$, and 
$M_p\big([0,1]\times (0,\infty]  \big)$ denotes the space of point measures in $[0,1]\times (0,\infty]$.

