body:
[Lem d4 of arXiv:2606.16237, 'The Backward Stochastic Partial Differential Integral Equations: Solvability and Compariso'] Assume that the conditions of Theorem (thm:b2 of the paper) hold. If \((u, q, r) \in \mathbb{S}^2(H^1) \cap \mathbb{H}^2 \times \mathbb{H}^1\times \mathbb{H}^{\nu,1}\) is a strong solution of BSPDIE (equation eq:3.2 of the paper), then there exists a constant \(C > 0\) depending  on \(\alpha\), \(K\), \(\kappa\), \(T\), and the function \(\gamma\) in Assumption (ass:b3 of the paper), such that
\begin{equation}
E\left[\sup_{0 \leq t \leq T} \| u(t) \|_1^2 \right] + ||| u |||_2^2 + ||| q |||_1^2 + ||| r |||_{\nu,1}^2
\leq C \left( ||| f_0 |||_0^2 + E\|\varphi\|_1^2 \right).
\end{equation}

