body:
[Prop classical solution semilinear PDE of arXiv:2505.12127, 'Generalised principal eigenvalues and global survival of branching Markov processes'] Suppose that $g:E{\rightarrow} {\mathbb R}$ is continuous and $\tilde f:{\mathbb R}\times E{\rightarrow} {\mathbb R}_{\geq 0}$ is bounded, non-negative, locally H\"older continuous and Lipschitz in the first variable uniformly over the spatial variable, i.e. 
\[
\sup_{x\in E}\sup_{u_1\neq u_2}\frac{\lvert f(u_2,x)-f(u_1,x)\rvert}{\lvert u_2-u_1\rvert}<\infty.
\]
We further assume that $\tilde{f}(x,0)\equiv 0$. Then for some $\beta\in (0,1)$ there exists a $C^{2,\beta}_{{\text{loc}}}$ classical solution of
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\partial_ty=L_0y+\tilde f(y,x),\quad x\in E,\; t>0,\\
y(x,0)=g(x),\quad x\in E,\quad y(x,t)=0,\quad t>0.
\end{split}
\end{equation}

