[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2604.22644, '2604.22644'] The tail distribution of the maximum penetration depth $\displaystyle M = \max_{0 \le t \le \theta_1} X_t$ is given by:
\begin{align}
    P(M \ge k) = \int_0^1 \frac{p}{S(k;p)} dp, \quad (k = 1, 2, \dots)
\end{align}
where $S(k;p)$ is the scale function from Theorem \ref{thm1}.

