[Proposition of arXiv:2609.01910, 'On the Tur\'{a}n number of the expansion of the book'] Let $k>2$ and $t>1$. Then

    \begin{displaymath}
\ensuremath{\mathrm{ex}}_r(n,B_{t,k,s}^r)=
\left\{ \begin{array}{l l}
\Theta(n^{r-1}) & \textrm{if\/ $k\le r$},\\
(1+o(1))\binom{k-1}{r}\left(\frac{n}{k-1}\right)^r & \textrm{if\/ $k>r$}.\\
\end{array}
\right.
\end{displaymath} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

