[Lemma wavesmoothupperbound of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] There is a universal constant $C<\infty $ such that for all $n\geq 2$, $t\geq 0$ and $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$,

 \begin{align}
    e^{tn(n-1)/2}E_{(0,x),...,(0,x)}[A_0^{N_t(\mathcal{P}_n)}Z_{n,t}]\leq C\exp(A_0 t^{(2H+2)/3}n^{4/3}).
\end{align}

