body:
[Proposition prop:moments of arXiv:2604.20094, 'Persistence and local extinction for superprocesses in random environments'] Let $\nu\in {\mathcal M}_F({\mathbb R}^d)$ and $f\in C_b({\mathbb R}^d)$. Then
  	\begin{equation}
  		{\mathbf E}_\nu\langle f, X_t \rangle= \langle P_tf, \nu\rangle
  	\end{equation}
  	and
  	\begin{equation}
  		{\mathbf E}_\nu \left[ \langle f, X_t \rangle^2\right] =\langle Q_t^{{\mathcal C}} (f\otimes f), \nu\otimes\nu\rangle+\left\langle\int_0^t P_{t-s}(\pi Q_s^{{\mathcal C}} (f\otimes f))\mathrm{d} s,\nu\right\rangle.
  	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:finit n of arXiv:2603.01823, 'on a fractional stochastic heat equation arising from the disordered pinning model'] Let  $u\in L^1(\Xi)$ be a mild solution to (equation e:she of the paper) in the sense of Definition~(def: solution of the paper). Then $u_n:=\mathbb E[u|\mathcal F_n]=\mathbb E[u|\xi_1,\dots,\xi_n]$ solves the projected equation (see Definition (def:projection of the paper))
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
u_n(t,x)=1+\int_{[n]}{\raisebox{-.82em}{\hspace{-1.69em}\scriptsize \bf o}}\hspace{.7em}  \mathbf{1}_{[0,t]}(\cdot) g_{\rho}(t-\cdot,x)u_n(\cdot,0)\xi. 
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

