body:
[Lemma covering_bound of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a VC-subgraph class of functions of VC dimension $V$ and with measurable envelope $F$. Then for any probability measure $Q$ with $\|F\|_{Q,2}>0$,
\begin{equation*}
N\left(\mathcal{F}, \|\cdot\|_{L_2(Q)},\varepsilon\|F\|_{Q,2}\right)\leq \left(\frac{K}{\varepsilon}\right)^{2V}
\end{equation*}
for a universal constant $K$ and $0<\varepsilon<1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.17449, 'Spectral Simplicity and Joint Eigenvalue Densities\\ for a Non-Gaussian Brownian Time Chan'] Almost surely,
\begin{equation}
 M_b(O)>0
 \qquad\text{for every non-empty open }O\subset D.

\end{equation}
Equivalently, $\supp M_b=D$.

[Defn Stationary Radial Ornstein Uhlenbeck process SDE of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] The normalized stationary radial Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process $\mathrm{ROU}_d(m)$, is the unique solution to 
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        &dR(t)=\bigg(\frac{m(d-1)}{R(t)}-mR(t)\bigg)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{t} +m \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{W(t)} \\
        &R(0) \sim \chi_d
    \end{split}
\end{equation}
for a standard one dimensional Brownian motion $W(t)$.

[Lemma lem:occupation of arXiv:2607.22220, 'Pathwise uniqueness for degenerate stochastic differential equations with H\"{o}lder conti'] For each $i=1,\ldots,K$, $a>0$, and $T>0$, there exists a constant $C_{T,R}>0$, independent of both $n$ and $a$, such that

\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\int_0^T
\rho_s p(x_{i+1}(s))\1_{\{x_i(s)\le a\}}\,\mathrm d s
\le C_{T,R}\sqrt a.
\end{equation}

