body:
[Lemma kernel-growth of arXiv:2609.00425, 'Individual and Uniform Eventual Positivity of Self-Adjoint Semigroups'] For each $n\in\mathbb{N}$, let $h_n\colon[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}$ be given by $h_n(t)\coloneqq\mathrm{e}^{-(n-\delta_n)t}-\mathrm{e}^{-nt}$. Then one has
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{\sup_{t \geq 0} h_n(t)}{u_n} \longrightarrow 0
    \end{align*}
    as $n \to \infty$.

