body:
[Thm thm_global_sol of arXiv:2607.27472, 'The stochastic Keller--Segel system in critical spaces'] Assume that the parameters $s,s_v,q,q_v,p,\kappa$ satisfy (equation Eq_standard of the paper) and  (equation Eq_pc1_new of the paper)--(equation Eq_pc5_new of the paper), and let $g^{i}$, $i\in \{1,2\}$, satisfy Assumptions (Ass_noise of the paper) and (equation assumption_for_global of the paper). 
		Moreover, let $(u_0,v_0)$ as in (equation eq_IV of the paper) be $\mathfrak{F}_0$-measurable  and $((u,v),\sigma)$ be the $L^p_\kappa$-maximal solution  to (equation 25.06.19.16.01 of the paper) provided by Theorem (thm:local_wp of the paper). 
		{Then, for each $T <\infty$, there exists a constant $C_{T}>0$ such that for each constant $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, if}
		\[
		\mathbb{E} \|(u_0,v_0) \|_{B_{q,p}^{d/q-2}(\mathbb{T}^d)\times B_{q_v,p}^{d/q_v}(\mathbb{T}^d)}^p \,\le\, C_{T} \varepsilon,
		\]
		then we have that 
		\[
		\mathbb{P}( \sigma \ge T) \ge 1-\varepsilon.
		\]
		Moreover, there exists a stopping time $\tau\in (0, \sigma]$ such that $\mathbb{P}(\tau \ge T) \ge 1 - \varepsilon$ and, if $p>2$, it holds that
		\begin{equation}

			\begin{aligned}
				&\mathbb{E}\left[ \mathbf{1}_{\tau \ge T} \|(u,v)\|^p_{H^{\theta, p}((0,T),w_\kappa; H^{2(1-\theta)+s,q}(\mathbb{T}^d)\times H^{2(1-\theta)+s_v,q_v}(\mathbb{T}^d))} \right] \\&
				\lesssim_\theta \mathbb{E} \|(u_0,v_0)\|_{ B_{q,p}^{d/q-2}(\mathbb{T}^d)\times B_{q_v,p}^{d/q_v}(\mathbb{T}^d)}^p,
			\end{aligned}
		\end{equation}
		for all $\theta \in [0,1/2)$. 
		If $p=2$, the previous estimate (equation 26.04.16.14.29 of the paper) has to be replaced by 
		\begin{equation*}
			\begin{aligned}
				&\mathbb{E}\left[ \mathbf{1}_{\tau \ge T} (\|(u,v)\|^2_{C([0,T]; H^{1+s,2}(\mathbb{T}^d)\times H^{1+s_v,2}(\mathbb{T}^d))}+\|(u,v)\|^2_{L^2([0,T],w_\kappa; H^{2+s,2}(\mathbb{T}^d)\times H^{2+s_v,2}(\mathbb{T}^d))}) \right]\\&
				\lesssim \mathbb{E} \|(u_0,v_0)\|_{H^{d/2-2,2}(\mathbb{T}^d)\times H^{d/2,2}(\mathbb{T}^d)}^2.
			\end{aligned}
		\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

