[Proposition prop:link_gat_der_mall_der of arXiv:2605.07832, 'A Bismut -Elworthy formula for BSDEs with degenerate noise'] Let $A$ be defined as in (equation A of the paper), let $\Lambda : \mathcal{D} (\Lambda) \subseteq U \rightarrow U $ be a positive self-adjoint operator on a separable Hilbert space $U$. Then for any $h\in K $ there exists $\widetilde u_t$ such that 
\begin{align}

\int_s^te^{(t-r)A} G(r)\widetilde u_t(r)dr= e^{(t-s)A}h, \quad \mathbb P\textup{-a.s.},    
\end{align}
and, for some positive constant $C$ which does not depend on $t\in(0,T]$.
\begin{align*}
\|\widetilde u_t\|_{L^2((0,t);U)}
\leq & C \frac{|h|_{K}}{t^{3/2}};
\end{align*}
moreover if $h=Jb=\begin{pmatrix}
0 \\ b
\end{pmatrix} $  with $b\in U$, then 
\begin{align*}
    \|\widetilde u_t\|_{L^2((0,t);U)}^2
    \leq C \frac{|b|^2_U}{t},
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

