[Proposition 5 (Effective sample size) of arXiv:2604.17526, '2604.17526'] Let~$w^1_K$, \dots, $w^N_K$ be the normalized weights defined in~\eqref{e:ais-small-error-and-wki-def}.
  Then the sum of the squared weights satisfies
  \begin{equation}
    \E \sum_{i = 1}^N (w^i_K)^2 
      \leq \frac{8\paren*{4C_w +1}}{N}
    \,.
  \end{equation}
  Consequently, the expected effective sample size is bounded by
  \begin{equation}
    \E \ESS(w^1_K, \dots, w^N_K)
      \geq \frac{N}{8\paren*{4C_w +1}}
    \,.
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 43 of arXiv:2609.01826, 'An extension theory for fully fractional Schr\"odinger equations with memory'] Let $0<s<1, t>0$, and $z>0$. Then the following oscillatory identity holds:
\begin{equation}
\int_0^t
\frac{e^{i \frac{z^2}{4\sigma}}}{(t-\sigma)^{1-s}\sigma^{1+s}}\,d\sigma =
4^s\,\G(s)\,e^{i\frac{\pi s}{2}}\,t^{s-1}\,z^{-2s}
e^{i \frac{z^2}{4t}}.
\end{equation}

