[Corollary 3 of arXiv:2606.27117, 'Occupation-Time Fluctuations of an Age-Dependent Branching System Driven by Poisson Immigr'] Assume that $\gamma=1$ and let
\(
h:=3-d/\alpha.
\)
Then, for $0\le s\le t$,
$$
\mathrm{Cov}\big(\langle \X(s),\varphi\rangle,\langle \X(t),\psi\rangle\big)
=
\frac{\Gamma(1/\alpha)\langle\lambda,\varphi\rangle\langle\lambda,\psi\rangle}
{2(\frac{d}{\alpha}-1)(h-1)h
\pi\alpha}
\L[
\frac{
2s^{h+1}
+
2t^{h+1}
+
\left(h-\frac12\right)(t-s)^{h+1}
-
\frac12(t+s)^{h+1}
}{h+1}
-
t(t-s)^h\R].
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] Given $A\in M_N(\mathbb C)$, define its adjoint matrix by $(A^*)_{ij}=\bar{A}_{ji}$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item $<Ax,y>=<x,A^*y>$, for any two vectors $x,y\in\mathbb C^N$.

\item $x\to Ux$ with $U\in M_N(\mathbb C)$ is an isometry precisely when $U^*=U^{-1}$.

\item $x\to Px$ with $P\in M_N(\mathbb C)$ is a projection precisely when $P^2=P^*=P$.
\end{enumerate}

