     In [MR1326606], it is shown that 
     \begin{equation}
         \frac{\partial }{\partial e_i} \gamma(\zeta) = \int_{\mathbb{T}^d} P_i^1(\psi(x;\zeta),\nabla_x \psi(x;\zeta), \Tilde{\psi}(x;\zeta), \zeta,x) dx,
     \end{equation}
     where for fixed $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$, $P_i^1$ is a multivariate polynomial on its remaining variables. The fact that $P_i^1$ has this polynomial form transforms the ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:20d7fd1511bbbb75d2dc3cc62e80259927e2c95414a9131692e9849ebe41eacd","revision_digest":"sha256:a38b286f8e21a2af6f3604f14f00c5a9dcb16b26ac2604a7316771d7b89e9e03","source_id":"arxiv:2608.17031","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

