[Theorem 36 of arXiv:2608.27630, 'Oriented planar maps and \\ annular mating of trees'] Let $\gamma\in(0,2)\backslash\{\sqrt2\}$. There is a constant $C_\gamma>0$ such that for every $b>0$, the above boundary length process for 
    \begin{equation}
         \int_0^\infty \MT(\ell,b,\ell+a)\,\d\ell
    \end{equation}
   has law $C_\gamma B_{0,-a+bi}^{\gamma;\bbH}$. Furthermore, it is possible to define the map $F$ introduced below Definition~\ref{def:Quantum-cell} such that it a.s.\ recovers the decorated LQG surface from its boundary length process.

[Theorem t:almost_Linfty of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $0<T<\infty$. Let $p,q\in (2,\infty)$ be such that 
\begin{equation}

\frac{2}{p}+\frac{d}{q}<1.
\end{equation}
Then for all $r\in (1,\infty)$ there exists $C_0>0$ such that for any $N$, any interval $I=(t_0-T,t_0)\subset (-1/4,\infty)$ with length $T<\infty$, and
\begin{equation}

F,G\in L^r_{\mathscr{P}}(\Omega; L^p(I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d;{\mathbb R}^{d\times d}))),
\end{equation}
satisfying
\begin{equation}

\mathrm{Tr} (G)=0 \text{ a.e.\ on }\mathbb{T}^d \qquad \text{ and }\qquad \nabla \cdot G =0\text{ in }\mathscr{D}'(\mathbb{T}^d),
\end{equation} 
a.e.\ on $I\times \Omega$, it holds that 
\begin{align}

\sup_{ I\times \mathbb{T}^d}\big( {\mathbf E}|v^N|^r \big)^{1/r}
&\leq C_0  \big({\mathbf E}\|F\|_{L^p( I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))}^r\big)^{1/r}+ C_0 \big({\mathbf E}\|G\|_{L^p( I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))}^r\big)^{1/r},
\end{align}
where $v^N$ is the unique energy solution to (equation eq:turbulent_Stokes_scaling_uniform_estimates_modified of the paper).
In particular, for all $r_0\in (1,\infty)$, there exists $C_1>0$ independent of $N,t_0,F$ and $G$ for which  
\begin{align}

\big( {\mathbf E}\|v^N\|_{L^{r_0}( I\times \mathbb{T}^d)}^{r} \big)^{1/{r}}
\leq C_1  \big({\mathbf E}\|F\|_{L^p( I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))}^{r}\big)^{1/r}+ C_1 \big({\mathbf E}\|G\|_{L^p( I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))}^{r}\big)^{1/{r}}.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:GramSpectrum of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Suppose that $n \leq d$. Let $X_1,\ldots,X_n$ be independent centered random vectors in $\mathbb{R}^d$ with $\psi_1$-norm bounded by $\psi$, and let $M$ denote the Gram matrix of $X_1,\ldots,X_n$. There exist constants $C_1,C_2 > 0$ such that, for any $\theta \in (0,1)$, holds
        \begin{equation*}
            d(1 - \delta) \leq \lambda_{\min}(G) \leq \lambda_{\max}(G) \leq d(1 + \delta)
        \end{equation*}
        with probability at least
        \begin{equation}

            1 - \exp{-C_2\sqrt{n}\log(e\sqrt{d/n})} - 2\P{\max_{i=1,\ldots,n} \abs{\frac{1}{d}\left\lVert\ifblank{X_i}{\:\cdot\:}{X_i}\right\rVert_2^2 - 1} \geq \theta},
        \end{equation}
        where $\delta$ is given by
        \begin{equation}

            \delta = C_1(\psi + \sqrt{1 + \theta})^2\sqrt{\frac{n}{d}}\log(e\sqrt{d/n}) + \theta.
        \end{equation}

[Lemma lm:Input-for-complex-analysis-lemma of arXiv:2605.16162, 'Deconfinement For $\mathrm{SO}(3)$ Lattice Yang--Mills at Strong Coupling'] Suppose $\ell$ is a rectangular loop in $\Lambda$ with both side-lengths at least $15$. Then
    \begin{equs}
        \phi_{\ell}(\beta):=\beta^{16-4|\ell|}\langle W_{\ell}\rangle_{\beta,\Lambda_{\infty}}
    \end{equs}
    extends to a holomorphic function on the disk $\mbb{D}(0,\beta^*)$ with
    \begin{equs}
        \phi_{\ell}(0)\geq \bigg(\frac{1}{9}\bigg)^{|\ell|},
    \end{equs}
    and there exists a constant $C_d>0$
    \begin{equs}
        \sup_{\beta \in \mbb{D}(0,\beta^*)} |\phi_{\ell}(\beta)| \leq C_d^{|\ell|}
    \end{equs}

