body:
[Cor graph of arXiv:2412.00610, 'Joint Poisson Convergence of Monochromatic Hyperedges in Multiplex Hypergraphs'] Consider a sequence $\bm H_n = (H_n^{(1)}, H_n^{(2)})$ of 2-multiplexes. Suppose the vertices of $\bm H_n$ are colored uniformly at random with $c_n$ colors as in (equation eq:cn of the paper), such that the following hold: 
\begin{itemize}
\item $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty}  \frac{|E(H_n^{(1)})|}{c_n} = \lambda_1$ and $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty}  \frac{|E(H_n^{(2)})|}{c_n} = \lambda_2$,

\item $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{|E(H_n^{(1)}) \cap E(H_n^{(2)})|}{c_n} = \lambda_{1, 2}$, 
\end{itemize} 
for constants $\lambda_1, \lambda_2, \lambda_{1, 2} \geq 0$, with $\lambda_{1,2} \le \lambda_1$ and $\lambda_{1,2} \le \lambda_2$. Then
  $$ \bm T(\bm H_n) \dto \left(\begin{array}{l}
          Z_1 + Z_{1,2} \\
          Z_2 + Z_{1,2}
          \end{array}\right) , $$
  where $Z_1 \sim \Pois(\lambda_1 - \lambda_{1,2})$, $Z_2 \sim \Pois(\lambda_2 - \lambda_{1,2})$, and $Z_{1,2} \sim \Pois(\lambda_{1,2})$ are independent. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:mixed-packet-debit of arXiv:2608.29403, 'Kac's Walk on Rotation Matrices Mixes in $\boldsymbol{\Theta(n^2)}$ Steps:\\ A Proof Disco'] Under the hypotheses of (lem:heterogeneous-packet of the paper), label every
vertex by either $W_i^\circ$ or $X_i$.  If at least one vertex is labelled
$X_i$, then
\[
 \boxed{
 \|\zeta_{P,\tau}\|_{\mathscr P_\tau}
 \le C^{|P|}n^{c^{\!*}(P)-2}n^{-1/2}.}
\tag{3.4.1x$_{7h}$}
\]
This debit is pointwise in $i$ and remains multiplicative under the
simultaneous one-base-per-circuit contraction.

