[Proposition of arXiv:2505.01739, 'Stochastic dominance for linear combinations of infinite-mean risks'] Let $X_1,\dots,X_n\sim F$ be iid where $F\in\mathcal H$. For vectors $(\theta_1, \ldots, \theta_n)$ and $(\eta_1, \ldots, \eta_n)$ in $\mathbb{R}^n_+$ such that $(\theta_1, \ldots, \theta_n) \preceq^w (\eta_1, \ldots, \eta_n)$,
\begin{equation*}
\sum_{i=1}^n \eta_i X_i \leq_{\rm st} \sum_{i=1}^n \theta_i X_i.
\end{equation*}

