[Definition def: bad events of arXiv:2411.10271, '$A$-localized states for clock models on trees and their extremal decomposition into glass'] Let $A\subset \mathbb{Z}_q$. We define the set of \uline{$A$-irregular edges} of the configuration $\omega \in \Omega$ by
    \begin{equation*}
        D_A(\omega):=\{\{x,y\}\in E:~\omega_x\neq \omega_y~\text{or}~\omega_x\in A^c~\text{or}~\omega_y\in A^c\}.
    \end{equation*}
    Furthermore, denote the set of edges attached to $\gamma \subset V$ by 
    \begin{equation*}
        E(\gamma):=\{\{x,y\}\in E,\{x,y\}\cap \gamma \neq \emptyset\}.
    \end{equation*}

[Lemma lem:interpolatedExpMoment of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Under the hypotheses of (prop:uniformBoundRepulsive of the paper), including (equation eq:logRateExtraAssumptions of the paper) when $\mathsf{s}=0$, for every fixed $\beta\ge0$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{N\ge1}\ \sup_{0<\eta\le\eta_0}\ \sup_{0\le t\le1}\
{\mathbb{E}}_{\mu^{\otimes N}}\Big[e^{-\beta W_{N,\eta,t}}\Big]\le C_{\mathrm{cf}}(2\beta,\mu).
\end{align}

