body:
[Lemma lemma_RN_infty of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] For $(\delta_m)_m$ as in Lemma (lemma_thinness_gamma of the paper), almost surely, for $\xi \in \{+,-\}$ with $j(\xi)=L$ if $\xi=+$ and $j(\xi)=R$ if $\xi=-1$,
\begin{align} 
    \lim_{m \to \infty} \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} \frac{C_{\sigma}^{-k}h^k}{k!}\delta_m^{\frac{15k}{8}} {\mathbb{E}}_{m,j(\xi)}^{\xi} \big[\big( \sum_{x \in \Omega_{m,j(\xi)}}\sigma_x\big)^k \big]
    = \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} \frac{h^k}{k!} \int_{\Omega_{j(\xi)}^k} f_{j(\xi)}^{(\xi,k)}(x_1, \dots ,x_k) \prod_{j=1}^{k} dx_j < \infty
\end{align}
where the functions $f_{j(\xi)}^{(\xi,k)}:=f_{\Omega_{j(\xi)}}^{(\xi,k)}$ are as in Theorem (theorem_spin_correlations of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem SSK with external field \cite{ChenDeyPanchenko,Baiketal21,landon2020fluctuations} of arXiv:2510.26960, 'Free energy fluctuations in SK and related spin glass models: \\ A literature survey'] For fixed external field strength $h>0$, the free energy of SSK at any inverse temperature $\beta>0$ exhibits the following convergence in distribution as $N\to\infty$:
 \begin{equation} 
N^{1/2}(F_N(\beta,h)-F(\beta,h))\to \mathcal{N}(0,v_{h,\beta})
 \end{equation} 
where formulas for $F(\beta,h)$ and $v_{h,\beta}$ can be found in Results 5.5-5.6 of [Baiketal21]. Note in particular
\begin{itemize}
\item As $h\to0$, the value of $F(\beta,h)$ converges to the formula given in (equation eq:limitingF_SSK of the paper);
\item The value of $v_{h,\beta}$ changes slightly depending on whether one chooses the external field to be random (as in [Baiketal21]) or deterministic (as in [ChenDeyPanchenko,landon2020fluctuations]).  See Section 5.3 of [Baiketal21] for a comparison.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

