[Lemma erasedmassdefintro of arXiv:2608.09856, '\bf Mass erasure on measured $\bbR$-trees,\\ applications to L\'evy forests'] Let $(T, d, \rho)$ be a rooted Polish $\mathbb{R}$-tree. Let $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_f (T)$ and let $h \in \mathbb{R}^*_+$. 
Then there is a unique ${\cal E}_h \mu \! \in \!  \mathcal{M}_f(T)$ such that 
\begin{equation}

({\cal E}_h \mu)  ( \theta_\sigma T) = \left( \mu (\theta_\sigma T) \! -\! h \right)_+ \; , \quad \sigma \! \in \!  T \; . 
\end{equation}
We call ${\cal E}_h \mu$ the \emph{$h$-erasure of $\mu$}. We also adopt the convention that ${\cal E}_0 \mu \! :=\!   \mu$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 20 (Polynomial-degree stationary potentials) of arXiv:2609.01143, 'The voter model on the hyperbolic graph'] At $\varphi=2-2\alpha$, for every fixed $\gamma>0$, with high probability uniformly over vertices with $h(v)\geq\gamma R$,
\begin{equation}
R_{2-2\alpha}(v)\leq \de(v)^{-\chi}n^{o(1)}.                                          
\end{equation}

[Definition String trajectory of arXiv:2505.16585, 'Expanded regimes of area law for lattice Yang--Mills theories'] A \textit{string trajectory} starting at $(s,K,Q)$ of length $l$ is a finite sequence
\begin{equs}
\Big((s_0,K_0,Q_0), (s_1,K_1,Q_1), \ldots, (s_l,K_l,Q_l)\Big),
\end{equs}
where $(s_0,K_0,Q_0)=(s,K,Q)$, and at each non-terminal step $i<l$, $s_i$ is non-null, and if $s_i$ is stuck in a minimal union of connected components $Q \sse P$, then $|Q|<\underbar{area}(s_i)$ and
\begin{equs}
(s_{i+1},K_{i+1},Q_{i+1}) \in \mc{R}(s_i,K_i,Q_i).
\end{equs}
In the case where $s_i$ is not stuck, then
\begin{equs}
(s_{i+1},K_{i+1},Q_{i+1}) \in \mbb{S}_{\pm}((s_i,K_i,Q_i),\mbf{e})\cup \mbb{M}_{\pm}((s_i,K_i,Q_i),\mbf{e})\cup\mbb{D}_{\pm}((s_i,K_i,Q_i),\mbf{e}).
\end{equs}

