[Lemma Phi-equicont of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Fix $0<\delta <\eta <1$ and $i\in \{1,2\}$. Then there
exists $N$ such that for all $n\geq N$ and all $x,y\in \lbrack \delta ,\eta
] $, 
\begin{equation}
|\Phi _{n}^{i}(x)-\Phi _{n}^{i}(y)|\leq |x-y|.  
\end{equation}
In particular, the tail family $\{\Phi _{n}^{i}\}_{n\geq N}$ is
equicontinuous and uniformly bounded on $[\delta ,\eta ]$.

[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2608.10876, 'Exponential Contraction for Underdamped Langevin Diffusions with Superlinear Forces'] Suppose that Assumptions \ref{as4.0}--\ref{as4.3} and \eqref{growth-regime} hold. Then \(R_\star\) defined in \eqref{Rstar-explicit} is finite. For every \(R\geq R_\star\),
\(\mathcal H\subset S_R\times S_R\).
Moreover, if at least one of \((x,v)\) and \((x',v')\) lies outside \(S_R\), then
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&2C_5+
\left(\frac{2C_5}{\eta_{3,R}}+F(x,v)+F(x',v')\right)
\left(2\gamma+1
+\frac{|\nabla U(x)-\nabla U(x')|}{\gamma |x-x'|}\right)\\
\leq &F(x,v)G(x,v)+F(x',v')G(x',v'),
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where the quotient is understood to be \(0\) when \(x=x'\). All constants are defined in \eqref{radius-1}, \eqref{radius-2}, \eqref{radius-3}, and \eqref{radius-45}.

