body:
[Lemma lem:completed of arXiv:2609.01672, '\textbf{All-Minors Matrix-Tree Theory for Superport Networks:\\ Completed Quotient-Inciden'] For \(F\in\mathcal{F}_{q-k+1}\) and \(|I|=k\),
\begin{equation}
\widehat\chi_F(I)\in\{0,+1,-1\},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\widehat\chi_F(I)\neq0
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
N\setminus I\text{ is a spanning tree of }H_F.

\end{equation}
Moreover, if \(\varepsilon_N(I)\) denotes the proof-level Jacobi orientation sign defined below, then
\begin{equation}
\widehat\chi_F(I)=(-1)^{k(q+1)}\varepsilon_N(I)\chi_F(N\setminus I).

\end{equation}

