[Lemma disclOU of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] There exists a deterministic sequence $(r_n)_{n\in\mathbb N}$ that goes to $0$ as $n$ goes to infinity such that a.s. for every $(x,t)\in D\times[0,T]$
    \begin{equation*}
        \limsup_{\varepsilon\to 0}\frac{\Phi_{\varepsilon}(x,t)}{\ln(\frac{1}{\varepsilon})} 
        = 
        \limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac{\Phi_{r_n}(x,t)}{\ln(\frac{1}{r_n})}.
    \end{equation*}
    Of course, the same holds when using $\liminf$ instead of $\limsup$.

