[Definition def:momentmap of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] We define the following \emph{potential} function $\Phi:M\to\mathbb{R}$ given for all $x\in M$ by 
 \begin{equation}
  \Phi(x):=\frac{1}{2}\log (\mathrm{K}(x)).
 \end{equation}
 Moreover, the \emph{moment map} is defined to be the one form $\mu:M\to T^*M$ given for all $x\in M$ by 
 \begin{equation}
  \mu(x):=D_x\Phi=\frac{1}{\mathrm{K}(x)}\mathbb{E}\left[\mathcal{X}(x)D_x \mathcal{X}\right].
 \end{equation}

[Lemma of arXiv:2602.11129, 'Information-Theoretic Thresholds for Bipartite Latent-Space Graphs Under Noisy Observation'] Given any $r_1, \ldots, r_k \in \alpha \times \alpha$, set $\gamma \coloneqq {\textsc{Supp}}(r_1, \ldots, r_k)$. Then for any $\beta \subseteq \alpha$ and all $\mathbf{t}$, we have 
    \begin{align*}
         \Phi_{\beta}^{(r_1, \ldots, r_k)}(\mathbf{t}) =  \Phi_{\beta \cap \gamma}^{(r_1, \ldots, r_k)}(\mathbf{t}).
    \end{align*}

