[Proposition 17 (Explicit expression of Hermite polynomials) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For any $n\in\N_0$, one has 
\begin{equation}
 H_n(x) = n!\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor n/2 \rfloor}
 \frac{(-1)^k}{2^kk!(n-2k)!}x^{n-2k}\;.
\end{equation}

