[Lemma lem:multColDen of arXiv:2508.03577, 'Phase Transitions in a Particle Model\\ for the Self-Adaptive Response to Cancer Dynamics'] Let $\chi_i=\1\gk{\textnormal{column }i\equiv 1}$. Then, if $M,N\to\infty$ and $M/N$ converges to a constant and $b=\tfrac{Mp}{qN}$ remains fixed, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}_\pi\left[\sum_i \chi_i\right]\sim  N  \frac{\Gamma(1+b)}{M^{b}}\, .
    \end{equation}

