    A function $f : \mathcal X^n \to \R$ fulfills the bounded differences property if for $c_1,...,c_n \geq 0$ and all $i \in [n]$: 
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{y, x_1,...,x_n \in \mathcal X} |f(x_1,...,x_n) - f(x_1,...x_{i-1} y, x_{i+1},...,x_n)| \leq c_i.
    \end{align*}

[Theorem thm:entropic_stability:gen of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Let (ass:differentiability of the paper) hold and $\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\nu},\,\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\mu}$  be the  the unique optimizers in (equation EOT of the paper) for the set of marginals $(\rho,\nu)$ and $(\rho,\mu)$. If there exists $\Lambda>0$ and a non-negative function $\omega\colon\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{Y}\to \mathbb{R}$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
y\mapsto c(x,y)+\psi^{\nu}_\varepsilon(y)
\end{equation*}
is $(\Lambda,\omega)$-semiconcave uniformly in $x\in\supp(\rho)$, then
\begin{equation*}
\mathrm{KL}(\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\mu}|\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\nu})\leq \mathrm{KL}(\mu|\nu)+\frac{\Lambda}{2{\varepsilon}}\,\mathbf{W}_\omega(\mu,\nu)\,.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

