[Theorem Tclt1 of arXiv:2510.22701, 'Gaussian fluctuations in Mean Field Stable matchings'] Let $\mu_n=\operatorname{\mathbb E} W_{n,2}$ and $\sigma^2_n = \mathrm{Var}(W_{n,2})$. If $d>2$ and $\log^4 n\leqslant \kappa_n \ll n^{(d-2)/(2(d-1))}$, then
    \begin{align}
        \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{\mu_n }{\operatorname{\mathbb E} C_{n,n}^{\scriptscriptstyle\rm{Wei}} } = 1, \quad \lim_{n\to\infty}  \frac{\sigma_n^2}{\mathrm{Var}(C_{n,n}^{\scriptscriptstyle\rm{Wei}})} = 1, 
    \end{align}
    and,  as $n\to\infty$,
    \begin{align}
        \frac{W_{n,2}-\mu_n}{\sigma_n}\overset{\mathrm{d}}{\longrightarrow} \mathcal{N}(0,1).
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Conjecture conj:1 of arXiv:2510.20461, 'Long time behaviour of one facilitated kinetically constrained models: results and open pr'] For any $q\in (0,1)$ and any function $f$ depending on the state of finitely many vertices
\begin{equation}

\lim_{t\to\infty}|{\ensuremath{\mathbb E}} _{\nu
}(f(\eta(t)))-\pi(f)|=0,
