[Thm EL_equations of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] The limit shape flow $\omega$ for $(R,b)$ is the solution to the following system of differential equations:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item the divergence equation, 
        \begin{align}
            \text{div}(\omega(x)) = \sum_{i=1}^d \pd{\omega_i}{x_i}(x) = 0;
        \end{align}
        \item a collection of ${d\choose 2}$ equations:
        \begin{align}
            \pd{}{x_i} \pd{}{s_j}\sigma(\omega(x)) - \pd{}{x_j}\pd{}{s_i}\sigma(\omega(x)) =0 
        \end{align}
        for all $i\neq j$ between $1$ and $d$.
    \end{itemize}

