[Corollary 28 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] Let $\epsilon\in\{0,1\}^{\ell}$.  For an occurrence $t$ of colour $j<n$,
let $t_j^+$ be the next occurrence of colour $j$, with
$t_j^+=\ell+1$ if none exists.  Then
$\mathfrak C(\mathbf i,\epsilon,\mathbf d)$ is balanced if and only if
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{\substack{t<s<t_j^+\\ i_s=j-1}}\epsilon_s
 +d_j\mathbf 1_{\{t_j^+=\ell+1\}}
 \ge\epsilon_t
\end{equation}
for every such $t$.  Initial states and rank $n$ impose no condition.

[Lemma lem-expnumbershreds of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] There is a $C\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for any $P\in{\mathcal M }_1^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\rm s}})}}}({\mathcal S })$, and for any $R\in\mathbb{N}$,
\begin{equation}
\int \partial\Pi_{W_{R}}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({\mathcal S }})}}}(P)({\rm d}\mu)\,|\mu|
\leq \frac {C|W_R|}R \Big(J_{W_R}(\Pi_{W_{R}}(P))+\langle P,\mathfrak N_U^{\ssup\ell}\rangle-\frac1{|W_R|}\langle\Pi_{W_R}^{\ssup{{\mathcal S }}}(\xi),\mathfrak p_{W_R}\rangle\Big).
\end{equation}

