[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2609.02808, 'Minimizers of Laplace eigenvalues under a lower curvature bound'] Fix $\mu>0$, let $\gamma$ be the phase of the natural-at-$0$ solution of
$(\varphi u')'+\mu\varphi u=0$, and let $\zeta$ be as above. Then
\begin{equation}
\gamma(t)\le\zeta(t)=\bar\gamma(\tau(t);\mu)
\qquad\text{for all }t\in(0,D).
\end{equation}

[Lemma PAS of arXiv:2601.15223, 'Large time behaviour for a class of 2D and 3D stochastic non-Newtonian fluids of different'] Suppose that condition (equation third-grade-paremeters-res of the paper) and Hypothesis (Hyp-f-B of the paper) are satisfied. Then the non-autonomous random dynamical system $\Phi$ associated with the system (equation STGF of the paper) possesses a $\mathfrak{D}$-pullback random absorbing set $\mathcal{M}=\{\mathcal{M}(\mathfrak{r},\omega):\mathfrak{r}\in\mathbb{R},\omega\in\Omega\}\in\mathfrak{D}$, where  $\mathcal{M}(\mathfrak{r},\omega)$ is defined by 
		\begin{align}
			\mathcal{M}(\mathfrak{r},\omega)=\{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{Y}}\in\mathbb{H}:\|\boldsymbol{\mathcal{Y}}\|^2_{\mathbb{H}}\leq\mathcal{K}(\mathfrak{r},\omega)\},
		\end{align}
		and $\mathcal{K}(\mathfrak{r},\omega)$ is given by
		\begin{align*}
			\mathcal{K}(\mathfrak{r},\omega)=  \frac{4e^{2y(\omega)} }{\min\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\{2\nu\varepsilon_0,\sigma^2\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\}} \int_{-\infty}^{0} e^{\frac{\sigma^2}{2}\zeta+2\sigma\int^{0}_{\zeta} y(\vartheta_{\upeta}\omega)\/\mathrm{d}\/ \upeta} \Upsilon^2(\zeta,\omega) \|\boldsymbol{\mathfrak{K}}(\cdot,\zeta+\mathfrak{r})\|^2_{\mathbb{H}^{-1}}\/\mathrm{d}\/ \zeta.
		\end{align*}

