[Corollary cor: thm for space v_initial of arXiv:2512.12902, 'Non-equilibrium fluctuations for the \\stirring process with births and deaths'] Let  $K\geq 2$ be a fixed  integer number  and $\zeta>0$. For any initial product measure $\mu^{\epsilon}$ satisfying (equation Ass1 of the paper),  and time  $0<t\leq T$
\begin{equation}
\sup_{\underline{x}\in\Lambda_{N}^{n,\neq}}|v^{\epsilon}_{n}( \underline{x},t|\mu^{\epsilon})|)-v^{\epsilon}_{n}( \underline{x}+\underline e_1,t|\mu^{\epsilon})|)\lesssim
\begin{cases}
\epsilon,&\;1\leq n\leq K\\
 \epsilon^{1+\zeta}, &n\geq K+1,
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where $\underline e_1$ being the unit vector in the positive 1st-direction. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition Global well-posedness--small data in critical space of arXiv:2605.28194, 'Delayed Blow-up in 3D Fluids via Pseudo-Transport Noise'] Let $a\in [-1,0),\,2b+a =0\text{ and } p=4$. For every $\epsilon\in (0,1)$, there exists $\delta=\delta(\nu,\epsilon)>0$ such that for all $s\geq0$ and \begin{equation*}
			u^N(s)\in L^p((\Omega,\mathcal{F}_s,\mathbb{P});X_{tr}) \quad \text{ and }\quad \|u^N(s)\|_{L^p(\Omega,X_{tr})}\leq \delta,
		\end{equation*}
		the local strong solution $u^N$ to (equation NS-SMR section of the paper) is global on $[s,\infty)$ with probability no less than $1-\epsilon$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 25 of arXiv:2608.31054, 'Revisiting Picard's proof of the Picard--Weber--Weck selection theorem'] Let $  u \in H_0(\Rot;\Omega)$. Then, 
    $J_\Phi^\top \widetilde{  u} \in H_0(\Rot;Q)$ and
    \begin{equation*}
        \Rotcirc_Q{(J_\Phi^\top \widetilde{  u})} 
        =  J_\Phi^\top\,\widetilde{\Rotcirc_\Omega   u}\,J_\Phi =: ( J_\Phi^\top \otimes J_\Phi^\top )\widetilde{\Rotcirc_\Omega   u}.
    \end{equation*}

