[Corollary 3 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Let~$\{T_k\}_{k\ge0}$ have the law of $\{\frac12|B_k|^2\}_{k\ge0}$ for~$B$ denoting a standard two-dimen\-sional Brownian motion. Let~$\{Z_{T_k}\}_{k\ge0}$  be a sequence of random Borel measures on~$[0,1]$ coupled with~$\{T_k\}_{k\ge0}$ so that \eqref{E:1.21a} holds as stated. Then
\begin{equation}

\ZZ(\textd x)\laweq \sum_{k\ge1}1_{ [b^{-k-1},b^{-k})}(x)\, b^{-2k} Z_{T_k}\bigl(b^k\textd x\bigr). 
\end{equation}
A.e.\ sample of~$\ZZ$ is diffuse. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lmm lmmGlobalLimitObs of arXiv:2607.29423, 'Schwarzian Field Theory at High Temperatures'] Let $s_1, s_2, s_3, s_4 \in \mathbb{T}$ be distinct points which lie on $\mathbb{T}$ in the clockwise order.
Then
\begin{equation}
\lim_{\sigma\to \infty}
\left[
\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma^2}^{-1}
\int_{\mathrm{Diff}^1(\mathbb{T})/\mathrm{PSL}(2, \mathbb{R})} 
\cross{\phi}{s_1}{s_2}{s_3}{s_4}\left(1- \cross{\phi}{s_1}{s_2}{s_3}{s_4}\right)
\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathscr{M}_{\sigma^2} (\phi)\right]
=
0.
\end{equation}
Suppose now that $s_1, s_2, t$ are distinct points which lie on $\mathbb{T}$ in the clockwise order.
Then
\begin{equation}
\lim_{
\substack{
s_4\to t+\\
s_3\to t-
}
}
\left[
\limsup_{\sigma\to \infty}
\left[
\mathcal{Z}_{\sigma^2}^{-1}
\int_{\mathrm{Diff}^1(\mathbb{T})/\mathrm{PSL}(2, \mathbb{R})} 
\cross{\phi}{s_1}{s_2}{s_3}{s_4}
\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mathscr{M}_{\sigma^2} (\phi)\right]
\right]
=
0.
\end{equation}

