body:
[Proposition prop:decreasHypGRF of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] Let $m>1$ and assume that $f_0(x)\neq 0$ for all $x\in M$ and let $t\in \mathbb{R}$ be a regular value of $\Phi_0$. Consider $S_t:=\Phi_0^{-1}(t)$ smooth hypersurface in $M$. For any admissible random fields $W\randin C^\infty(S_t,\mathbb{R}^{m-2})$ on $S_t$ and all open set $U\subset S_t$, we have:
  \begin{equation}
    \mathbb{E}\#\sol{\mathcal{X}_0|_{S_t},W; U}\leq \mathbb{E}\#\sol{\mathcal{X}|_{S_t},W; U}.
  \end{equation} 
   In particular
  \begin{equation}
    \esol{\mathcal{X}_0|_{S_t}; U}\leq \esol{\mathcal{X}|_{S_t}; U}.
  \end{equation} 
  In both cases, the inequality is an equality if and only if the right hand side is zero in which case every term is equal to zero.

