[Proposition prop:convergenceOnepoint of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] Let $L$ be a L\'evy process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ fulfilling (equation eq-nonsingular of the paper) and let $X$ be the corresponding stochastic exponential.
		Assume that $G_X$ satisfies condition (i-p) and $\mathds{E} \big[\sup_{0 \le s \le 1} M(X_s)^\epsilon \big]<\infty$ for some $\epsilon >0$. 
	Then there are $\gamma>0$, $0<c<1$ and $n_0 \in \N$, such that for all $n\ge n_0$ and all $f \in \mathcal{B}_\gamma$,
	\begin{align}
	\sup_{y,z \in P(\mathbb{R}^d)} \sup_{0 \le r \le 1}	\Big|\mathds{E} \big[f(Z_{n+r}^y)\big] - \mathds{E} \big[f(Z_n^z)\big] \Big| \le [f]_\gamma c^n.
	\end{align}
	Moreover, there are constants $d>0$ and $D>0$ such that for all $t>0$ and all $f \in \mathcal{B}_\gamma$, 
	\begin{align}
		\Big| \mathds{E} \big[f(Z_{t}^y)\big] - \pi(f) \Big| \le D [f]_\gamma e^{-dt}.
	\end{align}

