[Lemma upper_bound_on_the_second_moment_of_the_occupied_sets_size_for_worms of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] Let us consider a graph $G$ with a transitive  subgroup of its automorphisms $\Gamma \leq \mathrm{Aut}(G)$.
Let $\nu_{o}$ be a $\Gamma$-rotation invariant measure on $\mathcal{H}_{o}$, then $\nu$ the measure on $Z$ induced from $\nu_{o}$ via (equation def:induced_measure_on_zoospace of the paper), and $\mathcal{X} = \sum_{i \in I} \delta_{(x,H)_i} \sim \mathcal{Q}_{\nu}^\lambda$.
Given some $R \in \mathbb{N}$ and an event $A^R \in \mathcal{Z}$ for which $A^R \subseteq Z^R(V(G))$ holds, let us consider the restricted zoo $\bar{\mathcal{X}} := \mathcal{X} \mathds{1} \left[ A^R \right]$ introduced in~(equation eq:set_hitting_animals_of_volume_at_most_R of the paper). Then we have
\begin{equation}

	\mathbb{E} \left[ \left| \mathrm{Tr} \left( \bar{ \mathcal{X} } \right) \right|^2 \right] \leq 
	\left( \left| \mathcal{B}(o, R) \right| + 1 \right) \cdot \mathbb{E}\left[ \left| \mathrm{Tr} \left( \bar{ \mathcal{X} } \right) \right| \right] + 
	\mathbb{E}^2 \left[ \left| \mathrm{Tr} \left( \bar{ \mathcal{X} } \right) \right| \right],
\end{equation}
from which it obviously follows that 
\begin{equation}

	\mathrm{Var} \left( \left| \mathrm{Tr} \left( \bar{\mathcal{X}} \right) \right| \right) \leq 
	\left( \left| \mathcal{B}(o, R) \right| + 1 \right) \cdot \mathbb{E}\left[ \left| \mathrm{Tr} \left( \bar{ \mathcal{X} } \right) \right| \right].
\end{equation}

