body:
[Lemma lem:lower of arXiv:2607.05054, 'Root Dynamics of Differentiated Polynomials with Rotationally Invariant Structure'] Under the same assumptions, after $ \ell m $ differentiations, the $ j $-th smallest radius $ r_j^{(n,m,\ell)} $ (for $ 1 \leq j \leq n-\ell $) satisfies  
\begin{align}
r_j^{(n,m,\ell)} \geq r_{j+\ell} \prod_{s=1}^{\ell} \left(1 - \frac{1}{\max\left(1, j+s-2 - y\right)}\right).
\end{align}  
In particular, if $ j > y + 2 $, then  
\begin{align}
r_j^{(n,m,\ell)} \geq r_{j+\ell} \frac{j - 2 - y}{j + \ell - 2 - y} \geq r_{j+\ell} \frac{j - 2 - y}{j + \ell}.
\end{align}  
For $ j \leq y + 2 $, the bound holds trivially as the right-hand side is nonpositive.

