[Theorem 3 (One-sided cumulants) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] Assume the set-up and conditions of Theorem~\ref{theo:main}. For $q=0$ and any fixed $p\ge 3$ it holds that
\begin{equation}
\kappa_{p,0}\left(X\right) = \frac{\eta^p}{N^{(p-2)/2}}\left(K_{p,0}(z)\kappa_p^{\mathrm{d}} + \mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{N^{1/2}}\right)\right),

\end{equation}
uniformly in $z\in\mathcal{D}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Cor 16 of arXiv:2608.30763, 'Ultracontractivity of heat semigroups with non-local Robin boundary conditions via two-sid'] For every $\varepsilon > 0$ there exists a constant $\beta(\varepsilon) > 0$ such that
\begin{align*}
& \Re \int_{\Omega} A \nabla u \cdot \overline{\nabla u} \d x + 
\Re \int_{\partial \Omega} B\gamma(u) \overline{\gamma(u)} \d \sigma(x) & \\
& \geq \ \left( \alpha - \varepsilon \| B \|_{\mathrm{L}^{2} \to \mathrm{L}^{2}} \right)  \| \nabla u \|_{\mathrm{L}^{2}(\Omega)^{d}}^{2}
- \beta(\varepsilon) \| B \|_{\mathrm{L}^{2} \to \mathrm{L}^{2}}   \| u \|_{\mathrm{L}^{2}(\Omega)}^{2} &
\end{align*}
is true for every $u \in H^{1}(\Omega)$.

