body:
[Proposition 31 of arXiv:2605.08844, 'Signature Kernel and Schwinger-Dyson Kernel Equations as Two-Parameter Rough Differential '] The equation
    \begin{equation}
Z_{s,t} = 1 - \sum_{\iota=1}^d \int_s^t \int_s^r Z_{s,u} Z_{u,r} dX^\iota_u dX^\iota_r.
\end{equation}
admits a unique solution.

