[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.29143, 'Least Variability in a Polynomial-Square Class\\ of Rational Kernels'] Let \(\widetilde a(x)=a(x/\beta)\). Then \(a\mapsto\widetilde a\) is a bijection of \(\Pcal_m\), with inverse \(p(t)\mapsto p(\beta t)\), and
\begin{equation*}
    \mathcal J_{\beta,\mu}(a)
    =\mathcal J_{1,\beta\mu}(\widetilde a).
\end{equation*}

[Lemma lem:smallissmall of arXiv:2606.11677, 'Feynman--Kac formula for the heat equation with a one-center point interaction in $d=3$.'] For each $t>0$, $x\in {\mathbb{R}}^3$, we have \begin{align*}
\varlimsup_{\delta\to 0}\varlimsup_{\varepsilon\to 0}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{t}{a_\varepsilon}}\sigma^{\varepsilon,x}_i1\{\sigma^{\varepsilon,x}_i<\delta\}\right]=0.
\end{align*}

