[Theorem of arXiv:2510.20013, '\bf Counterexample to\\ majority optimality in NICD with erasures'] For \(p=0.40\) one has
\begin{align*}
&\Phi_{0.40}(f)=\frac{2689}{6250}=0.43024,\quad
\Phi_{0.40}(\mathrm{Maj}_5)=\frac{5363}{12500}=0.42904,
\end{align*}
hence \(\Phi_{0.40}(f)> \Phi_{0.40}(\mathrm{Maj}_5)\). In particular, majority is not optimal at \(p=0.4\) already for \(n=5\).

