body:
[Thm 1 of arXiv:2606.21778, 'Pontryagin Maximum Principle in Free Probability Theory'] Let $\hat{u} \in U$ and $\hat{x}$ the associated controlled diffusion. Suppose that there exists a solution $(\hat{y}, \hat{z})$ to the associated BSDE \eqref{eq:BSDE-classic}, such that

\begin{equation*}
	H\left(t, \hat{x}_t, \hat{u}_t, \hat{y}_t, \hat{z}_t\right)=\max _{u \in U} H\left(t, \hat{x}_t, u, \hat{y}_t, \hat{z}_t\right), \quad 0 \leq t \leq T, \quad \text { a.s. } 
\end{equation*}

and

\begin{equation*}
	(x, u) \rightarrow H\left(t, x, u, \hat{y}_t, \hat{z}_t\right) \quad \text { is a concave function, }
\end{equation*}

for all $t \in[0, T]$. Then $\hat{u}$ is an optimal control, i.e.

$$
J(\hat{u})=\sup _{u \in U} J(u) .
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:replacement of arXiv:2605.26652, 'Pathological Large Deviations of the KMP Process in Dimension $d\ge 2$'] Let $F$ be local, locally Lipschitz and satisfy the growth bound $|F(\xi)|\le C(1+\sum_{x\in A}\xi_x)$, for some finite set $A$. For fixed $\varphi\in C([0,T]\times\mathbb T^d)$, fixed $K$, and fixed $\delta>0$, it holds that \begin{equation}
 \limsup_{\varepsilon\downarrow0} \limsup_N\mathbb{Q}^{N,K}\left(\left|\int_0^T V^{F,N,\varphi}_\varepsilon(t,\xi^N_t)\mathrm d t \right|>\delta\right)=0.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2608.30551, 'Critical Discrete Hardy Inequalities in $L^p$'] Let \(\sigma\in(0,1/2)\) and \(\alpha\in(\sigma,1/2)\). Then
\begin{equation}
    \Delta^\sigma k_{-\alpha}=k_{\sigma-\alpha}.
\end{equation}
In particular, \(\Delta^\sigma k_{-\alpha}>0\), and hence \(k_{-\alpha}\) is
strictly superharmonic. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 46 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $f \in C_b^{2 \alpha,3}([0,T] \times W,\bar{W})$ be arbitrary. Then there exists $g \in C_b^{2 \alpha,2}([0,T] \times (W \times W), L(W,\bar{W}))$ with $\| g \|_{C_b^{2 \alpha,2}} \leq \| f \|_{C_b^{2 \alpha,3}}$ such that
\begin{align}
f(t,y_1) - f(t,y_2) = g(t,y) (y_1-y_2)
\end{align}
for all $t \in [0,T]$ and all $y = (y_1,y_2) \in W \times W$.

