[Theorem 16 of arXiv:2608.30174, 'Exact counting of spherical metrics with one conical singularity on rectangular tori'] Let \(u\in X_{\rm ax}\) be a solution of \eqref{eq:mfe}, and suppose that a nonzero function \(\phi\in X_{\rm ax}\) satisfies
\[
(\Delta+\e^u)\phi=0.
\]
Let \(q_t\) be the holomorphic path defined in \eqref{eq:exact-q-path-preview}. 
Given that the base point \(p_0\), let \(M_h(B(t))\) and \(M_v(B(t))\) be the corresponding monodromy matrices, as defined in Section \ref{Sec 3}. Recall $\mathcal{Z}(B)=\operatorname{tr}
\bigl(M_h(B)M_v(B)\bigr) $, then
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\dd}{\dd t}\operatorname{Im}\mathcal{Z}(B(t))\bigg|_{t=0}=0.
\end{equation}

[Definition heatkernel of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] The fundamental solution of the heat equation in dimension $d$ is given by
\begin{align}

p_h(t,x) = \frac{1}{(2\pi t)^{d/2}} \exp\left(-\frac{|x|^2}{2t}\right).
\end{align}

[Theorem 4 (Uniform Christoffel bound) of arXiv:2608.30304, '2608.30304'] For all $n\in\Nzero$, all
$\alpha,\beta\ge-1/2$ and all $x\in(-1,1)$,
\begin{equation}
\lambda_n^{(\alpha,\beta)}(x)
\ \ge\ \frac{w_{\alpha,\beta}(x)\sqrt{1-x^2}}
{3C_*^2\,(n+1)\,\Phi_n(\alpha+\beta+1)} .
\end{equation}
In particular the Gauss--Jacobi quadrature weights for
$w_{\alpha,\beta}$ obey the same lower bound at their nodes. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 23 (First variation of the model Dyson equation) of arXiv:2608.07820, 'Linear Spectral Statistics for Entrywise-Transformed Spiked Wigner Matrices under Shifted '] Let \(\overline m_N\) and \(\overline m_N^0\) be as in
Proposition~\ref{prop:R3-external-input}, for \(S_N\) and \(S_N^0\),
respectively.  Uniformly on \(\Gamma\),
\begin{equation}
 N\bigl(\overline m_N(z)-\overline m_N^0(z)\bigr)
 \longrightarrow
 \lambda\beta_2^{f,\nu}
 \frac{m(z)^3}{1-m(z)^2}.
\end{equation}
The linear profile and the remainder have zero order-one response.

