body:
[Corollary 26 (Sudakov-type comparison through supremum relaxation) of arXiv:2606.07931, 'Pointwise Complexity for Gaussian Fields:\\Upper Envelopes, Algorithmic Lower Bounds, and '] In the Gaussian location setup of Theorem~\ref{thm:nn-comparison}, take the ordinary nearest-neighbor decoder and the centered reference law.  If \(L_\pi(\Delta)\) is above a universal constant, then choosing
\[
\tau^2\asymp \frac{\mathsf V_\pi}{L_\pi(\Delta)}
\]
yields
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\sup_{s,u\in T}(X_s-X_u)
\gtrsim
\Delta^2\sqrt{\frac{L_\pi(\Delta)}{\mathsf V_\pi}}.
\end{equation}
In particular, if \(\mathsf V_\pi\le C_0\Delta^2\), then
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\sup_{s,u\in T}(X_s-X_u)
\gtrsim_{C_0}
\Delta\sqrt{L_\pi(\Delta)}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, with
\begin{equation}
N_{\rm spread}^{\rm loc}(T,d,\Delta;C_0)
:=
\sup_{\pi:\,\mathsf V_\pi\le C_0\Delta^2}
\frac{1}{\sup_{a\in T}\pi(B_d(a,\Delta))},
\end{equation}
one has
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\sup_{s,u\in T}(X_s-X_u)
\gtrsim_{C_0}
\Delta\sqrt{\log N_{\rm spread}^{\rm loc}(T,d,\Delta;C_0)},
\end{equation}
whenever the logarithm is above the universal threshold required by the information condition.

[Lemma lem:technical of arXiv:2508.03577, 'Phase Transitions in a Particle Model\\ for the Self-Adaptive Response to Cancer Dynamics'] Let $T$ be the collection time in the coupon collector's problem with $M$ coupons, where we draw according to an exponential random clock with parameter $q$. We then have that
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}\ek{{\rm e}^{-\alpha T}}=\frac{\Gamma\left(M+1\right)\Gamma\left(1+M\alpha/q\right)}{\Gamma\left(M+1+M\alpha/q\right)}\sim \frac{\Gamma(1+M\alpha/q)}{M^{M\alpha/q}}\, ,
    \end{equation}
    where asymptotics hold given that $\alpha/q$ does not vary with $M$.

