[Lemma l.sec3ber1 of arXiv:2606.11043, 'Thick points under Gaussian free field dynamics'] For $\alpha > \gamma$, there is $p:\mathbb R\to [0,1]$ such that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb E[\1_{ G_{\varepsilon, \alpha}(z)}e^{\gamma h_{\varepsilon}(x)- 
        \frac{\gamma^2}{2}\mathbb E[h_{\varepsilon}^2(x)]}]\geq 1-p(\varepsilon_0),
    \end{equation*}
    and $p$ is such that tends to  $0$ as $\varepsilon_0\to 0$. This implies that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb E\left[\1_{ G^{c}_{\varepsilon, \alpha}(z)}e^{\gamma h_{\varepsilon}(z)- 
        \frac{\gamma^2}{2}\mathbb E[h_{\varepsilon}^2(z)]}\right] \underset{\varepsilon_0\to0}{\longrightarrow}
        0.
    \end{equation*}

