[Lem 11 (\textit{cf.} {\cite[Exercise 2.8.17) of arXiv:2511.21496, 'Optimal local central limit theorems on Wiener chaos'] {NourdinPeccati}}] 
Let $m \in \N_0$ and $\{F_n\}_{n \in \N} \subset \bigoplus_{i=0}^{m}\cW_i$. 
If the collection of the laws of the sequence $\{F_n\}_{n \in \N}$ is tight, then for any $\alpha \in \R$ and $p \in [1, \infty)$, 
\begin{equation}

    \sup_{n\in \N} \norm{F_n}_{\bW^{\alpha, p}} < \infty. 
\end{equation}

