[Lemma lem:est-on-Yn of arXiv:2412.05142, 'Strong convergence of the Euler scheme for singular kinetic SDEs driven by $\alpha$-stable'] Let $p\geqslant 1$ and $\epsilon>0$. Suppose that Assumption (ass:main1 of the paper) holds. Let $M$ be as (equation def:noise of the paper) and let  $Z^n=(X^n,V^n)$ satisfy (equation eq:SDE-EM of the paper). Then for $ Y^n:=Z^n-M$ there exists a constant $N=N(d,\beta,\|b\|_{{\mathbb C}_{\boldsymbol{a}}^\beta},\alpha,\epsilon,p)$ so that for any $(s,t)\in[0,1]_\leqslant^2$
    \begin{align}

       &  [Y^n-\Gamma_{\cdot-k_n(\cdot)}Y^n_{k_n(\cdot)}]_{C_p^0|{\mathscr G},[s,t]}\leqslant Nn^{-1}; \\&
      [Y^n-\Gamma_{\cdot-k_n(\cdot)}Y^n_{k_n(\cdot)}]_{{\mathscr C}_p^{\frac{1}{2}}|{\mathscr G},[s,t]}\leqslant N n^{-\frac{1}{2}-(\frac{\beta}{\alpha}\wedge\frac{1}{2})+\epsilon} .
    \end{align}

