body:
[Lemma lem:increment-rademacher of arXiv:2604.05941, 'Banach spaces of continuous paths with finite $p$-th variation'] For $n\ge1$ and $k\in I_n$, set $\Delta_k^n x:=x(\frac{k+1}{2^n})-x(\frac{k+1}{2^n})$. Under Assumption~(assum: uniform mag of the paper), we define for any $p>1$
    \begin{equation}
        y_m:=2^{m(\frac1p-\frac12)}c_m
        \qquad\text{and}\qquad
        \rho:=2^{-(1-\frac1p)}\in(0,1).
    \end{equation}
    Then, we have the identity
    \begin{equation}
        2^{\frac{n}{p}}\Delta_k^n x = \sum_{j=1}^{n}\rho^{j}\,y_{n-j}\,\varepsilon_j(k),
    \end{equation}
    with the level sign notation $\varepsilon_j(k)$ of (equation eq:level-signs-epsj of the paper). Moreover, we have the relationship for every $m \ge 0$
    \begin{equation}
        \xi_m^{(p)} = 2^{-\frac{mp}{2}}\sum_{k\in I_m}|\theta_{m,k}|^p = 2^{m(1-\frac{p}{2})}c_m^p, \qquad\text{hence}\qquad y_m=\big(\xi_m^{(p)}\big)^{1/p}.
    \end{equation}

