[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2609.01826, 'An extension theory for fully fractional Schr\"odinger equations with memory'] For $0<s<1, a = 1-2s, t>0$, and $z>0$ we have:
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{\G(s)} \int_0^\infty \frac{\mathbf 1_{(0,\infty)}(t-\sigma)}{(t-\sigma)^{1-s}} P_a(z,\sigma) d\sigma = \frac{1}{\G(s)} \frac{e^{i \frac{z^2}{4t}}}{t^{1-s}}.
\end{equation}

