body:
[Lemma lem:contour of arXiv:2608.12954, 'Rainbow percolation'] Let $\omega\in\{0,1\}^V$, suppose $\0$ is open and its open cluster $C$ is
finite. Then there is a finite set $\Gamma\subseteq V$ with
$s:=\abs\Gamma\ge1$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] every vertex of $\Gamma$ is closed and $\mathsf H$-adjacent to
  $C$;
\item[(ii)] every infinite self-avoiding $\mathsf H$-path started at $\0$
  meets $\Gamma$;
\item[(iii)] $\Gamma$ is connected in $\mathsf H^\star$;
\item[(iv)] $(k^\ast,0)\in\Gamma$ for some $0\le k^\ast\le s-1$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

