body:
[Lemma 66 (Potential function $\alpha_{Cone\ A}$) of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] Given $Cone\ A \in CONE(H_0)$. A potential function $\alpha_{Cone\ A} \in C^0(H_0)$ is obtained by
\begin{equation*}
\alpha_{Cone\ A}(a):=\Vert v_{{\partial}Cone\ A}(a) \Vert \quad (a \in C_0(H_0)),
\end{equation*}
where $\Vert (x,y,z) \Vert :=x+y+z$. ${\alpha}_{Cone\ A}$ is called the \textit{potential function on $H_0$ defined by $Cone\ A$}.

