[Theorem thm:upper_tail of arXiv:2411.04988, '{\bf A relation between isoperimetry and total variation decay with applications to graphs'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a graph with degrees bounded by $M$. There exists a posiitve constant $c=c(M)$ such that
\[
\mathbf{P}_x( d_G(X_0,X_n) \geq \lambda D_n^*) \leq e^{-c\lambda} \; \text{ and } \; \mathbf{P}_x\left( -\log P^n(X_0,X_n) \geq \lambda (H_n^* + \log n) \right) \leq e^{-c\lambda}
\]
for every $x\in V$, $n\geq 2$, and $\lambda \geq 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

