[Lemma lemma4.8 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] For given $k,\ell\in\mathbb{N}$, integer tuples $\mathbf{s}\in\mathbb{R}_+^{2\ell}$ and some $t>0$, consider a measurable set $S\subset\mathbb{R}^{k+2\ell}$ satisfying
\begin{equation}2(\prod_{i=1}^{2\ell}s_i)t^{2\ell}(\frac{12}{\sqrt{2\ell}})^{2\ell}\left(\max_{y,\mathbf{a}}(\gamma_k(F_y(S;\mathbf{a})-F_y(S;\mathbf{a})))^\frac{1}{4}+e^{-k/8}\right)\leq\gamma_{k+2\ell}(S).
\end{equation}
    Then we can find some $x\in S$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        (\Gamma_{2\sqrt{k},16}\setminus\Gamma_{2\sqrt{k},\mathbf{s},t}+x)\cap S\neq\emptyset.
    \end{equation}

