[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2609.00516, 'Exceptional points on Atkin--Lehner quotients'] Assume $N$ is squarefree and $\CM(R) \ne \emptyset$.
The field of definition of any $P \in \overline{\CM}(R)$ has degree 
\begin{equation}

[\Q(P) : \Q] = \frac{h(R)}{ 2^{\omega (N/N(R)) - \varepsilon(N,R) }},  \qquad 
\varepsilon(N,R)=
\begin{cases}
1 & \operatorname{disc}(R)\in \bigcup_{\substack{m\mid N, \\ m>1}} \Delta(m),
  \\ 0 & \text{otherwise,}
\end{cases} 
\end{equation}
where $\Delta(m)$ is the set of discriminants of orders in $\Q(\sqrt{-m})$ whose CM points are fixed by $w_m$ (see also \eqref{eq:delta_m}).

[Proposition eq:FS-UB-top-exists of arXiv:2606.06612, 'The limit shape and emergence of the \\ Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $m \geq 0$. For every sequence of $L \to \infty$ such that each $L$ satisfies $\pi^0_{\Lambda}(\mathfrak{L}_0 \neq \emptyset) > \delta_L$, then sampling $\mathfrak{L}_n$ under the measures $\pi^0_{\Lambda}(\cdot \mid \mathfrak{L}_0 \neq \emptyset)$, every weak limit point $({\ensuremath{\mathbf Y}}_n(t))_{0 \leq n\leq m}$ of the processes $(Y_n(t))_{0 \leq n\leq m}$ satisfies 
     \begin{align}
         &({\ensuremath{\mathbf Y}}_n)_{0 \leq n\leq m} \preceq \bigotimes_{0 \leq n\leq m}\mathsf{FS}_{\sigma_n}\,,\\
         &({\ensuremath{\mathbf Y}}_n)_{0 \leq n\leq m} \succeq \bigotimes_{0 \leq n\leq m}\mathsf{FS}_{\sigma_n}\,.
     \end{align}
    If the sequence $L \to \infty$ is such that each $L$ satisfies $\pi^0_{\Lambda}(\mathfrak{L}_0 = \emptyset)> \delta$, then sampling $\mathfrak{L}_n$ under the measures $\pi^0_{\Lambda}(\cdot \mid \mathfrak{L}_0 = \emptyset)$ we have
    \begin{align}
         &({\ensuremath{\mathbf Y}}_n)_{1\leq n\leq m} \preceq \bigotimes_{1 \leq n\leq m}\mathsf{FS}_{\sigma_n}\,,\\
         &({\ensuremath{\mathbf Y}}_n)_{1 \leq n\leq m} \succeq \bigotimes_{1 \leq n\leq m}\mathsf{FS}_{\sigma_n}\,.
     \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

