body:
[Theorem p1q of arXiv:2509.24452, 'A family of non-uniform distributions on the set of parking functions generated by random '] Consider $\pi_1$ under the measure $\mathcal{P}_n^{(q)}$, with $q\in(0,1)$.
Then
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathcal{P}_n^{(q)}(\pi_1=k)=(1-q)q^{k-1},\ k\in\mathbb{N}.
\end{equation}
That is, $\pi_1$ converges in distribution to the geometric distribution with parameter $1-q$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2604.15753, 'The truncation property and continuity for \\ the long-range contact process on $\mathbb{Z'] Let $\lambda \in \Lambda$ and $\delta>0$. Then, for every finite $A \subset \bZ^d$ and every $N \geq 1$,
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{t \rightarrow \infty} \lim_{L \rightarrow \infty} \bP_{\lambda,\delta} \left(\left|  \leftidx{_L}A_t^A \right| \geq N\right) =  \bP_{\lambda,\delta} \left(\forall t>0, A_t^A \neq \emptyset \right)
\end{equation}

