[Definition def:Lambda-k of arXiv:2608.30831, 'Sharp discrete Hardy constants in dimensions three and four\\ and strict upper bounds from'] For $1\le k\le N$, set
\begin{equation}
 \Lambda_k(N):=\lambda_{\min}\!\left(M_N^{(k)}\right).
\end{equation}

[Definition 15 ($(1\times\ell)$-periodic weights) of arXiv:2508.04938, 'Perfect t-embeddings of doubly periodic Aztec diamonds'] Let $\{\alpha_i\}^\ell_{i=1}$, $\{\beta_i\}^\ell_{i=1}$ and $\{\gamma_i\}^\ell_{i=1}$ be three sets of positive real numbers satisfying~$\beta_i\neq \beta_j$,~$\alpha_i/\gamma_i\neq \alpha_j/\gamma_j$ if~$i\neq j$ and~$\beta_i<1<\alpha_i/\gamma_i$ for all~$i, j \in\{1,\ldots,\ell\}$. 
We define $(1\times\ell)$-periodic weights in the following way, for~$i=1,\dots,\ell$ set
\begin{equation*}
\alpha_{j,i}=\alpha_i, \quad \beta_{j,i}=\beta_i, \quad \gamma_{j,i}=\gamma_i \quad \text{and} \quad  \delta_{j,i} = 1.
\end{equation*}

[Theorem thm: disorder relevance of arXiv:2602.04429, 'Disordered systems and (subcritical) polynomial chaos\\ with heavy-tail disorder'] {}
Assume that $J_{\delta} v_{\delta} \sum_{x \in \Omega_{\delta}} \sigma_x$ converges in distribution under \(\mathrm{P}_{\delta}^{\mathrm{ref}}\) as~\(\delta\downarrow0\), to a strictly positive random variable. 
Then, if $\lim_{\delta\downarrow 0} \frac{\beta_{\delta}V_{\delta}}{J_{\delta}}  = +\infty$, the partition function~$Z_{\Omega_{\delta}}^{\omega,\beta_{\delta}}$ goes to $0$ in probability. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2608.29152, 'Uniform Statistical Convergence of Empirical Sinkhorn Potentials\\ with Exponential and Po'] For a model satisfying Definition~\ref{def:tight-graph-model}, there exist constants $\eps_0, \eta_0>0$ and $C_0<\infty$ (dependent only on the finite model) such that for $0<\eps\le\eps_0$ and any $\delta\in(0,1)$, if 
\begin{equation}
 t_{n,\delta} := \sqrt{\frac{\log(2(I+J)/\delta)}{2n}} \le\eta_0,
\end{equation}
then with probability at least $1-\delta$, we have $d_\infty([\widehat f_{\eps,n}],[f_\eps]) \le C_0\eps \sqrt{\log(2(I+J)/\delta)/n}$.
This fixed-cost model maintains the $n^{-1/2}$ rate and features a favorable linear scaling with $\eps$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma k_0_all_nice of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Under the same assumptions and the choice of $\beta_0$ as in Lemma (lemma: recursion of the paper), if $\mathcal{G}_{k_0}$ denotes the event that all $m_{k_0}$-boxes are nice, then $\beta_1 \ge \beta_0$ implies
    \begin{align}
        \lim_{m \to \infty} \hat{\mathbb P}_{m,\beta_1}(\mathcal{G}_{k_0}^c) = 0.
    \end{align}

