body:
[Cor 3 of arXiv:2609.03653, 'The derived set of multiple star polylogarithms'] The map
\[
\eta_{-1}:\widehat{\mathcal{T}}\longrightarrow\left[\frac12,1\right),
\qquad
{\bf k}\longmapsto
\lim_{r\rightarrow+\infty}
\sum_{n_1\geq\cdots\geq n_r\geq 1}
\frac{(-1)^{n_1-1}}{n_1^{k_1}\cdots n_r^{k_r}}
\]
is bijective. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Defn KMSW-inv of arXiv:2510.26123, 'Directed distances in bipolar-oriented triangulations:\\ exact exponents and scaling limit'] Let $n\geq 1$ and $\mathfrak m$ be a bipolar-oriented triangulation with $n$ total edges, with $l$ edges on its left boundary and $r$ edges on its right boundary. We define the corresponding KMSW walk $\mathfrak  Z = (\mathfrak  L(j),\mathfrak  R(j))_{0\leq j\leq n-1}$ as follows: for $0\leq j\leq n-1$, 
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathfrak  L(j)$ is the height in the tree $T_{UL}(\mathfrak  m)$ of the initial vertex of $\lambda_{j+1}$ (i.e.\ its distance in $T_{UL}(\mathfrak  m)$ from the source);
    \item $\mathfrak  R(j)$ is the height in the tree $T_{LR}(\mathfrak m)$ of the terminal vertex of $\lambda_{j+1}$ (i.e.\ its distance in $T_{LR}(\mathfrak m)$ from the sink) minus $r-1$.
\end{itemize}

[Lemma lemma_uniform_bound_infty_Omega of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $\xi \in \{-,+\}$. There almost surely exists $m_0$ such that almost surely, for any $m \geq m_0$ and any $k \geq 1$,
\begin{equation*}
    \sum_{(x_1,\dots,x_k) \in \Omega_{m,j(\xi)}} \delta_m^{\frac{15k}{8}}{\mathbb{E}}_{m,j(\xi)}^{\xi}[\sigma_{x_1} \dots \sigma_{x_k}] \leq C_{k,\infty}^{(\xi)}
\end{equation*}
with $\sum_k\frac{h^k}{k!}C_{k,\infty}^{(\xi)} < \infty$ almost surely.

