[Prop slice-sym-mon-is-universal of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $X^\otimes\in\CMon(\Spc_T)$. Then the Yoneda embedding $\smash{y\colon {\mathpalette\ulhelper{X}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}\to\ul\Spc_{T/X}}$ refines to a strong symmetric monoidal functor $\smash{{\mathpalette\ulhelper{X}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}^\otimes\to\ul\Spc_{T/X}^\otimes}$ for the slice symmetric monoidal structure, thus exhibiting $\smash{\ul\Spc_{T/X}^\otimes}$ as the symmetric monoidal $T$-cocompletion of $X^\otimes$.
    \begin{proof}
        Observe first that any lax symmetric monoidal refinement of $y$ is already strong: namely, we can check this after postcomposing with the conservative strong symmetric monoidal functor $\textup{fgt}\colon\ul\Spc_{T/X}^\otimes\to\ul\Spc_T^\times$, and as $\textup{fgt}\circ y\colon X\to\ul\Spc_T$ takes values in the full subcategory spanned by the terminal object, it admits a unique lax symmetric monoidal structure, which is automatically strong. 

        Since the tensor product on $\ul\Spc_{T/X}$ is $T$-bilinear (Lemma~(lm:tensor-bil of the paper)), any symmetric monoidal enhancement $y^{\otimes}$ of the Yoneda embedding extends uniquely to a symmetric monoidal, $T$-cocontinuous functor ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{\PSh}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_T(X)^{\otimes}\to \ul\Spc_{T/X}^{\otimes}$ from the free symmetric monoidal $T$-cocompletion of $X$. As explained in Remark~(rk:slice-vs-shift of the paper), the underlying functor $\ul\PSh_T(X)\to {{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\Spc}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_T}_{/X}$ is an equivalence, which then implies that $y^{\otimes}\colon {\mathpalette\ulhelper{X}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}\to \ul\Spc_{T/X}^{\otimes}$ is a free symmetric monoidal $T$-cocompletion. 

        We are therefore reduced to constructing a lax symmetric monoidal structure on the Yoneda embedding $y$, which by the definition of $\ul\Spc_{T/X}^{\otimes}$ as a pullback amounts to constructing a commutative square in ${\textup{Fun}}(T^{{\textup{op}}},\text{OP}_\infty)$
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                {\textup{Hom}}(-,X)^\otimes\arrow[r]\arrow[d] & \Ar(\ul\Spc_T)^\times\arrow[d,"\ev_1"]\\
                1^\otimes\arrow[r,"X"'] & \ul\Spc_T^\times
            \end{tikzcd}
        \]
        such that $\textup{id}_X\in{\textup{Hom}}(X,X)$ gets sent to its Yoneda image, viewed as an element in the fiber over $(\textup{pr}_2\colon X\times X\to X)\in\ul\Spc_T(X)$.
        By the universal property of cartesian symmetric monoidal structures [HA]*{Proposition 2.4.1.7}, this is equivalent to constructing a commutative square of $T$-$\infty$-categories
        \begin{equation}
            \begin{tikzcd}
                \textup{Un}^\text{cc}\circ {\textup{Hom}}(-,X)^\otimes\arrow[r]\arrow[d] & \Ar(\ul\Spc_T)\arrow[d,"\ev_1"]\\
                \textup{const}\,\text{Fin}_*\arrow[r,"X"'] & \ul\Spc_T
            \end{tikzcd}
        \end{equation}
        sending $\textup{id}_X$ in the fiber over $1\in\text{Fin}_*$ to the Yoneda image of $\textup{id}_X$ and such that $\textup{Un}^\text{cc}({\textup{Hom}}(Y,X)^\otimes)\to\Ar(\ul\Spc_T(Y))$ satisfies the Segal condition for every $Y\in\PSh(T)$. Note moreover that if the top arrow factors through $\ul\Spc_{T,*}\subset\Ar(\ul\Spc_T)$, then the Segal condition is automatic as the forgetful functor $\ul\Spc_{T,*}\to\ul\Spc_T$ is conservative and preserves fiberwise limits.

        Let us abbreviate ${\mathcal{B}}\coloneqq\PSh(T)$. By [HHLNb]*{Example~2.5.10}, the composite of the Yoneda embedding ${\mathcal{B}}^{\textup{op}}\to{\textup{Fun}}({\mathcal{B}},\Spc)$ with straightening for left fibrations is given by $X\mapsto{\mathcal{B}}_{/X}$, i.e.~as the \emph{cartesian} straightening of $\ev_1\colon\Ar({\mathcal{B}})\to{\mathcal{B}}$. Thus, a diagram of the form $((diag:lax-yoneda-before-un of the paper))$ is equivalent (via cartesian unstraightening) to
