body:
[Lem 13 of arXiv:2608.05185, '\large\bf ON THE HEAT FLOW CONJECTURE FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] The eigenvalues of \(\mathbf{X}_{N,c}\) have joint density
\begin{equation}
 \frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{N,c}}
 \left|\Delta(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_N)\right|^2
 \prod_{j=1}^{N}\dd\gamma_{N;1,c,0}(\lambda_j).
\end{equation}
Here \(\mathcal{Z}_{N,c}>0\) is the normalising constant.
Relative to \(\gamma_{N;1,c,0}\), they form a determinantal point process
with correlation kernel
\begin{equation}
 K_{N,c}(z,w)
 =\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}
 \frac{h_{k,c,N}(z)\overline{h_{k,c,N}(w)}}{\kappa_{k,N}},
 \qquad
 \kappa_{k,N}=\frac{k!}{N^k}.
\end{equation}
As an integral operator on
\(\mathrm{L}^2(\gamma_{N;1,c,0})\), \(K_{N,c}\) is the orthogonal
projection onto
\[
 \mathscr{H}_{N,c}
 =\operatorname{span}\{h_{0,c,N},\ldots,h_{N-1,c,N}\}.
\]

[Theorem thm:2nd moment upper bound of arXiv:2504.14457, 'Abstract'] Under the Assumptions (assumption:finite var of the paper) and (assumption:bounded of the paper) and with $H$ given by equation~(equation a1a2condition of the paper), let $u$ be the solution to the equation~(equation eqn:DO process of the paper). There is a positive constant $C<\infty$ such that for all $t\in \mathbb{R}_+$ and $x,y\in \mathbb{R}^d$,
\begin{align}
    E[u(t,x)u(t,y)]\leq C  u_0^2 \cdot \exp(C t^{\frac{4H-a}{2-a}}).
\end{align}

