body:
[Theorem 16 of arXiv:2609.02610, 'The frame set of the first Hermite function'] Let $\beta>0$ and define $\varphi_\beta\colon\R\to\R$ by
\begin{equation}
  \varphi_\beta(t)=\e^{-\pi t^2/\beta}
  \quad\text{for all }t\in\R.
\end{equation}
Let $u=(u_k)_{k\in\Z}\in\ell^\infty(\Z)$, and let
$f\colon\R\to\C$ be the nonzero function defined by
\begin{equation}
  f(t)=\sum_{k\in\Z}u_k\varphi_\beta(t-k)
  \quad\text{for all }t\in\R.
\end{equation}
Let $\cZ(f)$ be the set of real zeros of the entire extension of $f$, and
define $\nu_f(\lambda):=\ord_\lambda f$ for $\lambda\in\cZ(f)$.  Then
\begin{equation}
  D^-(\cZ(f),\nu_f)\leq1.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

