body:
[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2608.10183, '2608.10183'] Fix a postsynaptic neuron \(j\) and a time \(t\). Let
\begin{equation*}
\theta_j^\eta(t)
:=
Q_j^{\eta_t}(+1),
\qquad
\theta_j^{\widehat\eta}(t)
:=
Q_j^{\widehat\eta_t}(+1).
\end{equation*}
There exists a coupling
$\left(
\varepsilon_j^\eta,
\varepsilon_j^{\widehat\eta}
\right)
$ of the two sign laws
$Q_j^{\eta_t}
$ and $Q_j^{\widehat\eta_t}
$ 
such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P
\left(
\varepsilon_j^\eta
\neq
\varepsilon_j^{\widehat\eta}
\right)
=
\left|
\theta_j^\eta(t)
-
\theta_j^{\widehat\eta}(t)
\right|.

\end{equation}

Moreover, define the corresponding synaptic increments by
\begin{equation*}
\xi_{ij}^\eta
=
w_{ij}
\mathbf 1_{\{\varepsilon_j^\eta=+1\}}
-
v_{ij}
\mathbf 1_{\{\varepsilon_j^\eta=-1\}},
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
\xi_{ij}^{\widehat\eta}
=
w_{ij}
\mathbf 1_{\{\varepsilon_j^{\widehat\eta}=+1\}}
-
v_{ij}
\mathbf 1_{\{\varepsilon_j^{\widehat\eta}=-1\}}.
\end{equation*}
Then
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E
\left[
\left|
\xi_{ij}^\eta
-
\xi_{ij}^{\widehat\eta}
\right|
\right]
=
\left(
w_{ij}+v_{ij}
\right)
\left|
\theta_j^\eta(t)
-
\theta_j^{\widehat\eta}(t)
\right|.

\end{equation}

[Lemma EHI:l:LeaveBallConstantHelper of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] For all $\varepsilon \in (0, 1)$, there exists a universal constant $C_{(EHI:l:LeaveBallConstantHelper of the paper)}(\varepsilon)=C_{(EHI:l:LeaveBallConstantHelper of the paper)}(\varepsilon, d)>0$ such that if $X \in \mathcal{I}(d, r_0)$, then for all $r>0$ and $x \in \mathbb{R}^d$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{P}_x \left( |X_t-x| > r \right) \geq (1-\varepsilon) \mathbb{P} \left( [X]_t \geq C_{(EHI:l:LeaveBallConstantHelper of the paper)}(\varepsilon) (r \vee r_0)^2\right).
    \end{equation*}

