[Corollary boundedness of arXiv:2606.29352, 'Exponential Mixing for 2D Stochastic Damped Euler Equation Driven by Bounded Noise'] Let $\gamma>0$ and $2<p \leq \infty$, there exists $\epsilon^\star(\gamma,w_0)>0$ such that for any $0\leq \epsilon < \epsilon^\star $
 \begin{equation}
     \sup_{t\geq0}\|\nabla w_\epsilon(t)\Vert_{p} < \infty,\; \mathbb{P}-a.s.. \end{equation}

[Prop 23 of arXiv:2609.03653, 'The derived set of multiple star polylogarithms'] For every nonempty finite index ${\bf k}$, the function
\begin{equation}
P_{\bf k}(z)=\frac{zF_{\bf k}'(z)}{F_{\bf k}(z)}
\end{equation}
has a removable singularity at $0$, belongs to $\mathfrak{T}$ after that singularity is filled in, and is not constant.

