body:
[Thm RUB of arXiv:2605.13666, 'When Does the Dice Sum Become Prime?'] The expectation of $\tau_N$ is bounded from above as
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{E}[\tau_{N}] \leq \sum_{p \geq N}(p-N)\cdot \left( \dfrac{5}{6}\right)^{\pi(N,p-1)},
\end{equation}
where the sum runs over all prime numbers~$p\geq N$.

