[Lemma lem:mst-complete-envelopes of arXiv:2608.09465, 'Balancing fractional Brownian motion'] For $H\in(0,1)$, the following estimates hold uniformly for all $j\in\mathbb{Z}$, and $s, t\in [0, 1]$:  
\begin{align}
\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\rho_{j,k}&\lesssim N_j\\
\left\|\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}|G_{j, k}^H|\right\|_\infty&\lesssim_H A_j\\
\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\frac{|G^H_{j,k}(t)-G^H_{j,k}(s)|^2}{\rho_{j, k}}&\lesssim_H A_j^2\begin{cases}\min\{1, 2^{2j}|t-s|^2\}& j\geq 0\\|t-s|^2& j<0\end{cases}
\end{align}

