[Theorem thm:generalized:sink:polynomial of arXiv:2412.09235, 'A semiconcavity approach to stability of entropic plans and exponential convergence of Sin'] Assume $c(x,\cdot)$ to be $\mathcal{C}^1(\mathcal{Y})$, that there exist $\Lambda\in(0,+\infty)$, a non-negative function $\omega\colon\mathcal{Y}\times\mathcal{Y}\to\mathbb{R}$ and $N\geq 2$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
y\mapsto c(x,y)+\psi^{n}_\varepsilon(y)
\end{equation*}
is $(\Lambda,\omega)$-semiconcave uniformly in $x\in\supp(\rho)$ and $n\geq N-1$. 
If $\nu$ satisfies the generalized transport inequality (equation eq:generalized:TI:gamma of the paper) for some $\gamma\in(0,1)$  then for any $n\geq N$ we have
\begin{equation*}
\mathrm{KL}(\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\nu}|\pi^{n+1,n})\leq (n-N+1)^{-\frac{\gamma}{1-\gamma}} \biggl(\frac{1-\gamma}{\gamma M^{\frac1\gamma}}+\frac1{(n-N+1)\,\mathrm{KL}(\pi_\varepsilon^{\rho\nu}|\pi^{N,N-1})^\frac{1-\gamma}{\gamma}}\biggr)^{-\frac{\gamma}{1-\gamma}}\,,
\end{equation*}
where for notation's sake we have introduced the constant 
\begin{equation*}
M=M\biggl(\gamma,\frac{\tau\Lambda}{2\varepsilon}\biggr)\coloneqq 2^{1-\gamma}\max\biggl\{\mathrm{KL}(\nu|\nu^{N,N-1})^{1-\gamma},\,\frac{\tau\Lambda}{2\varepsilon}(1+\mathrm{KL}(\nu^{N,N-1}|\nu)^{1-\gamma})\biggr\}\,.
\end{equation*}

