[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2609.03855, 'A Fejér--Riesz inequality for Dirichlet series'] There is a constant $C_0 >0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
 \int_0^1 |f(1/2+\sigma)|\,d\sigma\le C_0\|f\|_{\mathscr H^1}, \qquad f \in \mathscr H^1.
\end{equation}
Therefore, there is a constant $C_0' > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \left|a_1+\sum_{n=2}^\infty \frac{a_n}{\sqrt n\log n}\right|
 \le C_0' \|f\|_{\mathscr H^1}, \qquad f \in \mathscr H^1.
\end{equation}
The sum in (equation eq:hardy of the paper) is convergent. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem deGlb of arXiv:2508.04954, 'Conditional exponential directed last passage percolation under a one-point upper large de'] For every $\mathsf{q} \in \mathsf{R}_1 \cup \cdots \cup \mathsf{R}_7$,  there exists a constant $c > 0$ such that 
\begin{equation} 
    \sum_{* \in \mathcal A_3} v_*\Delta \mathrm G_{*}  \geq \Delta \mathrm G_{123} + c|{\mathbf v}| 
\end{equation}  
for every 
${\mathbf v}= (v_{123}, v_{12}, v_{23}, v_1, v_2, v_3)\in {\mathbb N}_0^6 \setminus \{(1,0,0,0,0,0)\}$ satisfying
\begin{equation} 
