[Prp prpBoundExpMomentsLine of arXiv:2607.29423, 'Schwarzian Field Theory at High Temperatures'] There exists $C>1$ such that for any $\sigma>0$, any $s \neq t\in \mathbb{T}$,
and any $\lambda\in [-C^{-1}, C^{-1}]$, we have
\begin{equation}
\int \exp\left\{\frac{2\lambda}{\sigma^2} \left(\obs{\phi}{s}{t} -\frac{1}{|t- s|}\right)\right\}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} \mathscr{M}_{\sigma^2}(\phi)
<\left(1-C|\lambda|\right)^{-1/2}
\exp\left\{\frac{C \lambda^2}{4|t-s|\sigma^2}\right\}
\mathcal{Z}\Big((1-|t-s|)\sigma^2\Big).
\end{equation}

