[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2608.06646, 'Three-dimensional stochastic wave equation with non-Lipschitz coefficients'] Suppose the initial values $u_0$, $v_0$ and the spatial covariance function $f$ satisfy the assumptions of Theorem~ef{T:MainTheorem}. Let $u$ be the solution to~\eqref{E:SWE}. Then, there exist constants $c,C>0$ such that for all $p\ge 2$, $T>0$, $0\le t\le  t'\le T$, $t'-t<1$ and $x\in\R^3$,
