[Proposition prop.ulequp of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For each $(t,m) \in [0,1] \times \mathcal{P}_2({\mathbb R})$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{V}^\infty(t,m) \leq \mathcal{U}_2(t,m).
    \end{align*}
    In particular, $\mathcal{V}^\infty$ is locally bounded on $[0,1) \times \mathcal{P}_2({\mathbb R})$.

