[Proposition prop:det2+Pf of arXiv:2412.04579, 'Solvable Families of Random Block Tridiagonal Matrices'] Let ${\lambda}\in {\mathbb R}^{2n}$. Then we have
 \begin{align*}
 \sum_{|\mathcal{A}|=n,\, \mathcal{A}\subset[\![2n ]\!]} \Delta(\mathcal{A})^2 \Delta (\mathcal{A}')^2&=(-2)^n \Delta (\lambda) \operatorname{Pf}\left(\frac{{\bf{1}}_{i\neq j}}{\lambda_i-\lambda_j}\right).
 \end{align*}
The right side is defined as the appropriate limit if the $\lambda_i$'s are not all distinct.

