[Lemma lm:lclt_lemma of arXiv:2605.09377, 'A factorization formula for the partition function in the semi-discrete parabolic Anderson'] There is a constant $c > 0$, depending only on the dimension $d$, such that for any $r \in \mathbb{N}$,     
	\begin{equation}    
		\sum_{0 < i_1 < \ldots < i_r < n} i_1^{-\frac{d}{2}} (i_2 - i_1)^{-\frac{d}{2}} \ldots (i_r - i_{r-1})^{-\frac{d}{2}} (n - i_r)^{-\frac{d}{2}} \leq c^r  n^{-\frac{d}{2}}, \quad n \geq r + 1.   
	\end{equation}

