[Corollary 45 of arXiv:2511.05386, 'CLT for $\beta$-ensembles with Freud weights, application to the KLS conjecture in Schatte'] Let $p>2$. There exists $C>0$ such that, for any $\alpha \in [0,1]$, $\abs{1/r_\alpha} \leq C$, $\abs{(1/r_\alpha)'} \leq C$, and for any $\lambda \in \R^*$, 
    \[
	\abs{\left(\frac{1}{r_{\alpha}}\right)''(\lambda)} 
	\leq \begin{cases}
	    C \abs{\lambda}^{p-3} & \text{if } p < 3, \\
	    C (1+(\log1/\abs{\lambda})_+) & \text{if } p = 3, \\
	    C & \text{if } p>3.
	\end{cases}
	\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:reprod-kernels of arXiv:2510.18392, 'Hyperuniformity of random measures, transport and rigidity'] For a  reproducing kernel $ K$ on $ \mathbb{R}^{ d}\times \mathbb{R}^{ d}$ such that 
\begin{align*}
 I = \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^{ d}}K(x,x)dx<\infty ,
\end{align*}
then for $n\in \mathbb{N}, x_{ 1},\dots ,x_{ n-1}\in \mathbb{R}^{ d},$
\begin{align*}
 \displaystyle\int_{}\rho _{ K}^{ (n)} (x_{ 1},\dots, x_{ n})  dx_{ n}= (I-(n-1))\rho _{ K}^{ (n-1)}(x_{ 1},\dots ,x_{ n-1}).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

