[Corollary cor_high of arXiv:2507.06522, 'Balanced multi-species spin glasses'] Assume (equation converging_ratios of the paper), (equation delta_decay of the paper), (equation balanced of the paper).
With $\beta_p$ as in (equation beta_def of the paper), define
\eeq{ 
\xi^\mathsf{single}(x) \coloneqq \sum_{p=1}^\infty \beta_p^2x^p, \quad x\in[-1,1].
}
For either ${\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}\in\{\mathsf{Ising},\mathsf{spherical}\}$, the following implication holds:
\eeq{ 
\lim_{N\to\infty}F_{N,{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}^\mathsf{single}(\boldsymbol{\beta}) = \frac{\xi^\mathsf{single}(1)}{2} \quad \implies \quad
\lim_{N\to\infty} F_{N,{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}(\vc\Delta,\vc\lambda_N) = \frac{\xi^\mathsf{single}(1)}{2}. 
}

