[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Assume \ref{ass:cont}, \ref{ass:sigma}, and \ref{ass:k:positive}.  If $U(0)=w(x_0)$ with $x_0\in\C$, then
        \begin{equation}

            U(t)\in\mathcal K=\overline{w[\C]}, \qquad 0\le t<\life{U},
        \end{equation}
    almost surely.  Consequently $\tau_{\mathcal K}=\life{U}$ a.s. and $X(t)=f(U(t))$ for all $t<\life{X}=\life{U}$.

