[Prop edge-weight-locality of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $d=d^{{\mathrm {res}}}$. Suppose that $V,V_1,V_2\in\mathfrak{C}$ are such that $\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V} = (\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V_1}) \cup (\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V_2})$ and $(\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V_1}) \cap (\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V_2}) = \{a,b\}$. There exists a countable set $\mathcal{Z}_V=\{z_1,z_2,\ldots\} \subseteq \mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V}$ that contains $a,b$, is dense with respect to $d^{{\mathrm {path}}}_{\overline{V}}$, and such that the following holds for sufficiently large~$m$. Let $A = \{z_1,\ldots,z_m\}$, $A_1 = A \cap \overline{V_1}$, $A_2 = A \cap \overline{V_2}$, and let $w$ (resp.\ $w_1$, $w_2$) be the weight function associated with $\mathfrak{d}_V(\cdot,\cdot)|_{A}$ (resp.\ $\mathfrak{d}_{V_1}(\cdot,\cdot)|_{A_1}$, $\mathfrak{d}_{V_2}(\cdot,\cdot)|_{A_2}$). Then
\begin{itemize}
    \item $w(x,y)=w_1(x,y)$ for each $x,y\in A_1$;
    \item $w(x,y)=w_2(x,y)$ for each $x,y\in A_2$;
    \item $w(x,y)=0$ for each $x\in A_1 \setminus \{a,b\}$, $y\in A_2 \setminus \{a,b\}$;
    \item $w(a,b)=0$.
\end{itemize}

[Definition 4 (Caputo fractional derivative) of arXiv:2608.25164, 'A time-fractional Kalman filter'] Let $\alpha>0$ and let $n=\lceil\alpha\rceil$. The Caputo derivative is
defined by
\begin{align}
D_C^\alpha f(t)
&=I^{n-\alpha}f^{(n)}(t)\nonumber\\
&=\frac{1}{\Gamma(n-\alpha)}
  \int_0^t(t-s)^{n-\alpha-1}f^{(n)}(s)ds,
  \qquad n-1<\alpha<n,
\end{align}
while $D_C^n f=f^{(n)}$ when $\alpha=n$.

