[Lemma lem:approximation lemma a bit more general prelim of arXiv:2605.28770, 'Cutoff profiles for conjugacy invariant random walks on symmetric groups'] Let $G$ be a finite group. Let $H$ be a subset of $G$, $A\subset B \subset \widehat{G}$, and let $(u_{\alpha})_{\alpha\in \widehat{G}}$ be a family of complex numbers. Then
\begin{equation}
    \left| \frac{1}{|G|}\sum_{g\in H} \left| \sum_{\alpha \in B} d_\alpha u_\alpha \overline{\ensuremath{\textup{ch}}^\alpha(g)} \right| - \frac{1}{|G|}\sum_{g\in H} \left| \sum_{\alpha \in A} d_\alpha u_\alpha \overline{\ensuremath{\textup{ch}}^\alpha(g)} \right|\right| \leq \sum_{\alpha \in {B\backslash A}} d_\alpha |u_\alpha|.
\end{equation}

