[Lem 21 of arXiv:2608.05185, '\large\bf ON THE HEAT FLOW CONJECTURE FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] Let \(N\geq1\) and \(c\in\C\) with \(|c|<1\).  Every polynomial \(P\) of
degree at most \(N\) satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \left|P(z)\right|^2
 \leq
 \left\|P\right\|_{\mathrm{L}^2(\gamma_{N;1,c,0})}^2
 \frac{1}{\sqrt{1-\left|c\right|^2}}
 \exp\!\left(NQ_{1,c,0}(z)\right).
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:approx-C4 of arXiv:2509.23086, 'On Optimal Markovian Couplings of L\'evy Processes'] Let \( \mu, \nu \in \Lambda_2(\mathbb{R}^d) \), and suppose \( \varphi, \psi \in C^2_2(\mathbb{R}^d) \) satisfy the quadratic growth condition \( |\varphi(x)|, |\psi(x)| \le C |x|^2 \) for some \( C \ge 0 \), along with \( \varphi \oplus \psi \le c_2 \). Then there exists a family \( \{(\varphi_\varepsilon, \psi_\varepsilon)\}_{\varepsilon > 0} \) such that for all \( \varepsilon > 0 \), the following hold:
	\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
		\item \( \varphi_\varepsilon, \psi_\varepsilon \in C_b^2(\mathbb{R}^d) \), and \( \varphi_\varepsilon(x) = \varphi(x) \), \( \psi_\varepsilon(x) = \psi(x) \) for all \( |x| < \frac{\varepsilon}{4} \);
		\item \( \varphi_\varepsilon \oplus \psi_\varepsilon \le \delta_2^\varepsilon \);
		\item \( \varphi_\varepsilon \to 0 \) in \( L^1(\mu) \), and \( \psi_\varepsilon \to 0 \) in \( L^1(\nu) \) as \( \varepsilon \searrow 0 \).
