[Lemma lem:SubgaussianVectorization of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Suppose that $M$ is an $m \times m$ random symmetric matrix whose symmetric vectorization $\symvec(M)$ is $\sigma$-subgaussian. Then
        \begin{equation*}
            \P{\left\lVert\ifblank{M}{\:\cdot\:}{M}\right\rVert \geq 4\sigma\sqrt{m}} \leq \exp{-m}.
        \end{equation*}

