Lemma~(LemmaKeyFacts of the paper)\textup{(i)} gives
\[
 |([n+1]^n)_\sigma|=(n+1)^{\ell(\sigma)},
 \qquad
 |(\mathrm{PF}_n)_\sigma|=(n+1)^{\ell(\sigma)-1},
\]
and hence $K_{\mathrm{PF}}(x,y)=(n+1)K_{\mathrm{BE}}(x,y)$. For the stationary laws, the $S_n$-orbit of $x\in\mathrm{PF}_n$ is unchanged when $x$ is viewed in $[n+1]^n$, since ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:0a05808db492e65240ddac34b9d2e335660fb90544861d4387ee54152f1d37e1","revision_digest":"sha256:b788f518f7d181c1e4c4179049881d651b8b69b58dfcf2545c88e3ed56c47bb8","source_id":"arxiv:2605.16244","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

