[Lemma 115 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $S_m = \sum_{i=1}^m \weight(e_i)$ for distinct edges $e_1, \ldots, e_m$. If $\mu$ is the uniform distribution on $[0,1]$, then for any $ 0 < \delta_* \leq 1$, we have
\begin{equation} 
	\P \big( |S_m - m \xi | \geq \delta_* m \xi \big) \leq 2 \exp \left( - \frac{\delta_*^2 m}{9 \max\{ \beta, 1 \}}\right).
\end{equation}

