body:
[Theorem th:sharp-alpha-min of arXiv:2412.01489, 'One- and two-particle spectral gap identities for the symmetric inclusion process and rela'] For all graphs $G=(V,(c_{xy})_{x,y\in V})$ and site weights $\alpha=(\alpha_x)_{x\in V}$, we have
	\begin{equation}
	\alpha_{\rm min}\set{	\frac1{{54}} \, \frac{ \alpha_{\rm ratio}}{{{(6e)}}^{\alpha_{\rm min}/\alpha_{\rm ratio}} } \, \frac{ c_{\rm min}}{|V|^2\, {\rm diam}(G) }}	\le {\rm gap}_{\rm SIP}(G,\alpha)\; \text{,}\;\;
	\end{equation} where
\begin{equation}
	\alpha_{\rm ratio}\coloneqq  \frac{\alpha_{\rm min}}{\alpha_{\rm max}}= \frac{\min_{x\in V}\alpha_x}{\max_{y\in V}\alpha_y}\le 1\; \text{,}\;\;\qquad c_{\rm min}\coloneqq \min_{\substack{x,y\in V\\ c_{xy}> 0}}c_{xy}>0\; \text{.}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:lbm-square-interface of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] The map $L$ takes values in $\mathcal M_{\rm fin}(D)$, and each $b_i$ is a finite
positive Radon measure.  Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 M_x\perp\mathcal L^2,\qquad \operatorname{supp}M_x=D,\qquad b_i\ll\mathcal L^2,\qquad L(\phi_i^2)=2\Lambda_i\phi_i^2M_x-b_i,\quad 1\le i\le M.

\end{equation}

