[Theorem 4 (Aggregate rectangle exit) of arXiv:2608.24837, 'Strategic geometry of competing first-passage random walks'] For \(m>d\geq2\),

\[
\sum_{r=1}^{d-1}J_{m,d,r}
\leq
d^2\sum_{j=1}^{d-1}\frac1{(m+j)^2}.
\tag{5.16}
\]

In fact, with \(a=m-d\geq1\),

\[
\sum_{r=1}^{d-1}J_{m,d,r}
\leq
T_{a,d}
=\frac{d^2(d-1)}
       {(a+d+1)(a+2d-1)}.
\tag{5.17}
\]

