We let
\bas{
S=\inf\{\ell\in\N: I_{-\ell}= 1\text{ and }\exists \, r\in\{0,\dots,\ell-1\}\text{ with } I_{-r}=1\}
}
The random variable  $S-1$ is negative binomially distributed with parameters $2$ and $q$ so that (using that $\beta>1-q$) we get that
\bas{
 \E\bigl[ \beta ^{-(S-1)}\bigr]  = \Bigl(\frac {\beta q}{\beta-(1-q)}\Bigr)^2.
}
