body:
[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2604.14752, 'Strong and weak rates of convergence in the Smoluchowski--Kramers approximation for stocha'] For all $\alpha\in[0,1]$ and all $\delta\in[0,\frac{\alpha}{2}]$, there exists $C_{\alpha,\delta}\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for all $\epsilon\in(0,1)$ and all $t>0$ one has
\begin{equation}
\underset{n\in\N}\sup~\Bigl(\lambda_n^{2\delta-\alpha}\big|f_n^{\epsilon,1,0}(t)-e^{-t\lambda_n}\big|^2\Bigr)\le Ct^{-2\delta}\epsilon^{2\alpha}.
\end{equation}

Moreover, for all $\alpha\in[0,1]$ and all $\delta\in[\frac{\alpha}{2},\frac12]$, there exists $C_{\alpha,\delta}\in(0,\infty)$ such that, for all $\epsilon\in(0,1)$ and all $t>0$ one has
\begin{equation}
\sup~\Bigl(\lambda_n^{2\delta-\alpha}\big|\frac{f_n^{\epsilon,0,1}(t)}{\epsilon}-e^{-t\lambda_n}\big|^2\Bigr)\le Ct^{-2\delta}\epsilon^{2\alpha}.
\end{equation}

