body:
[Lemma W1.1-1L of arXiv:2411.09949, '$W_{\bf d}$-convergence rate of EM schemes for invariant measures of supercritical stable '] Under $(\mathbf{H}^\gamma)$ and (equation Dis of the paper), for any $m\in(0,\alpha)$,
there exist $\eta_0=\eta_0(\Theta)\in(0,1)$ and $C_1,C_2, C_3>0$ depending on $\Theta,m,\eta_0$
such that for any $\eta\in(0,\eta_0)$, there is a unique invariant probability measure $\mu_{\eta}$ such that for any $x\in{\mathbb R}^d$ and $k\in{\mathbb N}$,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}|Y_{k}^{x}|^{m}\leqslant (1-C_1\eta)^k\rho_{m}(x)+C_2,
\end{align}
and for any $f\in L_m^\infty({\mathbb R}^d)$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{\|f/\rho_{m}\|_{\infty}\leqslant 1}|\mathbb{E}f(Y_{k}^{x})-\mu_{\eta}(f)|\leqslant C_3 \rho_{m}(x)\mathrm{e}^{-\lambda k},
\end{align}
where $\lambda=-\log(1-C_1\eta)>0$.

