[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2609.00810, 'Uniqueness and Stability of Monge--Amp\`ere potentials in Big Cohomology Classes'] Let $u$ be a $\theta$-psh function and define the Kiselman-Legendre transform with level $c$ by
		\begin{equation}
			\Phi_{c,\delta}\coloneqq\inf _{0< t\leq \delta }\Big[\rho_tu(z)+K (t-\delta)
			-c\log\Big(\frac t{\delta}\Big)\Big].
		\end{equation}	
		Then, for  some positive constants $0<\delta_0<1$ and $K>1$  depending on the curvature tensor of $\omega_X$ on $X$,
		the function $\rho_tu(z)+Kt$ is increasing in $t\in (0, \delta_0]$ and
		one has the following estimate for the complex Hessian:
		\begin{equation}
			\theta+dd^c \Phi_{c,\delta}\geq -(Ac+2K\delta)\,\omega_X,
		\end{equation}
		where $A$ is a lower bound of the negative part of the bisectional curvature of $\omega_X$.

[Proposition of arXiv:2606.21556, 'Mean field limit of non-exchangeable interacting diffusions on co-evolutionary networks'] The following conditions are equivalent:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item[(i)] The map \([0,1]\to \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{C}^d_T)\), given by \(\xi \mapsto P^{\xi}\), is measurable
		when \(\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{C}^d_T)\) is endowed with the narrow topology.
		\item[(ii)] For every \(0\leq t_1\leq \ldots\leq t_n\leq T\) with \(n\in \mathbb{N}\), the map
		\[
			\begin{aligned}
				[0,1] &\longrightarrow \mathcal{P}((\mathbb{R}^d)^n) \\
				\xi &\longmapsto \pi_{t_1,\ldots,t_n \#}  P^{\xi},
			\end{aligned}
		\]
		is measurable.
	\end{enumerate}

[Lemma lem:boundary_part_of_loops of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] Fix $j \in \{1,\ldots,N\}$.  If 
	\begin{align*}
		\partial U_j \not \subseteq \overline{\bigcup_{\SCL \in \Gamma_A^{\mathrm{out}} \cup \Gamma_A^{\mathrm{in}} \cup \Gamma_A} \SCL},
	\end{align*}
	then we have that $U_j$ is surrounded by an outermost loop in $\overline{\Gamma}$.

[Prop LiValkoProp of arXiv:2602.08739, '\large \bf MOMENTS OF C$\beta$E FIELD PARTITION FUNCTION, $\mathsf{Sine}_{\beta}$ CORRELAT'] Let $\beta,\delta>0$.
Then, there exists a coupling of the $(\mathcal{CJ}_{N,\beta,\delta})_{N=1}^\infty$ and $\mathcal{HP_{\beta,\delta}}$ such that almost surely, as $N \to \infty$,
\begin{equation*}
\mathfrak{q}^{\beta,\delta}_N(\mathrm{e}^{\mathrm{i}z/N})\mathrm{e}^{-\mathrm{i}z/2}\longrightarrow\tilde{\boldsymbol{\xi}}^{\beta,\delta}(z),
\end{equation*}
uniformly on compacts in $z\in \mathbb{C}$ and the entire function's $\tilde{\boldsymbol{\xi}}_{\infty}^{\beta,\delta}$ zero set is exactly given by $\mathcal{HP}_{\beta,\delta}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

