[Cor corollary:identificacionL* of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Under $\mathbb{N}_{x,0}$ and $\mathbb{P}_{0,x,0}$, for every $u \in \mathcal{D}$, we have 
\begin{equation} 
    ( L^*_t(\rho^{u,*} ,  W^{u,*}) : t \geq 0 ) = ( L_{\Gamma_t}( \rho^u,W^u ) : t \geq 0). 
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:one-sided-spherical-code of arXiv:2607.29330, 'Large deviations for the maximum of\\ the generalized TAP free energy'] For every \(a\in(0,1)\),
		\begin{equation}
			\limsup_{N\to\infty}
			\frac1N\log A_N(a)
			\le-\frac12\log(1-a).
		\end{equation}
		In particular,
		\begin{equation}
			\lim_{a\downarrow0}
			\limsup_{N\to\infty}
			\frac1N\log A_N(a)=0.
		\end{equation}

[Theorem thm:hd_moments_main of arXiv:2508.18807, '{\bf Critical long-range percolation I: High effective dimension}'] Suppose that at least one of the three hypotheses of (equation HD of the paper) holds.

 There exists a positive constant $A$ such that
\begin{equation}

\mathbb E_{\beta_c,r} |K|^p \sim  (2p-3)!! A^{p-1} \frac{\alpha}{\beta_c} r^{(2p-1)\alpha}
\end{equation}
as $r\to\infty$ for each integer $p\geq 1$
and
\begin{equation}

\mathbb P_{\beta_c}(|K|\geq n) \sim \frac{\alpha}{\beta_c} \sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi A}} \cdot \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}
\end{equation}
as $n\to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:one-band-centered-capped-estimate-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] There exist constants \(C<\infty\), \(c>0\), and \(\eta>0\) such that, for every \(n\ge1\), every \(2^n\le\lvert\xi\rvert\le2^{n+1}\), and every \(d\in\mathfrak D_{\xi,n}^{\mathrm{osc}}\), 
\[\mathbb{P}\left(
\mathcal G_n^{\mathrm{pre}}
\cap
\left\{
\lvert F^{\mathrm{pre,cap}}_{\xi,d,n}\rvert
+
\sup_{L>m_{\xi,d}}
\lvert F^{\mathrm{post,cap}}_{\xi,d,n,L}\rvert
>
2^{-sn/2}2^{-2\varepsilon n}
\right\}
\right)
\le
C\exp(-c2^{\eta n}).\]

