[Definition 2 (Regular pre-grazing horizon) of arXiv:2608.16701, 'Order-Sensitive Fast-Synapse Limits in Sparse Excitatory--Inhibitory Threshold--Reset Netw'] A time $T>0$ is regular for the class solution when it is neither a firing
nor a release time of any class and there is $\gamma_T>0$ such that every
class firing time $s\in(0,T)$ is transversal:
\begin{equation}
 b_q(\theta_q,A_q(s-))+I(s)\ge\gamma_T.

\end{equation}
The first grazing time is the first threshold contact at which this lower
bound fails.

[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2608.06646, 'Three-dimensional stochastic wave equation with non-Lipschitz coefficients'] For $0<\beta<2$, let $f$ be the Riesz kernel.
    \begin{align}
        f(z)=|z|^{-\beta}\,.
    \end{align}







    Then, for any $0<\gamma_1,\mu_1<\min\{2-\beta,1\}$ and $0<\gamma_2,\mu_2<1-\beta/2$, $f$ satisfies Assumption~\ref{A:CovAssumption} with parameters
$\nu=2-\beta$, $\nu_1=2-\beta-\gamma_1$, $\nu_2=2-\beta-2\gamma_2$, and the corresponding choices of $\gamma_1$, $\gamma_2$, $\mu_1$, and $\mu_2$.

