\begin{align*}
S(n + 1, k) & = k S(n, k) + S(n, k - 1) \\
& \leq k \binom{k + 1}{2} S(n - 1, k) +  \binom{k}{2} S(n - 1, k - 1) && \text{(inductive hypothesis twice)} \\
& \leq \binom{k + 1}{2} \big(k S(n - 1, k) + S(n - 1, k - 1)\big) && \text{(triangular numbers are nondecreasing)}\\
& = \binom{k + 1}{2} S(n, k).
\end{align*}
So the claim holds by induction.

