[Theorem 9 (Liminf Inequality) of arXiv:2609.01237, ''] Let $\{ \alpha_k \} \subset (0,1)$ be a sequence of numbers such that $\alpha_k \searrow 0$ as $k \to \infty$.  For any function $u \in L^2(\Omega)$ and any sequence $\{ u_k \} \subset L^2(\Omega)$  that satisfies $u_k \to u$ strongly in $L^2(\Omega)$ as $k \to \infty$, we have
    \begin{align}
\liminf_{k \to \infty} \cF_{\alpha_k}[u_k] \geq \cF_0[u].
	\end{align}

