[Definition 54 ($\sim_T$) of arXiv:2608.29086, '2608.29086'] Given $P_1P_2P_3,\ Q_1Q_2Q_3 \in \pi^{-1}(abc)$. An equivelence relation $\sim_T$ on $ \pi^{-1}(abc)$ is defined by
\begin{equation*}
P_1P_2P_3 \sim_T Q_1Q_2Q_3 \text{ if and only if they have the same slope},
\end{equation*}
i.e., $\exists k \in \mathbf{Z}$ such that  
\begin{equation*}
\{Q_1, Q_2, Q_3\}=\{P_1+(k,\ k,\ k), P_2+(k,\ k,\ k), P_3+(k,\ k,\ k)\} \subset \mathbf{Z}^3.
\end{equation*}

