[Proposition prop:higher_regularity of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Suppose $f:[0,T]\times \mathbb T^3 \times \mathbb R^3 \to [0,1]$ is a weak solution to (equation e.LFD of the paper) with nonvacuum initial data in the sense of (d.nonvacuum of the paper) and an element of $L^\infty_m$ for some $m > 5$. Then, $f$ is a classical solution to (equation e.LFD of the paper). Moreover, for any fixed $k \in \mathbb N$, there is $m_0$ such that, if $m \geq m_k$, then
        \begin{equation*}
            D^k_{t,x,v} f \in L^\infty.
        \end{equation*}
        The constant $m_k$ depends on $k$, $T$, $\|f_{\rm in}\|_{L^\infty_{m_0}}$, and the nonvacuum parameters $r$, $\delta$, and $v_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary corollary_bound_on_last_point_if_close_to_mu_c_appendix of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] If $\mu_0 \in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{Z})$ and $R > R_{\mu_0}(\varepsilon)$ then for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $w \in \Omega_{n}^{(0)}(\mu_0,2^{-R}\varepsilon)$,
\begin{equation*}
|w_n| \leq R+2 \varepsilon n.
\end{equation*}

