body:
[Theorem thm:feebee of arXiv:2609.02304, 'Bayes-Optimal BER and AUC: \\Estimation and Evaluation of Estimators'] For $t \in [0, \frac{1}{2}]$, define
  $
    F_{\nu}(t) \coloneqq
    \frac{
      \lambda_{\nu} \paren{
        2 \theta (1 - \theta) t + \theta^{2}
      }
      - \lambda_{\nu}(\theta)^{2}
    }{
      2 \lambda_{\nu}(\theta) (1 - \lambda_{\nu}(\theta))
    }
  $.
  For any noise level $\nu \in [0, 1)$, 
  the optimal BER and AUC for
  the noise-injected distribution are given by
  $
    \mathrm{BER}^*_\nu = F_{\nu}(\mathrm{BER}^*)
  $
  and
  $
    \mathrm{AUC}^*_\nu = 1 - F_{\nu}(1 - \mathrm{AUC}^*)
  $,
  respectively. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

