body:
[Teo T: Extinction of arXiv:2606.10165, 'The frog model with death and drift on free products of complete graphs'] Let $m \geq 2$ and $d \geq 2$ be fixed integers. 
We define the function
\begin{equation}

\psi(\alpha,p) = \frac{p}{2} \left(2-\alpha +\sqrt{(2-\alpha)^2-\frac{4 (1-\alpha)((m-2)(2-\alpha)+\alpha d(m-1))}{(d(m-1)+m-2)^2}}\right).
\end{equation}

Then, \(\FM{\mathbb{D}_{m,d}}{\alpha,p}\) dies out almost surely for $(\alpha, p)$ such that $\psi(\alpha,p) < 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thm 8 (Aru-Lupu-Sep\'ulveda \cite{ALS1}) of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let $a<v$. Fix $z\in D$.
Then the r.v. 
\begin{displaymath}
\dfrac{1}{2\pi}\log\Big(\dfrac{\CR(z,D)}{\CR(z,D\setminus A_{a})}\Big)
\end{displaymath}
has the same distribution as $T_a$ under $W_0 = v$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma Lsdeter of arXiv:2606.15203, 'The existence of invariant sublinear expectations for $G\text{-}$SDEs'] Let $(P_{s,t}\varphi)(x)=E_P[\varphi( X_s^{t,x,\theta})]$. Then there exists a deterministic function  $\bar{\theta}_r$ and a diffusion process on $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, P)$,
    \begin{equation}
  \bar{X}_s^{t,x,\bar{\theta}}=x+\int^s_t b(\bar{X}_r^{t,x,\bar{\theta}})dr+\int^s_t\bar{\theta}_rdW_r,  
\end{equation}
such that for any $\varphi \in  B_b(\mathbb{R}^d)$, $P_{s,t}\varphi$ has the following representation, $(P_{s,t}\varphi)(x)=E_P[\varphi(\bar{X}_s^{t,x,\bar{\theta}})]$.

