body:
[Theorem thm-well-posedness of arXiv:2603.01823, 'on a fractional stochastic heat equation arising from the disordered pinning model'] Concerning the mild Skorohod solution to the SHE (equation e:she of the paper) in the sense of Definition~(def: solution of the paper), we have the following results:
\begin{enumerate}
\item When $\rho\in(0,2)$,  there exists no $L^p$-solution for any $p\ge2$; if  the solution to (equation e:she of the paper) is unique, then there exists no $L^p$-solution for any $p>1$.
\item When $\rho=2$, there exists a unique local $L^p$-solution but no global $L^p$-solution, for any $p>1$.
\item When $\rho\in(\frac{1}{2H-1},2]$, there exists a unique global $L^1$-solution.
\end{enumerate}

[Definition Number operator/Ornstein-Uhlenbeck operator of arXiv:2411.07680, 'Energy solutions of singular SPDEs on Hilbert spaces with applications to domains with bou'] The {{\em number operator\/}}, also called {{\em Ornstein-Uhlenbeck
  operator\/}}, is defined as
  \begin{equation}
    \mathcal{N} := \delta D, \qquad \ensuremath{\operatorname{dom}} (\mathcal{N}) := \{ F
    \in \ensuremath{\operatorname{dom}} (D) : D F \in \ensuremath{\operatorname{dom}} (\delta) \} .
  \end{equation}

[Theorem t:orgsnew of arXiv:2604.03979, 'Stationary Distributions in Monotone Markov Models: Theory and Applications'] Let $(P_t)$ be increasing. If
    $(P_t)$ is weakly order mixing, then $(P_t)$ is globally stable if and only
    if $(P_t)$ has at least one tight trajectory. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition proposition_estimates_psi_second_derivatives of arXiv:2609.00973, 'The Vlasov-Maxwell point charge system : study of the spherically symmetric case'] Let $t\geq T_0$ and $\mathcal{M}$ be defined as in (equation equation_definition_mathcal_M of the paper). The second order derivatives of $\widetilde{\Psi}$ satisfy
    \begin{equation}
        t^{\frac{3}{2}}\|\partial_\theta\partial_a\widetilde{\Psi}\|_\infty+ t^2\|(1+a^{-2})\partial_\theta^2 \widetilde{\Psi}\|_\infty\lesssim \mathcal{M},
    \end{equation}
    \begin{equation}
        t\left\|\frac{a^2}{1+a^2}\partial_a^2\widetilde{\Psi}\right\|_\infty\lesssim \|(a^{-6}+a^6)\gamma\|_{L^1}+\|(a^{-3}+a^3)\gamma_a\|_{L^1}+t^{-\frac{1}{2}}\mathcal{M}.
    \end{equation}

[Theorem of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] For any $1\leq i\leq N$, set 
\begin{align*}
\hat{Y}^i:=Y^i-\bar{Y}^i, \ \hat{K}:=K^{(N)}-K,\ \hat{Z}^i:=Z^i-\bar{Z}^i.
\end{align*}
Then, there exists a constant $C$ independent of $N$, such that
\begin{align*}
\mathsf{E}\left[\sup_{t\in[0,T]}|\hat{Y}^i_t|^2\right]\leq CN^{-1/2}, \ \mathsf{E}\left[\sup_{t\in[0,T]}|\hat{K}_t|^2\right]\leq CN^{-1/2}, \ \mathsf{E}\left[\int_0^T|\hat{Z}^i_t|^2dt\right]\leq CN^{-1/2}.
\end{align*}

