[Lemma I alpha elementary estimates of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Fix $\alpha\in(0,1/2]$. For every $A>0$, there exists $C_A>0$
	such that, for every $t\geq1$,
	\begin{equation}
		I_\alpha(t)
		+
		A(1+\log(1+t))^{-2\alpha}
		\leq
		\int_0^{2\log(1+\sqrt{t})+C_A}
		(1+s)^{-2\alpha}\,\text{d} s .
	\end{equation}
	Moreover, for every $A>0$, there exist constants $C_A>0$ and
	$t_A\geq1$ such that, for every $t\geq t_A$,
	\begin{equation}
		I_\alpha(t)
		-
		A(1+\log(1+t))^{-2\alpha}
		\geq
		\int_0^{2\log(1+\sqrt{t})-C_A}
		(1+s)^{-2\alpha}\,\text{d} s .
	\end{equation}
	Finally, there exists $C>0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\int_0^L t\,I_\alpha'(t)\,\text{d} t
		\leq
		C\,L\,(1+\log(1+L))^{-2\alpha},
		\qquad L\geq1.
	\end{equation}

[Corollary 3 (Exact separation at fixed levels and windows) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Assume \cref{ass:global-noise,ass:edge,ass:real-SLL} and weighted compatibility on a neighborhood of a fixed $z_0>b$.  Set $\vartheta_0=d(z_0)^{-1/2}$.  If, for some fixed $\gamma>0$,
\[
   \min_{1\le i\le r_n}|\theta_{n,i}-\vartheta_0|\ge\gamma
\]
with probability tending to one, then
\begin{equation}
  \#\{j:\sigma_j(W_n)>z_0\}
  =\#\{i:\theta_{n,i}>\vartheta_0\}
\end{equation}
with probability tending to one.  No rank restriction and no upper bound on the spike strengths are needed.  Subtracting the identity at the endpoints gives exact counts on any fixed finite union of superedge intervals whose inverse endpoints stay a fixed distance from the spike strengths. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 80 (Equivalent exterior and Fredholm spectral gauges) of arXiv:2606.29292, 'Intrinsic Gaussian Tensor Geometry and Random Operator Spectra'] Let $B\in\Sch_2(E)$ be skew-adjoint, let
$a_1\ge a_2\ge\cdots$ be its positive skew singular values, and let
$0<\rho<2$.  Define
\begin{align}

 \mathfrak F_\rho(B)
 &:=\sup_{N\ge1}(N!)^{1/(\rho N)}
   \left(
    \frac{2^N}{N!}\|\alpha_B^{\wedge N}\|
   \right)^{1/N},\\
 M_\rho(B)
 &:=\sup_{x>0}x^{-\rho/2}\log\mathscr D_B(x),
 \qquad
 \mathscr D_B(x):=\prod_{j\ge1}(1+xa_j^2).
\end{align}
Then
\begin{equation}

 c_\rho\|B\|_{\Sch_{\rho,\infty}}
 \le \mathfrak F_\rho(B)
 \le C_\rho\|B\|_{\Sch_{\rho,\infty}},
\end{equation}
and, with $W_\rho:=\sup_jj^{1/\rho}a_j$,
\begin{equation}

 M_\rho(B)\le C_\rho W_\rho^\rho,
 \qquad
 W_\rho\le(\log2)^{-1/\rho}M_\rho(B)^{1/\rho}.
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}

 B\in\Sch_{\rho,\infty}
 \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
 \mathfrak F_\rho(B)<\infty
 \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
 M_\rho(B)<\infty.
\end{equation}
Thus the weak-Schatten scale is equivalently encoded by factorial exterior
powers or by the positive-axis growth of the Fredholm product. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2608.13235, 'Mixing Properties of Random Laguerre Tessellations'] Let $l \in \n$ be large enough so that $c_l\coloneqq \sqrt{3k(l)^2+2k(l)-7}-1 > 0$ and choose $K_1(l)\geq 2k(l)+3$. Then for any $r \geq 1$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \varphi \in \hatMsetl \cap E^1_{r,K_1(l)} \implies  \varphi(rc_lB^d \times (-\infty,r^2]) = 0.
    \end{equation*}

[Lemma eq:mixture-tail-cost of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:mixture-tail}
For the law in (prop:moment-law of the paper), every \(a>0\) and \(\eta>0\) satisfy
