[Prop mle1 of arXiv:2505.16585, 'Expanded regimes of area law for lattice Yang--Mills theories'] Let $s \in \mc{S}_\Lambda$ be non-null with at least one good edge $\mbf{e}$, and let $K : \mc{P}_\Lambda^+ \ra \N$ be a plaquette count. We have that
\begin{equs}
\phi(s, K) = \mp \sum_{s' \in \mbb{S}_{\pm}(s, \mbf{e})} \phi(s', K) \mp \frac{1}{N^2} \sum_{s' \in \mbb{M}_{\pm}(s, \mbf{e})} \phi(s', K) \mp \frac{\beta}{N} \sum_{(s', K') \in \mbb{D}_{\pm}(s, \mbf{e}, K)} \phi(s', K').
\end{equs}

[Theorem thm:asymptotical_optimality of arXiv:2607.13748, 'Load Balancing with Individually Heterogeneous Servers'] Suppose that the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:stationary_bounds of the paper) hold. Then, for any tie-breaking policy $\pi$ where the stationary  $(X_1^{\pi,n}(\infty), \boldsymbol{\xi}^{\pi,n}(\infty))$ exists for all $n\in \mathbb{N}$, and for all $y>0$, we have 
    \begin{align}
        \lim_{n\to \infty} \mathbb{P}(X_{+1}^{\mathrm{JFSQ}, n}(\infty)>y\mid \varsigma^n+\nu^n>\varepsilon)&\leq \liminf_{n\to \infty} \mathbb{P}(X_{+1}^{\pi, n}(\infty)>y\mid \varsigma^n+\nu^n>\varepsilon),\\

        \lim_{n\to \infty} \mathbb{P}(X_{+2}^{\mathrm{JFSQ}, n}(\infty)>y\mid \varsigma^n+\nu^n>\varepsilon)&\leq \liminf_{n\to \infty} \mathbb{P}(X_{+2}^{\pi, n}(\infty)>y\mid \varsigma^n+\nu^n>\varepsilon).
    \end{align}
      conditional on the event $\{\varsigma^n+\nu^n>\varepsilon\}$ where $\varepsilon>0$ is such that $\mathbb{P}(\varsigma + \nu=\varepsilon) = 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

