[Definition 4 of arXiv:2605.15781, 'Mean-Field Backward Stochastic Differential Equations with Nonlinear Resistance and Double'] Let $s\in C[0,T]$, $a\in \mathbb{R}$ and $l,r:[0,T]\times \mathbb{R}\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$ be two functions such that $l\leq r$ and $l(T,a)\leq 0\leq r(T,a)$. A pair of functions $(x,K)\in C[0,T]\times BV[0,T]$ is called a solution of the backward Skorokhod problem for $s$ with nonlinear constraints $l,r$ ($(x,K)=\mathbb{BSP}_l^r(s,a)$ for short) if 
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] $x_t=a+s_T-s_t+K_T-K_t$;
\item[(ii)] $l(t,x_t)\leq 0\leq r(t,x_t)$, $t\in[0,T]$;
\item[(iii)]  $K$ has the decomposition $K=K^r-K^l$, where $K^r,K^l\in I[0,T]$ satisfy 
\begin{align}
\int_0^T I_{\{l(s,x_s)<0\}}dK^l_s=0, \  \int_0^T I_{\{r(s,x_s)>0\}}dK^r_s=0.
\end{align}
\end{itemize}

[Prop avargecoh of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] Let $\nu$ be a Borel probability measure on $\mathcal F$. Then
\begin{equation}
M_n(\lambda)=\int_{\mathcal F} M^\Phi_n(\lambda)\nu(d\Phi)
\end{equation}
defines a coherent system on $\mathbb{G}^p$.

