[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2506.20789, 'Central limit theory for Peaks-over-Threshold partial sums of long memory linear time seri'] Under the assumptions of Lemma~\ref{lem:2.2}, it holds that
\begin{align*}
      \mathbf{E}\left|
\sum_{t=1}^{n}
  \mathcal{U}_n(X_t)
      \right|^r
      \ \lesssim \
      \sum_{k=-\infty}^{n}
      \left(
      \sum_{t=k\lor 1}^{n}
      \norm{
      P_{k-t}\, \mathcal{U}_n(X_0)
      }_{L^r(\PP)}
      \right)^r
      \,.
  \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Thm lims of arXiv:2411.05235, 'A comparative study of three mathematical approaches applied to the reversal of AMR'] If $\mathcal{K}_{0}^{f} > 1$ and $\dfrac{\beta N-\gamma-\mu}{\beta N}-\dfrac{\beta}{\gamma+\mu}<\epsilon<1$, then there exists $\xi_{f} \in (0,\mathcal{K}_{0}^{f})$ such that for any $R_0 \in (0,\mathcal{K}_{0}^{f})$,
\begin{equation}
   \displaystyle\lim_{t \to \infty} R(t; R_0,\alpha) = \xi_{f},
\end{equation}
where $\xi_{f}$ is the equilibrium point defined in (equation eq-det of the paper).

