body:
[Lemma lem:alternating of arXiv:2607.27810, 'Perturbed Beta Corners Process'] Let $n\ge2$, let $t_1>\cdots>t_n$ or $t_1<\cdots<t_n$, and let
$u\in\mathbb R^n$. Then
\begin{equation}

	\sum_{1\le i<j\le n}(-1)^{i+j}\,\frac{(u_i-u_j)^2}{(t_i-t_j)^2}
	\;\le\;0,
\end{equation}
with equality if and only if $u_1=\cdots=u_n$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

