[Proposition log-coefficients of arXiv:2608.30212, 'A Painlev\'e equation for the H\"ormander-Bernhardsson constant'] Let $n=2k$ and let $\varphi_j, \psi_j\in (0,\pi)$ satisfy (equation Phi-interlace of the paper). Define $b_\ell$, $\ell\ge 1$ by
\begin{align}
\log D_n(z) =- \sum_{\ell=1}^\infty b_\ell z^\ell,
\end{align}
and let $H_n = {\rm sgn}(i D_n(e^{i\theta}))$. Then $H_n$ is a $\pm 1$ function on $(0,\pi)$ changing sign exactly at $\varphi_j$ and $\psi_j$ with $H_n(0+)=(-1)^{k+1}$ and
\begin{align}
b_\ell = \int_0^\pi \sin(\ell \theta) H_n(\theta) d\theta \qquad (\ell = 1,\hdots, n)
\end{align}

[Corollary itm:z1 of arXiv:2603.05467, 'Thresholds for colouring the random Borsuk graph'] Fix $\varepsilon,\delta > 0$. There exists a $L=L(\varepsilon,\delta) \in \ensuremath{ \mathbb N}$ such that, for every $\mu,\alpha>0$ and $k \in \ensuremath{ \mathbb N}$ 
and all sufficiently small $\beta>0$, one of
the following holds:

\begin{enumerate}
 \item $\ensuremath{{\mathbb P}}_{\mu}(A) < \varepsilon$, or;


 \item There exist indices $i_1,\dots,i_L$ such that
 $\ensuremath{{\mathbb P}}_{(1+\delta)\mu}( A | Z_{i_1}=\dots=Z_{i_L}=1) > 1-\varepsilon$.






\end{enumerate}

