[Lemma LS2 of arXiv:2510.22701, 'Gaussian fluctuations in Mean Field Stable matchings'] For $d>2$, we have that 
    \begin{align}
        \underset{n\rightarrow \infty}{\mathrm{lim}} \frac{1}{n}\sum^{n}_{k=\kappa_n+2} \bbclr{\frac{k}{n}}^{-4} I_0\bbclr{\frac{k}{n}}^2 =  \underset{n\rightarrow \infty}{\mathrm{lim}} \frac{1}{n}\sum^{n-1}_{k=\kappa_n} \bbclr{\frac{k}{n}}^{-4} I_{(\kappa_n-1)/n}\bbclr{\frac{k}{n}}^2 = d^2\gamma(d).
    \end{align}

