[Lemma 29 (Sphere quadratic forms) of arXiv:2608.19594, 'Mesoscopic Rectangular Spikes under Subspace Local Laws:\\Outlier Values and Singular Subs'] Let $w$ be uniform on the unit sphere of $\F^N$, and let $D$ be deterministic Hermitian with $\norm D_{\op}\le M$.  Then
\begin{equation}
 \Pp\left(\left|w^*Dw-\frac1N\tr D\right|>t\right)
 \le 2\exp\left(-cN\min\left(\frac{t^2}{M^2},\frac tM\right)\right)
\end{equation}
for all $t>0$.  In particular the Gaussian form $2\exp(-cNt^2/M^2)$ holds for $0<t\le M$, and on any range $t\le CM$ the two exponents agree up to the constant $c$.

