[Definition 2 of arXiv:2512.07156, 'Lorenz ordering of parasite loads across hosts in Isham's model of Host-Macroparasite Inte'] The {\em Lorenz curve} $L: [0,1] \to [0,1] $ for the distribution $F$ on $[0,\infty)$ with finite mean $ \mu$ is given by
    \begin{equation}
        L(u) = \frac{\int_{0}^{u} F^{-1}(y)\, dy}{\mu}, 
    \end{equation}
    where $ F^{-1}$ is the quantile function
    \begin{equation}
        F^{-1}(y) = \sup \{ x : F(x) \leq y \} \quad \text{for } y \in (0,1).
    \end{equation}

