[Definition 32 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Block-Interaction Matrix}

    Let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $\R^n$ with density $\nu(x) \propto \exp(-V(x))$. Let $x, y \in \R^n$ and $z^{(k)}(x,y) := (x_{I_1},..., y_{I_k},..., x_{I_m})\T$. Define the matrix A via its entries for $k, \ell \in [m]$ and $i \in I_k, j \in I_\ell$
    \begin{align*}
        A_{ij}^\rho(x,y)
        = \frac{1}{\sqrt{\rho_k-\rho} \cdot \sqrt{\rho_\ell-\rho}} \cdot 
        \begin{cases}
            \nabla_x^2 V(z^{(k)})_{ij} & \text{if $k \neq \ell$}, \\
            0 & \text{if $k = \ell$}.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align*}

