[Lemma L:K1-2 of arXiv:2606.23865, 'Uniform-in-time Gaussian fluctuations for multiscale nonlinear stochastic systems via Mall'] Let the terms $\mathsf{K}_1(t, r_1 \vee r_2; \varepsilon, \eta)$ and $\mathsf{K}_2(t, r_1 \vee r_2; \varepsilon, \eta)$ be defined in equation (equation E:Second-der-X-W2W2 of the paper). Then, for any $p \in \mathbb{N}$ and $t \ge r_1 \vee r_2,$ there exists a time-independent positive constant $K$ such that
\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
\mathsf{K}_1(t, r_1 \vee r_2; \varepsilon, \eta) & \le K \left[\eta^{2p} + {\varepsilon^{2p}}\right]  e^{-(2p) \alpha (t- r_1 \wedge r_2)}, \\
\mathsf{K}_2(t, r_1 \vee r_2; \varepsilon, \eta) & \le K \left[ \eta^{2p} + {\eta}^p \varepsilon^p \right] e^{- (2p)\alpha (t-r_1)} e^{- (2p)\frac{\lambda}{\eta} (r_1 - r_2)}\mathds{1}_{(r_1 \ge r_2)} + K \left[ \eta^{2p} + {\eta}^p \varepsilon^p \right] e^{-(2p) \alpha (t- r_1)}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}

