[Lemma t_star_good_approx_eq of arXiv:2606.17425, 'Order statistics for edge eigenvectors of Wigner matrices'] For any $\bar{x} \in \mathbb{R}^n$ we have, \begin{equation}
	\abs{t^*_{\tau, k}(\bar{x}) - x_{(k)}} \leq \tau \log (2 n). 

	\end{equation}	Secondly, for a fixed integer $l$, there exists a constant $C_l$ not depending on $n$ or $k$ such that \begin{equation}
	\sum_{j_1, \dots, j_l} \abs{\frac{\partial^l}{\partial x_{j_1} \cdots \partial x_{j_l}} t^*_{\tau, k}(\bar{x})} \leq \frac{C_l}{\tau^{l-1}},

	\end{equation} where the indices $j_1, \ldots, j_l$ are iterated from $1$ to $n$.

