[Lemma 44 (Initial estimate) of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm:opt_ll}, let $E_*$ be a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. Uniformly for $|E-E_*|\leq\eps_*$ and $\eps_*\leq\eta\leq1$,
        \begin{align}
                \norm{\calP[G(E+\ii\eta)-\Pi(E+\ii\eta)]} = O_\prec\left(\frac1{N\eta}\right). 
        \end{align}
        On the same domain,
        \begin{align}
                G(z)-\Pi(z)=O_\prec\left(\sqrt{\frac{\Im m(z)}{N\eta}}+\frac1{N\eta}\right),\qquad \avg{B(G(z)-\Pi(z))}_L = O_\prec\left(\frac1{N\eta}\right) 
        \end{align}
        uniformly for deterministic $B$ with $\|B\| = O(1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

