[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2606.06231, 'Sensitivity of SDE Solutions to Perturbations of the Diffusion and Drift'] Under Assumption \ref{assump:main_assumptions_1},  for all $g\in L^1(P_{{X}|_{[0,T]}})$ we have
\begin{align}
&\pm\left(E_{{\tilde{X}|_{[0,T]}}}[g]-E_{{{X}|_{[0,T]}}}[g]\right)\\
\leq &\inf_{c>0}\left\{\frac{1}{c}\log E_{{{X}|_{[0,T]}}}\left[\exp(\pm c(g-E_{{{X}|_{[0,T]}}}[g]))\right]+\frac{1}{c}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\tilde{X}|_{[0,T]}}\|P_{{X}|_{[0,T]}})\right\}\,,\notag
\end{align}
where the bound holds regardless of the definition of $E_{{\tilde{X}|_{[0,T]}}}[g]$ in the $\infty-\infty$ case. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem bound of arXiv:2608.25889, 'Slope Inequalities for the Geography Problem of Spin Symplectic 4-Manifolds'] Let $s\geq 0$ be an even integer.  If\/ $n$ is a positive integer satisfying 
\begin{equation}
s\leq \frac{1}{8} \sigma(W_n),
\end{equation} 
then we have  
\begin{equation}
\Lambda_s \leq - 10s - 1 
+ \frac{1}{4}c_1^2(W_n).
\end{equation}

[Theorem thm-Pfister of arXiv:2603.17861, 'Gaussian concentration, integral probability metrics, and coupling functionals\\ for infin'] Let $\mu\in\mathscr{M}_\tau^1(\Omega)$ be an asymptotically decoupled measure, and let
$C>0$. Then the following statements are equivalent:
\begin{align}

\bar{d}(\mu,\nu)  \leq \sqrt{\scaleto{2C}{7pt}
\scaleto{s}{6pt}(\nu|\mu)}\,,\qquad \forall \,\nu\in\mathscr{M}_\tau^1(\Omega),
\end{align}
and the thermodynamic Gaussian concentration bound (equation ping of the paper).
In other words, if one of these inequalities holds for some constant $C$,
then so does the other, with the same constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma EHI:l:expressionsForG>0 of arXiv:2511.08956, '\textbf{Towards a characterization of elliptic Harnack inequality for jump processes}'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be an isotropic unimodal L\'{e}vy jump process on $\mathbb{R}^d$, and let the functions $G_D^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle, k}(\cdot, \cdot)$ be as defined in Definition (EHI:d:GkDef of the paper). Then for all $x, y \in D$,
    \begin{equation} 
        G^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle, >0}_D(x, y) = \mathbb{E}_x \left[ \indicatorWithSetBrackets{T^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle}<\tau_D} G_D(X_{T^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle}}, y) \right] = \int_{B(0, r)} G_D(z, y) \mathbb{E}_x \left[ \int_0^{T^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle} \wedge \tau_D} \hat{j}^{\left\langle r_0 \right\rangle}(|X_t-z|) \; \mathrm{d} t \right] \; \mathrm{d} z.
    \end{equation}

