[Lemma l:GeneratorWellDefined of arXiv:2411.14936, 'Massive Particle Systems,\\Wasserstein Brownian Motions,\\ and the Dean--Kawasaki Equation'] The operator~$\boldsymbol\mssL$ is well-defined on~$\Cyl{}{}$ and
\begin{equation}
\boldsymbol\mssL u = \Sigma_{a\in A} (\mssL_a f_a)({\,\cdot\,}_a)\, \Pi_{\substack{i\in A\\ i\neq a}} f_i({\,\cdot\,}_i) \,\mathrm{,}\;\, \qquad u=\Pi_{a\in A} f_a({\,\cdot\,}_a) \,\mathrm{.}
\end{equation}

\begin{proof}
Since~$\mssH_{k,\bullet}$ is conservative by Assumption~(ass:SettingK of the paper), we have~$\mssL_k \car_k\equiv 0$ for every~$k$.
It follows that the series in~(equation eq:t:BendikovSaloffCoste:00 of the paper) reduces to the finite sum in~(equation eq:t:BendikovSaloffCoste:000 of the paper).
\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

