[Lemma lemma4.3 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] Let $K>0$ with the property that (equation 1.6 of the paper) holds.  Then  the function $u$ obtained in Lemma (lemma4.2 of the paper) exhibits the convergence
\begin{align}
    u(\cdot,t)\rightarrow u_{\infty}\qquad in\;(W^{1,\infty}(\Omega))^*\qquad as\; t\to \infty
\end{align}
with some $u_{\infty}\in(W^{1,\infty}(\Omega))^*$ which satisfies
\begin{align}
    \|u_{\infty}-u_0\|_{(W^{1,\infty}(\Omega))^*}\leq C(K)\cdot \left\{\int_\Omega v_{0}\right\}^{\sigma}
\end{align}
with $C(K)>0$  as given in Lemma (lemma4.1 of the paper).

