body:
[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2609.00757, 'Improved bounds in Birch's theorem for forms in many variables'] Let \(I\) be a translate of a box of side length \(H_1\) contained in \(|\h|\ll H_1B^\eps\), let \(\alpha\in\RR\), and let \(q\leq B^2\) be a positive integer.
Then \((I\cap\ZZ^n)\setminus\{\boldsymbol 0\}\) can be partitioned into \(O_{d,n,\eps}(B^\eps)\) sets \(E\) with the following property.
For each part \(E\), we can choose an integer \(\zeta\geq\sigma\) and shifts \(\h_i(\h_1)\) as above so that
\[
 \dim\operatorname{Sing}_{\QQ}(G_{\h_1}^{[3]})\leq\zeta,
 \qquad \text{for } \h_1\in E.
\]
Moreover, for every prime \(p\mid3b_q\), the dimension of \(\operatorname{Sing}_{\mathbb F_p}(G_{\h_1}^{[3]})\) is independent of \(\h_1\in E\).
Hence \(R_\zeta(G_{\h_1},q)\) is also independent of \(\h_1\in E\) and we denote its common value by \(R_\zeta\).

With these choices, we have
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{\h_1\in E}
 \frac{|S_{\h_1}(\alpha;B)|}{B^n}
 \ll B^\eps H_1^n
 \left(
 Q^{\sigma-\zeta}R_\zeta^{-1/2}
 \max_{\h_1\in E}
 \frac{|T_{\h_1}(\alpha;B)|}{B^n}
 \right)^{1/2^{r-1}}.
\end{equation}
The implied constant depends only on \(F,\omega\) and \(\eps\).

[Corollary cor:approximate_duality of arXiv:2509.10984, 'Weak Existence and Uniqueness for Super-Brownian Motion with Irregular Drift'] Let $(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a solution to (equation eq:SPDE1 of the paper) with $X_0 \sim \eta \in \mathcal{P}_p(\mathcal{C}^+_{tem})$, $p>2$,  and let $a$ be defined as in (equation eq:def_d of the paper). Let $Y^n$ be as above, independent of $X$.
	Then there exists $T_0 >0$ , depending only on $a$ and $\langle \mu,1\rangle$, such that for each $X_0 \sim \eta \in \mathcal{P}_p(\mathcal{C}^+_{tem})$ satisfying (equation eq:cond_x_0 of the paper), we get
	\begin{equation*}
		\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty}\mathbb{E}[(-1)^{J^n_T}\exp\Big(-\langle Y_T^n, X_{0}\rangle-a \int_0^T\langle Y_s^n, 1 \rangle ds\Big)\Big] = \mathbb{E}[\exp(-\langle Y_0,X_T\rangle)],
	\end{equation*}
for all $T \leq T_0$.

