[Lemma 19 (Stability of the Mild Solution) of arXiv:2607.03318, 'Continuous Differentiability of the Value Function for Infinite-Dimensional Finite-Horizon'] Let Assumptions \ref{ass:coefficients} and \ref{ass:problem_data} hold. For a fixed penalization parameter $\varepsilon > 0$, let $u_{\varepsilon, 1}$ and $u_{\varepsilon, 2}$ be the respective mild solutions of \eqref{eq:hjb_penalized} driven by the problem data triplets $(f_1, \Phi_1, \Psi_1)$ and $(f_2, \Phi_2, \Psi_2)$. Then there exists a constant $C_T > 0$ such that:
\begin{equation*}
    \|u_{\varepsilon, 1}(t, \cdot) - u_{\varepsilon, 2}(t, \cdot)\|_{\mathcal{B}_m} \le C_T \left( \|\Psi_1 - \Psi_2\|_{\mathcal{B}_m} + \|f_1 - f_2\|_{\mathcal{B}_{m, T}} + \frac{1}{\varepsilon} \|\Phi_1 - \Phi_2\|_{\mathcal{B}_{m, T}} \right).
\end{equation*}

