[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2608.29554, 'Limiting Behavior of a Class of Hermitian Yang--Mills Metrics, II: Exponential Approximati'] There exist constants $c>0$ and $\epsilon_0>0$, independent of
$\epsilon$, such that for any $0<\epsilon\leq\epsilon_0$,
\begin{equation}
\|\Tr H_\epsilon\|_{L^\infty}
\leq
\left(1+e^{-c/\epsilon}\right)
\|\Tr H_\epsilon\|_{L^1(dV)}.

\end{equation}

[Lemma Lemma 2-KMTrate of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] \ \\ 
1. There exists a constant $c >0$ such that, for any $n\geqslant 1$, $a \in (0,1]$ and $x \geqslant a\sigma \sqrt{n}$, 
\begin{align}
\left| \frac{\mathbb{P} \left( \tau_x > n \right)}{H\left(\frac{x}{\sigma\sqrt{n}}\right) } - 1 \right|  
\leqslant \frac{c}{a} n^{-\frac{\delta}{2(3+\delta)}}. 
\end{align}
2. Moreover, if $\delta \geqslant 1$, then there exists a constant $c >0$ such that, for any $n\geqslant 1$, $a \in (0,1]$ and $x \geqslant a\sigma \sqrt{n}$, 
\begin{align}
\left| \frac{\mathbb{P} \left( \tau_x > n \right)}{H\left(\frac{x}{\sigma\sqrt{n}}\right) } - 1 \right|  
\leqslant \frac{c}{a\sqrt{n}} .
\end{align}

