[Lemma lemma3.4 of arXiv:2412.05709, 'Incipient infinite clusters and volume growth for Gaussian free fields and loop soups on m'] For any $d\ge 3$ with $d\neq 6$, there exists $C>0$ such that for any $u\ge C$, $n\ge 1$, $m\ge un^{1\boxdot \frac{d-4}{2}}$, $h\in [0,m^{-d^{5}}]$, and any $\diamond\in \{\mathbf{N},\mathbf{x},\mathbf{T}\}$ with $\diamond \ge m^{d^5}$, 
