[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2609.03403, 'Hyperpositive functions, sector bounded functions and a trace formula'] In the above notation, $B=0$ and $d\mu$ is absolutely continuous with respect to Lebesgue measure and
  \begin{equation}
    \frac{d\mu(x)}{dx}=\begin{cases}{\rm Re}\, F(x)+\frac{tT}{2},\quad a.e.,\quad t\ge 0,\\
                      {\rm Re}\   F(x),\quad\hspace{0.9cm} a.e.,\quad t\le 0.
                         \end{cases}
      \end{equation}

