[Lemma lem:relative-entropy:bound of arXiv:2605.16904, 'Positive-rate PCA and IPS with stationary Bernoulli measures are rapidly forgetful \footno'] Let $\lambda=\lambda_q$  be a Bernoulli measure with strictly positive marginal $q\colon\Sigma\to(0,1)$.
	Let $X$ and $Z$ be random configurations from $\Sigma^{\mathbb{Z}^d}$, and suppose that $Z\sim\lambda$.
	Then, 
	\begin{equation}
		D\big((X_A\given X_B) \relto[\big] Z_A\big) \leq
			\abs{A}\log(\sfrac{1}{q_\mathsf{min}}) \;.
	\end{equation}
	for every two disjoint finite sets $A,B\Subset\mathbb{Z}^d$,
	where $q_\mathsf{min}\coloneqq\min\{q(a): a\in\Sigma\}$.

