body:
[Theorem 2 (Explicit first obstruction) of arXiv:2607.17630, 'Higher-Order Hankel Obstructions to Free Infinite Divisibility\ for Beta Distributions'] Let $p,q>0$, put $s=p+q$, and set
\begin{equation}
 \Psi(p,q)=2s^3(s+1)+pq\bigl(s^3-7s^2-16s-12\bigr).
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 D_1(\beta_{p,q})=
 \frac{p^2q^2\Psi(p,q)}
 {s^6(s+1)^3(s+2)^2(s+3)}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, $\Psi(p,q)<0$ implies that $\beta_{p,q}$ is not FID.

