[Lemma lem:26 of arXiv:2504.12293, 'Near-existence of bigeodesics in dynamical exponential last passage percolation'] There exists a constant $c>0$ such that for all $p_1\leq q_1, p_2\leq q_2$, we have
  \begin{equation}

    \mathrm{Cov}(T_{p_1}^{q_1},T_{p_2}^{q_2})\geq c\int_0^\infty (\mathbb{E}|\Gamma_{p_1}^{q_1,0}\cap \Gamma_{p_2}^{q_2,t}|) e^{-t}dt.
  \end{equation}

