[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2606.21433, 'Central limit theorem for\\ the averaged Adam optimizer'] Let $\theta\in\R^d$ so that $X(U,\theta)$ is integrable.
The martingale correction $\Psi_\theta$ is well-defined by equation \cref{eq:34663}
and the following statements hold for all $ \bx\in\ell^d_\varrho $:
\bas{
|\Psi_{\theta}(\bx)|\le (1-\sqrt{\beta})^{-1}\bigl(\|\bx\|_{\ell_{\varrho}^{d}}+\|\varrho\|_{\ell_{1}} \,\E[|X(\theta,U)|]\bigr)
}
and
\bas{
\E\bigl[ g(\bX^{\bx,\theta}(1))+\Psi_{\theta}(\bX^{\bx,\theta}(1))-\Psi_{\theta}(\bx) \bigr] =f(\theta) ,
}
where we use the notation introduced in \cref{def:mart_cor}.

