[Proposition prop:cherUmin of arXiv:2411.11345, 'Real Gaussian exponential sums via a real moment map'] For all $x\in \mathbb{R}^m$, $x\in U_-$ if and only if 
  \begin{equation}
    g^x(\mu(x)-a_0)<m+\sum_{k=1}^{m-1} \binom{m+1}{k+1} e^{-2k\Phi_0(x)}+e^{-2m\Phi_0(x)}.
  \end{equation}
  Similarly $x\in U_+$ if and only if the reverse inequality holds.

