[Lemma lem:L_b of arXiv:2505.09604, 'Exceptional force, uncountably many solutions in the KPZ fixed point'] Assume that $b$ satisfies (equation eq:global_appx of the paper). Then, for $s < t$ and $x,y \in \mathbb{R}$,
\begin{equation} 
\mathcal{L}(x,s;y,t) \le b(y,t) - b(x,s),
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation} 
\text{Equality occurs if and only if } x \text{ maximizes } z \mapsto b(z,s) +\mathcal{L}(z,s;y,t) \text{ over } z \in \mathbb{R}.
\end{equation}

[Thm expl_asymptotics of arXiv:2411.00629, '\Large Transformation of Stochastic Recursions and Critical Phenomena in the Analysis of t'] Let $\alpha>1$.  Then as $t\to\infty$, 

\begin{equation}
 \mathbb P (L\ge t)\sim e^{-t} \ \text{and}\  \mathbb P (S\ge t)\sim e^{-t}
\end{equation}

so that ${\mathbb{E}}(S)\le {\mathbb{E}}(L)<\infty$, where $f(t)\sim e^{-t}$ means $f(t)/e^{-t}\in[1/c,c]$ for 
all $t>t_0$ for some $c,t_0>0$.
 In particular, ${\mathbb{E}}(S)\le {\mathbb{E}}(L)<\infty$.

