[Prop cos-TVS of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1)$. For $a_c=a_c(\alpha)=\lambda/\alpha$, let $\mathds A_{-a_c, a_c}$ be the critical two-valued set in a valid domain $D$. For any continuous, bounded  function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$,
\begin{align}
    \lim_{n\to \infty}(:\! \cos( \alpha \phi ) \!: , f\1_{[\mathds A_{-a_c, a_c}]_n}) = \mathbb E\left[ (:\! \cos( \alpha \phi ) \!: , f) \mid \mathcal F_{\mathds A_{-a_c, a_c}} \right ], 
\end{align}
where the limit is in probability. In particular, the left-hand side converges to $(\mu, f)$ where $\mu\equiv\mu(a_c)\equiv\mu(\alpha)$ is a random measure which is measurable with respect to $\mathds A_{-a_c, a_c}$.

