[Lemma lem:escape of arXiv:2608.10184, 'The sharp SAT/UNSAT phase transition in random ellipsoid fitting'] Let $A$ be an $s \times M$ matrix with independent $\mathcal{N}(0,1)$ entries and let $T$ be a nonempty compact subset of the unit sphere of $\mathbb{R}^M$.  Then for every $t > 0$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\left\{
\inf_{x \in T} \|A x\|_2 \;\le\; \mathbb{E}\|g_s\|_2 - w(T) - t
\right\}
\le e^{-t^2/2} ,
\qquad g_s \sim \mathcal{N}(0, I_s).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

