[Proposition prop:distance_across_rectangle of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] {kkmt2026cle4_part2}}]
	For each $r > 0$, write
	\begin{equation*}
		V_r \defeq \left\{z \in \BC : 0 < \Re(z) < r, \ 0 < \Im(z) < 1\right\};
	\end{equation*}
	write $T_r$ (resp.\ $B_r$) for the top (resp.\ bottom) side of $V_r$; let $\Gamma_{V_r}$ be a non-nested $\CLE_4$ in $V_r$. (By convention, $V_r$ is of conformal modulus $1/r$.) Then there is a deterministic constant $c \in (0, 1)$ such that 
	\begin{equation*}
		\BP\!\left\lbrack D_{\Gamma_{V_r}}^{V_r}(T_r, B_r) \le 1/r\right\rbrack \ge c
	\end{equation*}
	for all sufficiently large $r > 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:edge_universality of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] For  $\alpha > 1$, set 
\begin{equation}
     \tilde{p}_n(x, y)=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{k\in \mathbb{Z}}f\Big(\frac{x-y+kN}{W}\Big), \quad M:=\sum_{k\in \mathbb{Z}} f\Big(\frac{k}{W}\Big),
\end{equation}
where the density profile $f$ satisfies the comparison conditions in Definition~(ass:ft of the paper) with respect to the $\alpha$-stable density $f_{\alpha}$. 
Under the same assumptions on the Markov chains $([N], P_N)$ and $([N], \widetilde{P}_N)$ as in Theorem~(prop:super_4 of the paper), the scaling limits of the correlation measures established in Theorem~(thm:convergence_proof of the paper) ($\alpha$-stable case) also hold for the matrix $X$. In particular, a new tricritical point process emerges at the critical bandwidth and critical external source, as described in Theorem~(thm:triple_critical_convergence of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

