[Lemma claim_estimate_remainder_terms of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] For any admissible sequence of operations ${\mathcal{O}}_1,\ldots,{\mathcal{O}}_T$, there exists a constant $C>0$ that does not depend on $\varepsilon$ such that
        \begin{equation}\nonumber
            \begin{aligned}
            \mathbb{E}{\mathcal R}_{{\mathcal{O}}_T\circ\cdots\circ{\mathcal{O}}_1\left({\mathcal T_0}\right)}\prec  N^{C\varepsilon}N^{-5/3}k^{2/3}\left\lVert A \right\rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}^2, 
            \end{aligned}
        \end{equation}
        where ${\mathcal R}_{{\mathcal{O}}_T\circ\cdots\circ{\mathcal{O}}_1\left({\mathcal T_0}\right)}$ is defined as in (equation reminder_terms_expansion of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 23 (Sign-barrier) of arXiv:2604.22567, 'Sign-balance of random Laplace eigenfunctions'] There exists a constant $\eps = \varepsilon_{1}>0$, and constants $C>0$, $T_{0}>0$ sufficiently large, only depending on $\Mcc$, with the following property. Let $T>T_{0}$, $\eta\in [1,T]$, $r>0$ satisfy either (a) $\frac{C}{T}<r<\frac{1}{C} \cdot \frac{1}{T^{\frac{d}{d+1}}}$ and $\eta> C(rT)^{d-1}$, or (b) $\Mcc=\Sc^{d}$, and $\frac{C}{T}<r < \frac{1}{C\sqrt{T}}$. Then, for every $x\in\Mcc$, there exists an element $h=h_{x,r}\in\Hc$ of the RKHS of norm
\begin{equation}

\|h\|^2_{\Hc} < C\cdot \max\{ 1,r^2 T \cdot\eta  \}\cdot (rT)^{2(d-1)},
\end{equation}
satisfying
\begin{equation}

\widetilde{\Dc}_{h;\eps}(x;r) > \varepsilon.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

