[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] (Simplified Proposition 3.3 from \cite{Bitter}). There exists a positive constant $C$ such that for every time-grid $\mathbb{T}_h = \{t_i\}_{i=1}^N$ and every $x, y \in \mathbb{R}^d$, the following holds:
\begin{equation*}
\mathcal{Q}_S\left( \frac{x - \theta_{t_i,t_j}(y)}{\sqrt{t_j - t_i}} \right) \le C \cdot \mathcal{Q}_S\left( \frac{x - \theta^\epsilon_{t_i,t_j}(y)}{\sqrt{t_j - t_i}} \right).
\end{equation*}

