A(\nu):=Dq_{\cQ}^{(r)}(\theta_0)h.
\end{equation*}
This is well defined because two representatives differ by an element of $\Ker(Dq_{\cQ}^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_T)$, which lies in $\Ker(Dq_{\cQ}^{(r)}(\theta_0)|_T)$ by assumption.
